	(94, '65e35de41116a7a22e54b319', '2025-05-14 10:01:12', 'Ingredients for 3 medium crusts:\r\n\r\n3 cups almond flour\r\n\r\n1 1/2 cups arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\r\n\r\n2 1/4 teaspoons baking powder\r\n\r\n2 1/4 teaspoons salt\r\n\r\n2 1/4 teaspoon oregano\r\n\r\n3/8 teaspoon black pepper\r\n\r\n4 eggs\r\n\r\n3/4 cups milk\r\n\r\nDirections:\r\n\r\nPreheat the oven to 425 degrees.\r\nLine a round pizza pan or cookie sheet with parchment paper. (I have 4 pizza pans so I can bake all three at once)\r\nCombine the dry ingredients in a large bowl. Whisk to blend together.\r\nAdd eggs and milk to the dry ingredients. Mix well. The batter will be runny—not like typical pizza dough.\r\nUse a spatula to spread the batter evenly onto the pan in a circle shape.\r\nBake the crust in the preheated oven for 8-12 minutes.\r\nRemove crust from oven and top with sauce and desired toppings. Or freeze the crust for later. Once cooled, place parchment paper between the crusts and they will store perfectly in a ziplock gallon freezer bag until ready to use. I also make sure the size of my circle stays within the range of a gallon bag for this reason.\r\nBake for another 10-15 minutes with toppings.\r\n‌\r\n\r\nOther Option: Ingredients for 1 large crust:\r\n\r\n2 cups almond flour\r\n\r\n1 cup arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\r\n\r\n1 1/2 teaspoon. baking powder\r\n\r\n1 1/2 teaspoon. salt\r\n\r\n1 1/2 teaspoon oregano\r\n\r\n1/4 teaspoon black pepper\r\n\r\n3 eggs\r\n\r\n1/2 cup milk\r\n\r\n‌\r\n\r\nSource: https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/'),
	(95, '65e35de41116a7a22e54b319', '2025-05-14 10:01:12', '**Ingredients for 3 medium crusts:**\n\n3 cups almond flour\n\n1 1/2 cups arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons baking powder\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons salt\n\n2 1/4 teaspoon oregano\n\n3/8 teaspoon black pepper\n\n4 eggs\n\n3/4 cups milk\n\n**Directions:**\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 425 degrees.\n2. Line a round pizza pan or cookie sheet with parchment paper. (I have 4 pizza pans so I can bake all three at once)\n3. Combine the dry ingredients in a large bowl. Whisk to blend together.\n4. Add eggs and milk to the dry ingredients. Mix well. The batter will be runny—not like typical pizza dough.\n5. Use a spatula to spread the batter evenly onto the pan in a circle shape.\n6. Bake the crust in the preheated oven for 8-12 minutes.\n7. Remove crust from oven and top with sauce and desired toppings. Or freeze the crust for later. Once cooled, place parchment paper between the crusts and they will store perfectly in a ziplock gallon freezer bag until ready to use. I also make sure the size of my circle stays within the range of a gallon bag for this reason.\n8. Bake for another 10-15 minutes with toppings.\n\n‌\n\n**Other Option: Ingredients for 1 large crust:**\n\n2 cups almond flour\n\n1 cup arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. baking powder\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. salt\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon oregano\n\n1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n\n3 eggs\n\n1/2 cup milk\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/](https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(96, '65e39452587a1979909f4a74', '2025-04-27 21:29:12', '**Serving: 24** **meatballs**\n\n### Ingredients\n\n- 2 pound ground beef\n- 2 large egg\n- 1 onion, minced or onion powder\n- 2 tablespoons tomato paste (can omit)\n- 4 tablespoons dijon mustard\n- 2 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 teaspoon celtic sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon baking soda\n\n### Instructions\n\n- In a large bowl, combine ground beef, egg, and onion\n- Mix in tomato paste, mustard, coconut flour, salt, pepper, and baking soda\n- Use a ¼ cup scoop to form meatballs (about 57 grams each)\n- Place meatballs on a parchment paper lined baking sheet\n- Bake at 350°F for 20-25 minutes, or until instant read thermometer reads 175°F\n- Serve with marinara sauce over spaghetti squash noodles or zucchini noodles\n\nSource: [https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/](https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(97, '65ea48c89c856f6ad662250b', '2025-04-27 21:24:32', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 1 to 1.5 cups kidney beans, cooked or canned\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoons cumin powder\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- Corn chips to serve this all on top of\n- Optional toppings: tomatoes, cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder \n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add spices.\n3. Add kidney beans.\n4. Serve meat and bean mixter over corn chips. Top with desired toppings.'),
	(98, '65e397521ddf77bca5c237fb', '2024-11-04 18:40:08', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder OR 1/2 tspn Chipotle seasoning (reduce to half tablespoon)\n- 1 pound ground beef or **1 can of jackfruit**\n- 28 ounces diced tomatoes (or 1 jar diced and 1 jar crushed)\n- 2 boxes of kidney beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper (reduce to 3/4 teaspoon)\n- Toppings: avocado, sour cream, grated cheddar cheese\n- Optional: Mix in 1-2 Seasoned Rice packets from Costco\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 15-20 minutes.\n5. Adjust seasoning with salt and pepper as needed.'),
	(99, '65e3a05c8c1b5970dcacc97d', '2024-03-11 17:58:55', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1 can of diced tomatoes\n- 2 boxes of pinto beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper\n- Corn tortillas (16 qty)\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 10 minutes.\n5. Fill tortillas, rolled up and into rectangular dish.\n6. Top with cheese.\n7. Bake at 350 degrees for 20 minutes.'),
	(100, '65e3a1e92948d057fe6ebd6d', '2025-04-27 21:21:14', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef, cooked and drained\n- 1 1/2 cups thinly slice potatoes, cooked and drained\n- 1 can coconut milk (entire can)\n- 1 cup milk (replace with water if we don’t have milk)\n- If needed, 1/2 cup water\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2-4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon sugar\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- If needed for thickening, 1 tablespoon tapioca. Mixed with a small amount of cold water before adding.\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook beef separately.\n2. Cook potatoes separately.\n3. To the cooked beef, add the milk and water and all the seasonings.\n4. If needed, add the tapioca thickener at this stage.\n5. Add the cooked sliced potatoes.'),
	(101, '65e3a89d761eefa02d605b06', '2025-05-10 18:41:34', 'Ingredients\n\n- Cubed chicken, cooked separately\n- Pasta, cooked separately\n- Broccoli florets, cooked separately\n- Cream sauce, cooked separately\n  - 1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n  - 1 teaspoon salt\n  - 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n  - 1/2 teaspoon sugar\n  - 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n  - 1 can of coconut milk-ONLY the thick part, drain the water\n  - 3-4 teaspoons of tapioca powder added to a very little splash of milk or cold water\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook the chicken, pasta and broccoli all separately.\n2. Mix the cream sauce ingredients together and bring to a slow boil.\n3. Combine all the ingredients together.'),
	(102, '65e3abc0f8cd991e2ff05bff', '2024-05-03 19:05:41', 'Ingredients:\n\n2 pounds ground beef\n4 teaspoons paprika\n3 teaspoons black pepper\n2 1/2 teaspoons salt\n2 2/3 teaspoon Maple Sugar or Sucanat Sugar\n1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper\n\nOptional: Lettuce, mayo, cheese, rotel\n\nDirections:\n\n1. Mix all spices together.\n2. Mix spices by hand tenderly into the meat so it doesn’t get too tough.\n3. Form 12 patties, flat like tortillas but also loosely packed so doesn’t dry out. (about 80 grams per patty)\n4. Preheat the pan on mid heat. Browning both sides of the patties but not cooking all the way through. Those become leftovers to freeze and cooked thoroughly as reheated for future meals.\n5. Thoroughly cook the remaining two patties for dinner that night.\n6. Make your burger with whatever toppings you prefer.'),
	(103, '65e3af887349307288afe8a6', '2025-04-27 21:20:59', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 6 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 3/4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 1 pound ground beef or turkey or jackfruit\n\n\nMashed potato ingredients:\n- 3 pounds potatoes, rinsed and cubed\n- 4 tablespoons butter\n- 1 cup milk\n- 1 1/2 cup grated Pecorino Romano cheese\n- 3/4 tablespoon sea salt\n- ground back pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat.\n2. Stir in the salt, pepper and thyme.\n3. Add the veggies and heat until cooked properly.\n4. In another pot, brown the ground meat.\n5. In a third pot, make the mashed potatoes. Add in the butter, milk cheese and salt and pepper after drained and mashed.\n6. Layer all the ingredients into a large dish. Veggies and meat stirred together. Mashed potatoes layered on top.'),
	(104, '67fc058a3968a44cf95a9b8c', '2025-04-27 21:21:31', 'Makes 6 burritos. Can prep insides ahead of time.\n\n- 2 sweet potatoes, peeled and cubed small (about 3-4 cups)\n- 1 red pepper, diced small\n- Coconut oil\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon chili powder\n- ½ teaspoon salt\n- ¼ teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 (15-ounce) can black beans, rinsed and drained\n- 1 cup shredded cheddar cheese\n- 12 tortillas as will likely need to double them up\n\nInstructions\n\n- Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. In a large bowl, toss together the sweet potatoes and red pepper with the oil, cumin, onion powder, chili powder, salt and pepper. Dump the coated veggies onto a large rimmed baking sheet and roast for 18-20 minutes, tossing halfway through. The vegetables should be tender but not mushy at the end of cooking time.\n- Let the vegetable mixture cool. Scrape the mixture into a large bowl and toss with the black beans. Taste the mixture and add additional salt and pepper to taste, if needed. Refrigerate the mixture until ready to assemble the burritos or use immediately.\n- Place 4 tortillas on a microwave-safe plate and cover with a damp paper towel. Microwave for 15-20 seconds until the tortillas are pliable. (Warm up 1/2 cupish of the mixture if premade) Place 1/4 cup or so of the mixture in the center of the tortilla and top with a sprinkle with shredded cheese. Fold in the sides of the tortilla and roll up. Place seam-side down on a baking sheet. Repeat with the remaining tortillas until you have all the burritos you need .\n- Bake in a 375 degree F oven for about 10-15 minutes, until heated through and the top of the tortilla is golden brown. Adjust the baking time as needed depending on if the filling has been refrigerated or not. For a softer tortilla, wrap each burrito in tin foil and heat through. Serve immediately.'),
	(105, '65ece37b52d21abd85f26e02', '2025-05-14 09:36:39', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 2 pound cubbed beef\n- 1/4 cup coconut flour\n- 2 teaspoon paprika\n- 4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 1 teaspoon oregano\n- 1 teaspoon basil\n- 1 teaspoon rosemary\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/4 teaspoon crushed red pepper\n- 1 head cauliflower, chopped\n- 4 large carrots, peeled and chopped\n- 2 bell peppers, chopped\n- 1 onion, chopped\n- 3 stalks of celery, chopped\n- 2 potatoes, chopped\n- 4 cups stock, chicken or beef\n- 1 jar whole tomatoes\n- 1 tablespoon arrowroot powder for thickening, if needed\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat oil in large pot over medium high heat.\n2. Combine coconut flour and spices in a large ziploc bag. And meat to the bag and shake until nicely coated.\n3. Add the seasoned meat to the skillet and brown for 3 minutes. Meat will continue to cook in sauce so browning meat is all you need to do.\n4. Add all vegetables and stir to combine.\n5. Cover and let veggies cook for a few minutes.\n6. Add stock and tomatoes. Stir and bring to a low boil.\n7. Lower heat and let simmer for 10-20. minutes.\n8. Add arrowroot powder to a small amount of cold water. Stir and then add to the stew, stirring to help thicken.'),
	(106, '65ece67dcbf220432b12ece8', '2024-03-09 17:02:16', 'Ingredients\n\n- 3 tablespoons butter\n- 1 large onion, chopped\n- 1 large red bell pepper, chopped\n- 2 medium poblano peppers, seeded and chopped\n- 1 jalapeno pepper, seeded and chopped\n- 2 cloves garlic, chopped\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 tablespoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 3/4 cups chicken stock\n- 1 1/2 cups crushed tomatoes\n- 4 ounces diced green chilies\n- 1 1/2 cup sour cream\n- 5 cups cooked, shredded chicken (substitute is jack fruit and white beans)\n- 4 cups cheddar cheese, grated\n- 16 corn tortillas\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees. Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and all peppers. Cook for about 8-10 minutes, until softened. Sitr in the garlic, chili powder, cumin, salt and cook for 1 minute.\n2. Sprinkle the coconut flour over the vegetable mixture and cook for 1 minute while stirring continuously. Stir in the stock and bring to a simmer for 4 minutes. Remove from the heat and stir in the tomatoes, chilies and sour cream.\n3. Place the chicken in a large bowl. Pour the vegetable mixture over the top and stir until combined.\n4. Place 8 tortillas on the bottom of a 13x9 dish. Top with half of the chicken mixture and then half of the cheese. Repeat with the remaining ingredients. Bake for 45-50 minutes until cheese is bubbly and the edges of the casserole are just turning golden brown.\n\n‌\n\nSource: Deliciouslyorganic.net'),
	(107, '65ecec7b734766a86f3ebd36', '2024-03-09 17:19:13', 'For the sauce:\n\n- 3 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 1/2 teaspoons coconut flour\n- 2 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon dried oregano\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 cups chicken stock\n- 12 ounces tomato paste\n- 1 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n\n#### For the Filling:\n\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 1 large yellow onion, chopped\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1/2 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n- 1 can of Pinto beans\n\n#### For the Wraps:\n\n- 1 recipe savory crepes, page 277 of [The Grain-Free Family Table ](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/the-grain-free-family-table/ "‌")or Siete grain-free tortillas (or corn tortillas)\n- 8 ounces raw cheddar, shredded\n\n### INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Place the coconut oil and coconut flour in a medium sauce pan over medium heat. Whisk constantly and cook until the coconut flour just turns golden brown, about 2 minutes. Add the chili powder, oregano and cumin and cook, stirring frequently until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Whisk in chicken stock, tomato paste and sea salt. Bring to a simmer over medium-low heat and cook until sauce begins to thicken, about 20 minutes.\n2. Place the coconut oil in a large sauté pan over medium heat. Swirl the pan to coat. Add the onion and cook, stirring frequently, until onion is translucent, about 5 minutes. Make a well in the center of the pan and add the cumin. Cook, stirring constantly until the cumin is fragrant, about 30 seconds. Stir cumin into the onions. Add the ground beef and salt. Cook, breaking up the beef with the back of a wooden spoon until beef is no longer pink.\n3. Preheat oven to 400ºF and adjust the rack to the middle position. Pour half the sauce in the bottom of an 11 x 7-inch baking dish and spread it out evenly. Place a crepe on the counter and top with 1/4 cup of the beef filling. Carefully roll the crepe around the beef and place it in the baking dish. Repeat with the remaining beef and crepes. Pour the remaining sauce on top of the enchiladas and sprinkle with the cheese. Bake for 25 minutes, or until golden brown and bubbly on top. Cool for 10 minutes. Serve.\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target "smartCard-inline")'),
	(108, '65ecf156ac509dcad1fe0753', '2024-03-09 17:35:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 4-lb whole chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil, melted\n- dash of salt\n- dash black pepper\n- 1/2 cup chicken broth\n\nInstructions\n\n1. Rinse the chicken and pat it dry. Place in baking pan. Drizzle with oil. Sprinkle on salt and pepper.\n2. Add the stock.\n3. Turn oven to 275 degrees and roast the chicken, covered, for about 3 hours.\n4. Increase to 375 degrees roasting for 30-45 minutes/\n5. Remove from the over allowing to rest 5-10 minutes before carving and serving.'),
	(109, '65ee0b619b77b54774c54f49', '2025-04-30 19:10:48', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 8 ounces baby spinach leaves (fresh or frozen)\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- Black pepper to taste\n- 1 package of mushrooms, sliced (optional)\n- 1/4 cup chopped walnuts, toasted (optional) [toast on a pan over medium heat for 4-5 minutes until golden brown]\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. Heat oil over medium heat in a large pot. Remove the seeds from the squash, scoop the flesh out and place in the pot. Add spinach leaves, cream and goat cheese. Toss well until goat cheese has melted and the mixture is hot.\n3. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with walnuts, if using.'),
	(110, '66b7c63aef984308441f4e1c', '2025-04-28 17:29:26', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 cans of salmon makes 14 patties\n- 3 eggs\n- about 2.5 cups of almond flour\n- Coconut oil for pan\n\nDirections\n\n1. Add salmon and eggs to a bowl and mix.\n2. Make 14 patties at 70 grams each\n3. Something here with the flour\n4. ‌\n5. Stove at 4.5'),
	(111, '67f6e86693b75b1c157d8e81', '2025-05-27 17:22:58', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel or 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 20–25 min. Add more liquid if needed. Serve as-is or over rice. Top with cheddar if desired.'),
	(112, '65ee10511a7846ac72bd44c3', '2024-03-10 15:10:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 spaghetti squash\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 6-8oz turkey bacon, sliced or chopped\n- 1 cup onion, diced\n- 1/2 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- Shredded cheddar cheese\n- Optional garnishes: shredded lettuce, tomato, nutritional yeast, black olives\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees. Slice squash lengthwise. Remove the seeds and guts and lay cut side down in a dish with water to cover sides up 1 inch. Roast for 43 minutes if put in right when preheat starts not after; until the squash is tender and pulls away intro strands easily.\n2. While the squash cooks, heat a large skillet on medium high.\n3. Cut 6-8 oz of sliced bacon in to cubes. Dice the onions. Mix together dry spices in a small dish.\n4. Melt the coconut oil in the preheated skillet. Add the bacon. Cook for 3-5 minutes.\n5. Add onions and saute with the bacon for 2-3 minutes or until the onions have softened slightly.\n6. Noe the ground beef gets added to the bacon and onion. Mix it well, sprinkle in the spices. Cook until ground beef is done.\n7. Harvest the squash and combine it with the meats. Stir all together.\n8. Top with cheese. Bake for 15 minutes and 375 degrees.\n9. Remove from oven and top with any optional ingredients.'),
	(113, '65ee228db885a5033c35e542', '2024-03-10 17:02:20', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 3/4 cup onion, diced\n- 1-2 marina sauce jars\n- coconut oil\n- 1 medium spaghetti squash\n- 2 medium zucchini\n- 8 oz grated cheddar cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon nutmeg\n- salt and pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees to cook squash for 43 minutes putting it in at start of preheat. To prep squash, cut lengthwise and remove string and seeds. Place face down in baking dish with water 1-inch up to the sides.\n2. Brown the ground beef and onions.\n3. Slice zucchini lengthwise into 1/8 inch slices.\n4. Once the spaghetti squash is cooked, shred the inside of the squash with a fork into a strainer. Gently press down on the squash to drain out some of the liquid.\n5. Mix the spaghetti squash with 2/3 of the grated cheese, nutmeg, salt and pepper. Set aside.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, build your lasagne. Zucchini slices on the bottom, spread half of the spaghetti squash mixture, spread half the meat mixture, finish with half of the tomato sauce. Repeat. Finish by adding the remaining zucchini slices (if you have any). Add the remaining cheese.\n7. Bake for 25-30 minutes.'),
	(114, '65ee2de69fd5eb92ee41ba40', '2024-03-10 17:15:42', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 28 oz jar spaghetti sauce\n- 3 medium zucchini or 1 eggplant, sliced 1/8 inch thick\n- sea salt\n- Cashew Ricotta Cheese (see that recipe card)\n- 16 oz shredded mozzarella cheese\n- 1/4 cup PR cheese\n- 1 large egg\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a medium skillet, brown meat. Drain. Add the marina sauce to the meat. Simmer on low while prepping the next steps.\n2. Slice the zucchini or eggplant into slices. Lightly salt the slices and set aside for 10 minutes. Salting it helps to take out the moisture. After 10 minutes, blot excess moisture with a paper towel.\n3. On a skillet, grill zucchini on each side until cooked, about 1-2 minutes per side. Place on a paper towel to soak any additional moisture.\n4. Preheat oven to 350 degrees.\n5. In medium bowl, mix the cashew ricotta, pr cheese and egg. Stir well.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, spread some sauce on the bottom. Layer the zucchini. Then ricotta mixture. Top with mozzarella. Repeat the process until all ingredients are used up. Top with sauce and mozzarella.\n7. Cover with foil and bake for 30 minutes.'),
	(115, '65ee2b079d6349ae5cd0a4ae', '2024-03-10 17:41:45', 'Note: For the veggies-can look for a frozen veggie blend to make this easier.\n\nIngredients (these ingredients are all doubled as this freezes well)\n\n- 8 tablespoon butter\n- 4 leeks, roughly chopped\n- 4 carrots, roughly chopped\n- 2 celery stalk, roughly chopped\n- 5 russet potatoes, diced\n- 6 zucchini, cut into 1 inch pieces\n- 8-10 cups chicken stock\n- 2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in the jumbo pot. Add leeks, carrots, celery. Low-medium heat, cover, cook for 20 minutes.\n2. Add potatoes and stock and thyme. Bring to a boil. Simmer for 10 minutes.\n3. Add zucchini. Simmer 15 more minutes. Until zucchini and potatoes are fork tender.\n4. Add salt and pepper.\n5. Using a hand immersion blender, puree the soup. Be careful not to fill the pot too high or this will be very messy.\n6. Season to taste with salt and pepper.'),
	(116, '65ee33402e06e43ef6df6ab4', '2024-03-10 17:40:35', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon butter\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoon dried italian seasoning\n- 6 cups chicken stock\n- 1 pound chicken thighs\n- 14 ounces diced tomatoes\n- 10 ounces frozen spinach leaves\n- Sea salt\n- PR cheese for sprinkling on top\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in a large pot over medium heat. Add garlic and italian seasoning. Pour in stock. Bring to a boil.\n2. Add chicken cooking for 12-15 minutes, until chicken is cooked through. Using a pair of tongs, remove the chicken placing on a cutting board.\n3. Add tomatoes and spinach to the soup and cook for 5-10 minutes.\n4. Chop chicken into bite-sized pieces. Season with sea salt.\n5. Ladle into bowls and garnish with PR cheese.'),
	(117, '65ee372e7bb627c87df43ca2', '2024-03-10 17:46:25', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 3 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 4 cups white beans\n- 4 cups kidney beans\n- 4 cups pinto beans\n- 4 cups chicken broth\n- cheddar cheese\n- salt and pepper to taste\n- Cayenne pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a large pot, add beans and broth and spices. Boil. Simmer, covered, 10 minutes.\n2. Blend with immersion blender.\n3. Serve with cheese on top.'),
	(118, '66804801d104693530f1c13c', '2024-06-29 12:44:39', 'Don\'t put nuggets in until preheat is done \nPlace parchment paper or equivalent in oven\nPreheat 425\nLay 4-6 nuggets in oven \nSet time for 16 minutes\nFlip nuggets over\nSet timer for another 6-7 minutes (check periodically for preferred brownness)\n\nIf you want veggie, we have mixed veggies, green beans, and broccoli. 1/2 to 1 C covered with water. Bring to boil, reduce heat to light boil for 3-4 minutes (broccoli may need an additional min or two)'),
	(119, '67e09ccb91874e7d03e8bac7', '2025-03-23 18:47:00', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1tsp Black pepper\n- 1/4 cup sunflower seeds, toasted (optional)\n- 1 Cup pasta per serving \n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with sunflower seeds, if using.\n3. Each serving can be done with a cup of penne pasta.'),
	(120, '67f6c4722785635c12d6bfef', '2025-04-09 14:03:49', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp chili powder\n- Salt + pepper to taste\n- Corn or flour tortillas\n  **Optional toppings:** diced tomato, avocado, cheese\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Heat a skillet, toss in black beans + spices, stir until warm and a little thickened.\n2. Warm tortillas.\n3. Spoon beans onto tortillas and pile on your toppings.'),
	(121, '67f6d1a82f24c4e9aa7fd634', '2025-04-09 15:00:02', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained)\n- 1 cup rice (white or brown)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes (with juice)\n- 1 bell pepper, chopped\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp cumin + 1/2 tsp smoked paprika (optional: chili powder, garlic)\n- Salt & pepper\n- Optional toppings: cheese, avocado, green onion, hot sauce\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion + pepper in a bit of oil until soft.\n2. Add spices, stir for a minute.\n3. Add rice, beans, tomatoes, and broth.\n4. Bring to a boil, then reduce to low, cover, and simmer until rice is cooked (about 20 min for white, 35-40 for brown).\n5. Fluff and top as you like!'),
	(122, '67f6d1f2c9c94bac53e7a203', '2025-04-09 15:01:07', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 large sweet potato, cubed\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie broth\n- 1 tsp cumin, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, 1/4 tsp cinnamon (optional but amazing)\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion until soft.\n2. Add sweet potato, beans, tomatoes, broth, and spices.\n3. Simmer until sweet potato is fork-tender (20–25 min).\n4. Taste, season, and top with avocado or a swirl of yogurt.'),
	(123, '67f6d2beff0244014051ceb1', '2025-04-09 15:04:22', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup rice\n- 1 can coconut milk (full-fat or light)\n- 1 cup water or broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp ginger powder\n- Salt to taste\n- Optional: lime, cilantro, chili flakes\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Dump it all in a pot.\n2. Bring to boil, then simmer covered 18–20 min until rice is done.\n3. Stir, taste, and finish with lime juice or chili flakes if you want a little kick.'),
	(124, '67f6d7a90dfe222116694fa7', '2025-04-09 15:25:31', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Weeknight protein bomb\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt, pepper\n- Optional: cooked rice or GF pasta to serve over\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add tomato sauce + black beans, simmer 5–10 min. Serve over rice or pasta. Add cheese if you want.'),
	(125, '67f6d7e733d4ebefa32d1be1', '2025-04-09 15:26:19', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Creamy + slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Optional: chili flakes, chopped spinach\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything 15 minutes. Blend half (optional) for a creamier texture. Garnish with a swirl of coconut milk or cheese.'),
	(126, '67f6d814dd2e1cc72fa318bd', '2025-04-09 15:27:11', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk **or** 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic & onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese for top\n\n**How-to:**\nMix cooked pasta, beans, sauce of choice, and seasonings. Pour into dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(127, '67f6d83b8b90154cd16b9174', '2025-04-09 15:27:46', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Meaty vegan stew\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded with hands or fork)\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 tsp each: garlic powder, onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add tomatoes + black beans. Simmer 20–30 min until thick. Great with rice or GF cornbread.'),
	(128, '67f6d86e51c3735b50f5af4e', '2025-04-09 15:28:38', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cheesy & hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Cooked GF pasta or rice\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Mix with beans, sauce, and pasta or rice. Spread in baking dish, top with cheese, bake 15–20 min.'),
	(129, '67f6d3181ecadb49da60fcbf', '2025-04-09 15:26:27', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained)\n- 3 cloves garlic, minced (or 1 tsp garlic powder)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Olive oil\n- Salt, pepper, pinch of chili flakes\n- Optional: handful of chopped kale or spinach, squeeze of lemon\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté garlic in olive oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, broth, herbs, and seasonings.\n3. Simmer 15–20 minutes until thickened and cozy.\n4. Add greens at the end if using, and finish with lemon juice for brightness.'),
	(130, '67f6d365cbfc9cd17164d86a', '2025-04-09 15:26:25', 'Creamy without cream, and full of flavor.\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb pasta (short shapes like orecchiette, penne, or shells)\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 3 cloves garlic (minced or sliced)\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 tsp rosemary or thyme (dried or fresh)\n- 1/2 cup veggie or chicken broth (or pasta water)\n- Salt, pepper, chili flakes to taste\n- Optional: squeeze of lemon, grated Parmesan, or a handful of spinach\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Cook pasta in salted water until al dente. Save about 1/2 cup pasta water.\n2. While pasta cooks, heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat.\n3. Add garlic and herbs. Sauté until garlic is fragrant.\n4. Add cannellini beans and broth (or pasta water). Simmer 5–7 min until beans start to break down a bit and sauce thickens.\n5. Stir in cooked pasta. Toss to coat and warm through.\n6. Add lemon juice or Parmesan if using, and adjust seasoning.'),
	(131, '67f6d89c820310bb4d5b7dfe', '2025-04-09 15:29:30', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Cozy, Italian-inspired\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cooked chopped spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend one can of beans with broth + coconut milk. Simmer with second can and seasonings for 15–20 minutes. Add greens last if using.'),
	(132, '67f6d8d2bf3d8478b9410442', '2025-04-09 15:30:17', '**Type:** Casserole/Bake\n**Vibe:** Dairy-free Alfredo-ish\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: smoked paprika or Italian herbs\n- Optional: shredded cheddar on top\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans, coconut milk, and seasonings. Mix with pasta, pour into baking dish, top with cheese (if using), bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(133, '67f6d8ed0ba832c5d59c9c5b', '2025-04-28 21:45:22', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-rich and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, stir in beans + sauce, simmer 10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(134, '67f6d9453c6e3f0e54ecc6a9', '2025-04-09 15:32:18', '**Type:** One-pot (or two-pot)\n**Vibe:** Rustic & herby\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 can diced tomatoes\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- White rice (served with or cooked into the beans)\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer beans, tomatoes, seasonings together 15 min. Serve over cooked rice or cook rice directly in with extra liquid.'),
	(135, '67f6d9860b7fd3757b014d4a', '2025-04-09 15:33:21', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild & creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp turmeric\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: serve over rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients together for 15–20 min. Serve over rice or scoop with flatbread if you’ve got it.'),
	(136, '67f6d9aa58884dc595fe1691', '2025-04-27 21:29:03', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty & homey\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1–2 chicken breasts (cooked & chopped or shredded)\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Mashed potatoes (can be made with butter + coconut milk)\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, broth, and seasoning in a casserole dish. Top with mashed potatoes. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(137, '67f6db51765d2af8a6120b7d', '2025-04-09 15:41:00', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Rich, soft, almost risotto-like\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 2 cups broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté seasonings in olive oil, add rice and liquid, bring to boil. Add beans halfway through. Simmer covered 18–20 min. Stir at the end—it’ll get creamy!'),
	(138, '67f6db7c34cc1b5aba24924f', '2025-04-09 15:41:37', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Smooth and simple\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Thyme or rosemary\n- Optional: a handful of spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Blend half or all for a smooth texture.'),
	(139, '67f6db98db7791bf47f312e3', '2025-04-09 15:42:03', '**Type:** One-skillet meal\n**Vibe:** Hearty and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Onion powder, garlic powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Stir in beans and tomato sauce. Simmer for 5–10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(140, '67f6dbb11897fad863756c6b', '2025-04-09 15:42:29', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Mild and creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings. Toss with pasta, put in baking dish, top with cheese. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(141, '67f6dbca7dc8d6736fe0c669', '2025-04-09 15:42:55', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Creamy and lightly spiced\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Cumin, turmeric, chili powder (optional)\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning to taste. Serve hot.'),
	(142, '67f6dbf15835da0a7474d6a8', '2025-04-09 15:43:32', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cozy classic with a twist\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (cubed)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme\n- Optional: GF biscuit topping or mashed potatoes\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, sauce in baking dish. Top with biscuits or mash. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 min.'),
	(143, '67f6dc0b38817fdb9a7f5ccc', '2025-04-13 13:28:47', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty & meaty without meat\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/4 cup water\n- 1 tsp salt\n- 1 tsp Garlic\n- 1 tsp onion powder\n- 1tsp paprika\n- 1 tsp oregano\n- Optional: coconut milk splash at the end\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans & tomatoes, simmer 20–30 min. Great on its own or over pasta or rice.'),
	(144, '67f6e574478306dc9e9ca55c', '2025-04-09 16:24:13', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Optional: peas or frozen mixed veggies\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together 20 minutes until creamy. Add frozen veggies near the end. Serve hot over rice.'),
	(145, '67f6e5a37594122dcbc2377e', '2025-04-09 16:25:42', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-packed, saucy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n- Optional: frozen corn or peas\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with seasonings, stir in chickpeas, Ro-Tel, and veggies. Simmer for 10 minutes.'),
	(146, '67f6e6027c1618ec53193a84', '2025-04-09 16:27:00', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Creamy & veggie-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli + carrots (from a veggie mix)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano or thyme\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20–25 minutes. Adjust thickness with more broth or milk. Serve with a spoon and a blanket.'),
	(147, '67f6e6456e211ca1e4aa1d01', '2025-04-09 16:27:53', '**Type:** Creamy pasta\n**Vibe:** White sauce–style, dairy-free\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend chickpeas, coconut milk, and seasonings. Heat in a saucepan, stir in pasta. Top with cheese if desired. Creamy, cozy, and satisfying'),
	(148, '67f6e6733fb047dae933107e', '2025-04-09 16:28:40', '**Type:** Chili-style\n**Vibe:** Simple and spicy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn or mixed veg\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: top with cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20 minutes. Add cheese at the end if using. Serve in a bowl or over rice.'),
	(149, '67f6e6b89008710652e5ceae', '2025-04-09 16:29:49', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty, like a gratin\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 2 cups cooked diced potatoes\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Top with cheese (if using) and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes.'),
	(150, '67f6e6e42de01a2f2a95d602', '2025-04-09 16:30:25', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Warm, earthy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth with seasonings. Add chickpeas and veggies halfway through. Stir occasionally. Done in ~20 min.'),
	(151, '67f6e742e6f1c9d1c849f7d0', '2025-04-09 16:31:57', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Silky, earthy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Blend part of the beans for a creamy texture or leave chunky. Top with cheddar if you like.'),
	(152, '67f6e7823bceb1b3d8bcc968', '2025-04-09 16:33:03', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty and slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with seasonings. Add beans, tomato sauce, and veggies. Simmer until heated through. Serve solo or over rice.'),
	(153, '67f6e7a7c0bdb6909c3d367d', '2025-04-09 16:33:38', '**Type:** Pasta\n**Vibe:** Mild, creamy, and dreamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Optional: grated cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings until smooth. Heat gently, toss with pasta, and top with cheese if using.'),
	(154, '67f6e7c1f4b788ab03a88cf1', '2025-04-09 16:34:04', '**Type:** Oven-bake\n**Vibe:** Roasty and nourishing\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1.5 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 1/4 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary, salt\n- Optional: cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Bake at 375°F for 25–30 minutes until golden. Top with cheese if desired.'),
	(155, '67f6e7dc4583dbdd2be5be67', '2025-04-09 16:34:32', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild curry, plant-powered\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth or Ro-Tel\n- Cumin, garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans, liquid, and simmer 20 min. Serve with rice or as a stew.'),
	(156, '67f6e803175f15f0baeac4bf', '2025-04-09 16:35:02', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Rustic, creamy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- 1/4–1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheese for topping\n\n**How-to:**\nMix everything, transfer to a baking dish, top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes.'),
	(157, '67f6e81c3a17c51bd6839c7f', '2025-04-09 16:35:28', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen peas or green beans\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning and serve with a spoon and a smile.'),
	(158, '67f6e8831688ad96ae92de1b', '2025-06-02 17:33:29', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory & protein-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 3/4 teaspoon Garlic powder\n- 3/4 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/2 teaspoon tumeric\n- 1/4 teaspoon salt\n- Optional: frozen peas or carrots\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add beans and coconut milk, simmer 15–20 minutes. Serve over rice.'),
	(159, '67f6e8a24e9fd13663bf250d', '2025-04-09 16:37:46', '**Type:** Brothy soup\n**Vibe:** Lighter but filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2–1 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 20 minutes. Optional: blend a portion for a thicker texture.'),
	(160, '67f6e8c26dddd811aa4785a0', '2025-04-09 16:38:19', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy & cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nStir all ingredients together in a baking dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(161, '67f6fe57c9b34bebc5416b69', '2025-04-09 18:10:44', '**Type:** Stir-fry\n**Vibe:** Quick and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded jackfruit with spices, add beans and Ro-Tel. Stir-fry until warmed through. Serve over rice'),
	(162, '67f6fade968000a006f6d470', '2025-04-09 17:55:38', '**Type:** One-pot rice dish\n**Vibe:** Quick & flavorful\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen corn or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nCook everything together in a pot. Simmer 15–20 minutes until rice is done and beans are tender.'),
	(163, '67f6fb0e0c712bac84d6e895', '2025-04-09 17:56:26', '**Type:** One-skillet creamy meal\n**Vibe:** Unexpectedly delicious\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme or curry powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté broccoli briefly, then add kidney beans and coconut milk with seasonings. Simmer until everything is tender and creamy.'),
	(164, '67f6fb2d2e2d1f757637bfa8', '2025-04-09 17:56:57', '**Type:** Skillet hash\n**Vibe:** Sweet, savory, and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1–2 cups cubed sweet potatoes (frozen or pre-cooked)\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n- Optional: ground chicken or beef\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté sweet potatoes until browned and soft. Add beans (and meat, if using), season, and cook until warmed through.'),
	(165, '67f6fb610f93ed8503be7f75', '2025-04-09 17:57:50', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Rich, cozy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 lb ground beef (or ground chicken)\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground meat, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes, adding veggies if you like.'),
	(166, '67f6fc015ab7e5dd2c1d4a16', '2025-04-09 18:00:41', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Spicy and robust\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine everything in a pot and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a side of rice or top with cheese.'),
	(167, '67f6fc2720d00eb77da6f821', '2025-04-09 18:01:07', '**Type:** One-pot chili\n**Vibe:** Hearty, plant-based\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with seasonings, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 30 minutes. Serve with rice or cornbread if desired.'),
	(168, '67f6fc43a4ddded4136e8275', '2025-04-09 18:05:30', '**Type:** One-pan rice dish\n**Vibe:** Flavor-packed, filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth, then add beans and veggies halfway through. Simmer until rice is cooked and beans are tender.'),
	(169, '67f6fd48e0026eacba4fd400', '2025-04-09 18:05:55', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Hearty and cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and tomato sauce in a baking dish. Top with cheese and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(170, '67f6fd69a70a93ba954db476', '2025-04-09 18:06:30', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory and satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, then add beans and coconut milk. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(171, '67f6fd876ff8e5425018be54', '2025-04-09 18:06:58', '**Type:** One-pan curry\n**Vibe:** Creamy and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Ground chicken\n- Garlic/onion powder, curry powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground chicken with spices, then add beans and liquids. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve with rice.'),
	(172, '67f6fda74d30ab49c784ad5b', '2025-05-07 17:27:58', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Bold and hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 teaspoon Chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes. Serve over corn mash (aka polenta), or top with cheese if desired.'),
	(173, '67f6fded3a189d2d126507a9', '2025-04-09 18:08:43', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Simple, savory, and smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 chicken breasts, cooked and shredded\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded chicken with seasonings, then add beans and Ro-Tel. Simmer with coconut milk for 15 minutes until everything is warm and combined.'),
	(174, '67f6fe0eeb47261f077fc5bc', '2025-04-09 18:09:15', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Hearty and veggie-packed\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine all ingredients and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a slice of gluten-free bread or over rice if desired.'),
	(175, '67f6fe2faf8069db3ed70ff9', '2025-04-09 18:09:47', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy, cheesy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and Ro-Tel in a baking dish. Top with cheese if desired. Bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(176, '67f6fe8de3ffa0131aebcc34', '2025-04-09 18:11:28', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Simple and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nMix rice, beans, Ro-Tel, and coconut milk. Pour into a baking dish and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until rice is cooked and bubbly.'),
	(177, '67f6feb7dc439bf5eff6cd44', '2025-04-09 18:12:06', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Smoky and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, smoked paprika, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup broth\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground beef with spices, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 20–25 minutes until everything is cooked through.'),
	(178, '68005051861ebf2dfc1c351e', '2025-04-16 19:51:52', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp coconut oil\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel (or canned tomatoes + green chiles)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt to taste\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- Optional: frozen corn or mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Heat oil in skillet, add seasonings and Ro-Tel, cook 2–3 min.\n2. Add beans and frozen veggies (if using), cook until heated.\n3. Stir in cooked rice and simmer 5–10 minutes.'),
	(179, '680050b91ed28e261cc3dbb2', '2025-04-16 19:52:59', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 chicken breast (cubed)\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp paprika\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1–1.5 cups water or broth\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown chicken in oil. Add seasonings.\n2. Stir in tomatoes, beans, water/broth, and veggies.\n3. Simmer covered for 15–20 min.'),
	(180, '680050f9448a7574075a59ea', '2025-04-16 19:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit, drained & shredded\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/4 tsp oregano\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook jackfruit in a pan to brown slightly.\n2. Add seasonings, Ro-Tel, and pinto beans.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min, mash slightly if desired.'),
	(181, '6800511b1f2c891143a064db', '2025-04-16 19:54:00', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 2 cups water or broth\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté seasonings in oil for 1 min.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, veggies, and broth.\n3. Simmer 20–30 minutes until veggies are tender.'),
	(182, '68005183a8bc2730a5655f53', '2025-04-16 19:55:53', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp oregano\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: nutritional yeast or mild cheddar (if tolerated)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Blend or mash beans for smoother texture (optional).\n2. Heat oil and seasonings, then add beans and tomato sauce.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min. Serve over gluten-free pasta.'),
	(183, '680051a5d487414bc769ea25', '2025-04-16 19:56:21', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 tsp curry powder\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1 cup frozen veggies\n- 1 cup cooked rice or serve over it\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook spices in oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, and veggies. Simmer 10–15 min.\n3. Serve over rice or stir in to make a one-pot dish.'),
	(184, '6824bb4a783db57b9ed8e3ca', '2025-05-14 10:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 jar marinara sauce\n- Canned green beans or sweet peas\n- Italian seasoning\n- garlic powder\n- onion powder\n- salt\n- pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook the ground chicken in a pot until browned.\n2. Add marinara sauce and a bit of water to loosen.\n3. Stir in drained beans (all 3 types) and canned green beans or peas.\n4. Season well with Italian herbs and simmer until flavors blend.\n5. Serve hot either as a stew or scoop into warmed almond flour tortillas for wraps.\n6. Divide into three meals.'),
	(185, '6824babde9b3732c346f3c9d', '2025-05-14 10:53:17', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Tortillas chips\n- Chili Powder\n- Cumin\n- Garlic Powder\n- Onion Powder\n- Paprika\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown the ground beef in a skillet, drain excess fat.\n2. Add frozen mixed vegetables and cook until softened.\n3. Stir in drained black beans and season with chili powder, cumin, etc.\n4. Add a little tomato sauce or water to bind the mix.\n5. Layer over tortilla chips or crush chips on top for a crunchy topping.\n6. Portion out into three meals. Optionally serve with salsa or cheese (if available).\n   '),
	(186, '680051ccffdc026a527075ab', '2025-04-16 19:56:58', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can kidney beans (optional combo)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook all ingredients in a pot over medium heat.\n2. Simmer uncovered for 20–30 min to thicken.\n3. Serve as-is or over rice'),
	(187, '6824bbd5acc27f4664c20175', '2025-05-14 10:52:57', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef (or skip for a vegetarian version)\n- 1 can chickpeas or kidney beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Almond flour tortillas\n- Paprika\n- Cumin\n- Garlic powder\n- Salt\n- black pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté the ground beef (if using) until browned.\n2. Drain excess fat.\n3. Add frozen mixed vegetables and sauté until tender.\n4. Stir in drained beans (chickpeas or kidney beans).\n5. Season well with spices using paprika, cumin, garlic powder, and pepper.\n6. Cook until everything is heated through and slightly crispy.\n7. Spoon into almond flour tortillas and wrap. Serve warm or grilled slightly for a toasted wrap.'),
	(188, '65e35de41116a7a22e54b319', '2025-05-14 10:01:12', '**Ingredients for 3 medium crusts:**\n\n3 cups almond flour\n\n1 1/2 cups arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons baking powder\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons salt\n\n2 1/4 teaspoon oregano\n\n3/8 teaspoon black pepper\n\n4 eggs\n\n3/4 cups milk\n\n**Directions:**\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 425 degrees.\n2. Line a round pizza pan or cookie sheet with parchment paper. (I have 4 pizza pans so I can bake all three at once)\n3. Combine the dry ingredients in a large bowl. Whisk to blend together.\n4. Add eggs and milk to the dry ingredients. Mix well. The batter will be runny—not like typical pizza dough.\n5. Use a spatula to spread the batter evenly onto the pan in a circle shape.\n6. Bake the crust in the preheated oven for 8-12 minutes.\n7. Remove crust from oven and top with sauce and desired toppings. Or freeze the crust for later. Once cooled, place parchment paper between the crusts and they will store perfectly in a ziplock gallon freezer bag until ready to use. I also make sure the size of my circle stays within the range of a gallon bag for this reason.\n8. Bake for another 10-15 minutes with toppings.\n\n‌\n\n**Other Option: Ingredients for 1 large crust:**\n\n2 cups almond flour\n\n1 cup arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. baking powder\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. salt\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon oregano\n\n1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n\n3 eggs\n\n1/2 cup milk\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/](https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(189, '65e39452587a1979909f4a74', '2025-04-27 21:29:12', '**Serving: 24** **meatballs**\n\n### Ingredients\n\n- 2 pound ground beef\n- 2 large egg\n- 1 onion, minced or onion powder\n- 2 tablespoons tomato paste (can omit)\n- 4 tablespoons dijon mustard\n- 2 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 teaspoon celtic sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon baking soda\n\n### Instructions\n\n- In a large bowl, combine ground beef, egg, and onion\n- Mix in tomato paste, mustard, coconut flour, salt, pepper, and baking soda\n- Use a ¼ cup scoop to form meatballs (about 57 grams each)\n- Place meatballs on a parchment paper lined baking sheet\n- Bake at 350°F for 20-25 minutes, or until instant read thermometer reads 175°F\n- Serve with marinara sauce over spaghetti squash noodles or zucchini noodles\n\nSource: [https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/](https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(190, '65ea48c89c856f6ad662250b', '2025-04-27 21:24:32', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 1 to 1.5 cups kidney beans, cooked or canned\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoons cumin powder\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- Corn chips to serve this all on top of\n- Optional toppings: tomatoes, cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder \n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add spices.\n3. Add kidney beans.\n4. Serve meat and bean mixter over corn chips. Top with desired toppings.'),
	(191, '65e397521ddf77bca5c237fb', '2024-11-04 18:40:08', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder OR 1/2 tspn Chipotle seasoning (reduce to half tablespoon)\n- 1 pound ground beef or **1 can of jackfruit**\n- 28 ounces diced tomatoes (or 1 jar diced and 1 jar crushed)\n- 2 boxes of kidney beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper (reduce to 3/4 teaspoon)\n- Toppings: avocado, sour cream, grated cheddar cheese\n- Optional: Mix in 1-2 Seasoned Rice packets from Costco\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 15-20 minutes.\n5. Adjust seasoning with salt and pepper as needed.'),
	(192, '65e3a05c8c1b5970dcacc97d', '2024-03-11 17:58:55', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1 can of diced tomatoes\n- 2 boxes of pinto beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper\n- Corn tortillas (16 qty)\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 10 minutes.\n5. Fill tortillas, rolled up and into rectangular dish.\n6. Top with cheese.\n7. Bake at 350 degrees for 20 minutes.'),
	(193, '65e3a1e92948d057fe6ebd6d', '2025-04-27 21:21:14', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef, cooked and drained\n- 1 1/2 cups thinly slice potatoes, cooked and drained\n- 1 can coconut milk (entire can)\n- 1 cup milk (replace with water if we don’t have milk)\n- If needed, 1/2 cup water\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2-4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon sugar\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- If needed for thickening, 1 tablespoon tapioca. Mixed with a small amount of cold water before adding.\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook beef separately.\n2. Cook potatoes separately.\n3. To the cooked beef, add the milk and water and all the seasonings.\n4. If needed, add the tapioca thickener at this stage.\n5. Add the cooked sliced potatoes.'),
	(194, '65e3a89d761eefa02d605b06', '2025-05-10 18:41:34', 'Ingredients\n\n- Cubed chicken, cooked separately\n- Pasta, cooked separately\n- Broccoli florets, cooked separately\n- Cream sauce, cooked separately\n  - 1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n  - 1 teaspoon salt\n  - 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n  - 1/2 teaspoon sugar\n  - 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n  - 1 can of coconut milk-ONLY the thick part, drain the water\n  - 3-4 teaspoons of tapioca powder added to a very little splash of milk or cold water\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook the chicken, pasta and broccoli all separately.\n2. Mix the cream sauce ingredients together and bring to a slow boil.\n3. Combine all the ingredients together.'),
	(195, '65e3abc0f8cd991e2ff05bff', '2024-05-03 19:05:41', 'Ingredients:\n\n2 pounds ground beef\n4 teaspoons paprika\n3 teaspoons black pepper\n2 1/2 teaspoons salt\n2 2/3 teaspoon Maple Sugar or Sucanat Sugar\n1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper\n\nOptional: Lettuce, mayo, cheese, rotel\n\nDirections:\n\n1. Mix all spices together.\n2. Mix spices by hand tenderly into the meat so it doesn’t get too tough.\n3. Form 12 patties, flat like tortillas but also loosely packed so doesn’t dry out. (about 80 grams per patty)\n4. Preheat the pan on mid heat. Browning both sides of the patties but not cooking all the way through. Those become leftovers to freeze and cooked thoroughly as reheated for future meals.\n5. Thoroughly cook the remaining two patties for dinner that night.\n6. Make your burger with whatever toppings you prefer.'),
	(196, '65e3af887349307288afe8a6', '2025-04-27 21:20:59', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 6 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 3/4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 1 pound ground beef or turkey or jackfruit\n\n\nMashed potato ingredients:\n- 3 pounds potatoes, rinsed and cubed\n- 4 tablespoons butter\n- 1 cup milk\n- 1 1/2 cup grated Pecorino Romano cheese\n- 3/4 tablespoon sea salt\n- ground back pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat.\n2. Stir in the salt, pepper and thyme.\n3. Add the veggies and heat until cooked properly.\n4. In another pot, brown the ground meat.\n5. In a third pot, make the mashed potatoes. Add in the butter, milk cheese and salt and pepper after drained and mashed.\n6. Layer all the ingredients into a large dish. Veggies and meat stirred together. Mashed potatoes layered on top.'),
	(197, '67fc058a3968a44cf95a9b8c', '2025-04-27 21:21:31', 'Makes 6 burritos. Can prep insides ahead of time.\n\n- 2 sweet potatoes, peeled and cubed small (about 3-4 cups)\n- 1 red pepper, diced small\n- Coconut oil\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon chili powder\n- ½ teaspoon salt\n- ¼ teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 (15-ounce) can black beans, rinsed and drained\n- 1 cup shredded cheddar cheese\n- 12 tortillas as will likely need to double them up\n\nInstructions\n\n- Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. In a large bowl, toss together the sweet potatoes and red pepper with the oil, cumin, onion powder, chili powder, salt and pepper. Dump the coated veggies onto a large rimmed baking sheet and roast for 18-20 minutes, tossing halfway through. The vegetables should be tender but not mushy at the end of cooking time.\n- Let the vegetable mixture cool. Scrape the mixture into a large bowl and toss with the black beans. Taste the mixture and add additional salt and pepper to taste, if needed. Refrigerate the mixture until ready to assemble the burritos or use immediately.\n- Place 4 tortillas on a microwave-safe plate and cover with a damp paper towel. Microwave for 15-20 seconds until the tortillas are pliable. (Warm up 1/2 cupish of the mixture if premade) Place 1/4 cup or so of the mixture in the center of the tortilla and top with a sprinkle with shredded cheese. Fold in the sides of the tortilla and roll up. Place seam-side down on a baking sheet. Repeat with the remaining tortillas until you have all the burritos you need .\n- Bake in a 375 degree F oven for about 10-15 minutes, until heated through and the top of the tortilla is golden brown. Adjust the baking time as needed depending on if the filling has been refrigerated or not. For a softer tortilla, wrap each burrito in tin foil and heat through. Serve immediately.'),
	(198, '65ece37b52d21abd85f26e02', '2025-05-14 09:36:39', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 2 pound cubbed beef\n- 1/4 cup coconut flour\n- 2 teaspoon paprika\n- 4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 1 teaspoon oregano\n- 1 teaspoon basil\n- 1 teaspoon rosemary\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/4 teaspoon crushed red pepper\n- 1 head cauliflower, chopped\n- 4 large carrots, peeled and chopped\n- 2 bell peppers, chopped\n- 1 onion, chopped\n- 3 stalks of celery, chopped\n- 2 potatoes, chopped\n- 4 cups stock, chicken or beef\n- 1 jar whole tomatoes\n- 1 tablespoon arrowroot powder for thickening, if needed\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat oil in large pot over medium high heat.\n2. Combine coconut flour and spices in a large ziploc bag. And meat to the bag and shake until nicely coated.\n3. Add the seasoned meat to the skillet and brown for 3 minutes. Meat will continue to cook in sauce so browning meat is all you need to do.\n4. Add all vegetables and stir to combine.\n5. Cover and let veggies cook for a few minutes.\n6. Add stock and tomatoes. Stir and bring to a low boil.\n7. Lower heat and let simmer for 10-20. minutes.\n8. Add arrowroot powder to a small amount of cold water. Stir and then add to the stew, stirring to help thicken.'),
	(199, '65ece67dcbf220432b12ece8', '2024-03-09 17:02:16', 'Ingredients\n\n- 3 tablespoons butter\n- 1 large onion, chopped\n- 1 large red bell pepper, chopped\n- 2 medium poblano peppers, seeded and chopped\n- 1 jalapeno pepper, seeded and chopped\n- 2 cloves garlic, chopped\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 tablespoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 3/4 cups chicken stock\n- 1 1/2 cups crushed tomatoes\n- 4 ounces diced green chilies\n- 1 1/2 cup sour cream\n- 5 cups cooked, shredded chicken (substitute is jack fruit and white beans)\n- 4 cups cheddar cheese, grated\n- 16 corn tortillas\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees. Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and all peppers. Cook for about 8-10 minutes, until softened. Sitr in the garlic, chili powder, cumin, salt and cook for 1 minute.\n2. Sprinkle the coconut flour over the vegetable mixture and cook for 1 minute while stirring continuously. Stir in the stock and bring to a simmer for 4 minutes. Remove from the heat and stir in the tomatoes, chilies and sour cream.\n3. Place the chicken in a large bowl. Pour the vegetable mixture over the top and stir until combined.\n4. Place 8 tortillas on the bottom of a 13x9 dish. Top with half of the chicken mixture and then half of the cheese. Repeat with the remaining ingredients. Bake for 45-50 minutes until cheese is bubbly and the edges of the casserole are just turning golden brown.\n\n‌\n\nSource: Deliciouslyorganic.net'),
	(200, '65ecec7b734766a86f3ebd36', '2024-03-09 17:19:13', 'For the sauce:\n\n- 3 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 1/2 teaspoons coconut flour\n- 2 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon dried oregano\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 cups chicken stock\n- 12 ounces tomato paste\n- 1 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n\n#### For the Filling:\n\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 1 large yellow onion, chopped\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1/2 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n- 1 can of Pinto beans\n\n#### For the Wraps:\n\n- 1 recipe savory crepes, page 277 of [The Grain-Free Family Table ](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/the-grain-free-family-table/ "‌")or Siete grain-free tortillas (or corn tortillas)\n- 8 ounces raw cheddar, shredded\n\n### INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Place the coconut oil and coconut flour in a medium sauce pan over medium heat. Whisk constantly and cook until the coconut flour just turns golden brown, about 2 minutes. Add the chili powder, oregano and cumin and cook, stirring frequently until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Whisk in chicken stock, tomato paste and sea salt. Bring to a simmer over medium-low heat and cook until sauce begins to thicken, about 20 minutes.\n2. Place the coconut oil in a large sauté pan over medium heat. Swirl the pan to coat. Add the onion and cook, stirring frequently, until onion is translucent, about 5 minutes. Make a well in the center of the pan and add the cumin. Cook, stirring constantly until the cumin is fragrant, about 30 seconds. Stir cumin into the onions. Add the ground beef and salt. Cook, breaking up the beef with the back of a wooden spoon until beef is no longer pink.\n3. Preheat oven to 400ºF and adjust the rack to the middle position. Pour half the sauce in the bottom of an 11 x 7-inch baking dish and spread it out evenly. Place a crepe on the counter and top with 1/4 cup of the beef filling. Carefully roll the crepe around the beef and place it in the baking dish. Repeat with the remaining beef and crepes. Pour the remaining sauce on top of the enchiladas and sprinkle with the cheese. Bake for 25 minutes, or until golden brown and bubbly on top. Cool for 10 minutes. Serve.\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target "smartCard-inline")'),
	(201, '65ecf156ac509dcad1fe0753', '2024-03-09 17:35:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 4-lb whole chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil, melted\n- dash of salt\n- dash black pepper\n- 1/2 cup chicken broth\n\nInstructions\n\n1. Rinse the chicken and pat it dry. Place in baking pan. Drizzle with oil. Sprinkle on salt and pepper.\n2. Add the stock.\n3. Turn oven to 275 degrees and roast the chicken, covered, for about 3 hours.\n4. Increase to 375 degrees roasting for 30-45 minutes/\n5. Remove from the over allowing to rest 5-10 minutes before carving and serving.'),
	(202, '65ee0b619b77b54774c54f49', '2025-04-30 19:10:48', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 8 ounces baby spinach leaves (fresh or frozen)\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- Black pepper to taste\n- 1 package of mushrooms, sliced (optional)\n- 1/4 cup chopped walnuts, toasted (optional) [toast on a pan over medium heat for 4-5 minutes until golden brown]\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. Heat oil over medium heat in a large pot. Remove the seeds from the squash, scoop the flesh out and place in the pot. Add spinach leaves, cream and goat cheese. Toss well until goat cheese has melted and the mixture is hot.\n3. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with walnuts, if using.'),
	(203, '66b7c63aef984308441f4e1c', '2025-04-28 17:29:26', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 cans of salmon makes 14 patties\n- 3 eggs\n- about 2.5 cups of almond flour\n- Coconut oil for pan\n\nDirections\n\n1. Add salmon and eggs to a bowl and mix.\n2. Make 14 patties at 70 grams each\n3. Something here with the flour\n4. ‌\n5. Stove at 4.5'),
	(204, '67f6e86693b75b1c157d8e81', '2025-05-27 17:22:58', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel or 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 20–25 min. Add more liquid if needed. Serve as-is or over rice. Top with cheddar if desired.'),
	(205, '65ee10511a7846ac72bd44c3', '2024-03-10 15:10:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 spaghetti squash\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 6-8oz turkey bacon, sliced or chopped\n- 1 cup onion, diced\n- 1/2 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- Shredded cheddar cheese\n- Optional garnishes: shredded lettuce, tomato, nutritional yeast, black olives\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees. Slice squash lengthwise. Remove the seeds and guts and lay cut side down in a dish with water to cover sides up 1 inch. Roast for 43 minutes if put in right when preheat starts not after; until the squash is tender and pulls away intro strands easily.\n2. While the squash cooks, heat a large skillet on medium high.\n3. Cut 6-8 oz of sliced bacon in to cubes. Dice the onions. Mix together dry spices in a small dish.\n4. Melt the coconut oil in the preheated skillet. Add the bacon. Cook for 3-5 minutes.\n5. Add onions and saute with the bacon for 2-3 minutes or until the onions have softened slightly.\n6. Noe the ground beef gets added to the bacon and onion. Mix it well, sprinkle in the spices. Cook until ground beef is done.\n7. Harvest the squash and combine it with the meats. Stir all together.\n8. Top with cheese. Bake for 15 minutes and 375 degrees.\n9. Remove from oven and top with any optional ingredients.'),
	(206, '65ee228db885a5033c35e542', '2024-03-10 17:02:20', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 3/4 cup onion, diced\n- 1-2 marina sauce jars\n- coconut oil\n- 1 medium spaghetti squash\n- 2 medium zucchini\n- 8 oz grated cheddar cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon nutmeg\n- salt and pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees to cook squash for 43 minutes putting it in at start of preheat. To prep squash, cut lengthwise and remove string and seeds. Place face down in baking dish with water 1-inch up to the sides.\n2. Brown the ground beef and onions.\n3. Slice zucchini lengthwise into 1/8 inch slices.\n4. Once the spaghetti squash is cooked, shred the inside of the squash with a fork into a strainer. Gently press down on the squash to drain out some of the liquid.\n5. Mix the spaghetti squash with 2/3 of the grated cheese, nutmeg, salt and pepper. Set aside.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, build your lasagne. Zucchini slices on the bottom, spread half of the spaghetti squash mixture, spread half the meat mixture, finish with half of the tomato sauce. Repeat. Finish by adding the remaining zucchini slices (if you have any). Add the remaining cheese.\n7. Bake for 25-30 minutes.'),
	(207, '65ee2de69fd5eb92ee41ba40', '2024-03-10 17:15:42', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 28 oz jar spaghetti sauce\n- 3 medium zucchini or 1 eggplant, sliced 1/8 inch thick\n- sea salt\n- Cashew Ricotta Cheese (see that recipe card)\n- 16 oz shredded mozzarella cheese\n- 1/4 cup PR cheese\n- 1 large egg\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a medium skillet, brown meat. Drain. Add the marina sauce to the meat. Simmer on low while prepping the next steps.\n2. Slice the zucchini or eggplant into slices. Lightly salt the slices and set aside for 10 minutes. Salting it helps to take out the moisture. After 10 minutes, blot excess moisture with a paper towel.\n3. On a skillet, grill zucchini on each side until cooked, about 1-2 minutes per side. Place on a paper towel to soak any additional moisture.\n4. Preheat oven to 350 degrees.\n5. In medium bowl, mix the cashew ricotta, pr cheese and egg. Stir well.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, spread some sauce on the bottom. Layer the zucchini. Then ricotta mixture. Top with mozzarella. Repeat the process until all ingredients are used up. Top with sauce and mozzarella.\n7. Cover with foil and bake for 30 minutes.'),
	(208, '65ee2b079d6349ae5cd0a4ae', '2024-03-10 17:41:45', 'Note: For the veggies-can look for a frozen veggie blend to make this easier.\n\nIngredients (these ingredients are all doubled as this freezes well)\n\n- 8 tablespoon butter\n- 4 leeks, roughly chopped\n- 4 carrots, roughly chopped\n- 2 celery stalk, roughly chopped\n- 5 russet potatoes, diced\n- 6 zucchini, cut into 1 inch pieces\n- 8-10 cups chicken stock\n- 2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in the jumbo pot. Add leeks, carrots, celery. Low-medium heat, cover, cook for 20 minutes.\n2. Add potatoes and stock and thyme. Bring to a boil. Simmer for 10 minutes.\n3. Add zucchini. Simmer 15 more minutes. Until zucchini and potatoes are fork tender.\n4. Add salt and pepper.\n5. Using a hand immersion blender, puree the soup. Be careful not to fill the pot too high or this will be very messy.\n6. Season to taste with salt and pepper.'),
	(209, '65ee33402e06e43ef6df6ab4', '2024-03-10 17:40:35', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon butter\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoon dried italian seasoning\n- 6 cups chicken stock\n- 1 pound chicken thighs\n- 14 ounces diced tomatoes\n- 10 ounces frozen spinach leaves\n- Sea salt\n- PR cheese for sprinkling on top\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in a large pot over medium heat. Add garlic and italian seasoning. Pour in stock. Bring to a boil.\n2. Add chicken cooking for 12-15 minutes, until chicken is cooked through. Using a pair of tongs, remove the chicken placing on a cutting board.\n3. Add tomatoes and spinach to the soup and cook for 5-10 minutes.\n4. Chop chicken into bite-sized pieces. Season with sea salt.\n5. Ladle into bowls and garnish with PR cheese.'),
	(210, '65ee372e7bb627c87df43ca2', '2024-03-10 17:46:25', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 3 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 4 cups white beans\n- 4 cups kidney beans\n- 4 cups pinto beans\n- 4 cups chicken broth\n- cheddar cheese\n- salt and pepper to taste\n- Cayenne pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a large pot, add beans and broth and spices. Boil. Simmer, covered, 10 minutes.\n2. Blend with immersion blender.\n3. Serve with cheese on top.'),
	(211, '66804801d104693530f1c13c', '2024-06-29 12:44:39', 'Don\'t put nuggets in until preheat is done \nPlace parchment paper or equivalent in oven\nPreheat 425\nLay 4-6 nuggets in oven \nSet time for 16 minutes\nFlip nuggets over\nSet timer for another 6-7 minutes (check periodically for preferred brownness)\n\nIf you want veggie, we have mixed veggies, green beans, and broccoli. 1/2 to 1 C covered with water. Bring to boil, reduce heat to light boil for 3-4 minutes (broccoli may need an additional min or two)'),
	(212, '67e09ccb91874e7d03e8bac7', '2025-03-23 18:47:00', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1tsp Black pepper\n- 1/4 cup sunflower seeds, toasted (optional)\n- 1 Cup pasta per serving \n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with sunflower seeds, if using.\n3. Each serving can be done with a cup of penne pasta.'),
	(213, '67f6c4722785635c12d6bfef', '2025-04-09 14:03:49', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp chili powder\n- Salt + pepper to taste\n- Corn or flour tortillas\n  **Optional toppings:** diced tomato, avocado, cheese\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Heat a skillet, toss in black beans + spices, stir until warm and a little thickened.\n2. Warm tortillas.\n3. Spoon beans onto tortillas and pile on your toppings.'),
	(214, '67f6d1a82f24c4e9aa7fd634', '2025-04-09 15:00:02', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained)\n- 1 cup rice (white or brown)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes (with juice)\n- 1 bell pepper, chopped\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp cumin + 1/2 tsp smoked paprika (optional: chili powder, garlic)\n- Salt & pepper\n- Optional toppings: cheese, avocado, green onion, hot sauce\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion + pepper in a bit of oil until soft.\n2. Add spices, stir for a minute.\n3. Add rice, beans, tomatoes, and broth.\n4. Bring to a boil, then reduce to low, cover, and simmer until rice is cooked (about 20 min for white, 35-40 for brown).\n5. Fluff and top as you like!'),
	(215, '67f6d1f2c9c94bac53e7a203', '2025-04-09 15:01:07', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 large sweet potato, cubed\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie broth\n- 1 tsp cumin, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, 1/4 tsp cinnamon (optional but amazing)\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion until soft.\n2. Add sweet potato, beans, tomatoes, broth, and spices.\n3. Simmer until sweet potato is fork-tender (20–25 min).\n4. Taste, season, and top with avocado or a swirl of yogurt.'),
	(216, '67f6d2beff0244014051ceb1', '2025-04-09 15:04:22', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup rice\n- 1 can coconut milk (full-fat or light)\n- 1 cup water or broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp ginger powder\n- Salt to taste\n- Optional: lime, cilantro, chili flakes\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Dump it all in a pot.\n2. Bring to boil, then simmer covered 18–20 min until rice is done.\n3. Stir, taste, and finish with lime juice or chili flakes if you want a little kick.'),
	(217, '67f6d7a90dfe222116694fa7', '2025-04-09 15:25:31', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Weeknight protein bomb\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt, pepper\n- Optional: cooked rice or GF pasta to serve over\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add tomato sauce + black beans, simmer 5–10 min. Serve over rice or pasta. Add cheese if you want.'),
	(218, '67f6d7e733d4ebefa32d1be1', '2025-04-09 15:26:19', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Creamy + slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Optional: chili flakes, chopped spinach\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything 15 minutes. Blend half (optional) for a creamier texture. Garnish with a swirl of coconut milk or cheese.'),
	(219, '67f6d814dd2e1cc72fa318bd', '2025-04-09 15:27:11', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk **or** 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic & onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese for top\n\n**How-to:**\nMix cooked pasta, beans, sauce of choice, and seasonings. Pour into dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(220, '67f6d83b8b90154cd16b9174', '2025-04-09 15:27:46', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Meaty vegan stew\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded with hands or fork)\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 tsp each: garlic powder, onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add tomatoes + black beans. Simmer 20–30 min until thick. Great with rice or GF cornbread.'),
	(221, '67f6d86e51c3735b50f5af4e', '2025-04-09 15:28:38', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cheesy & hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Cooked GF pasta or rice\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Mix with beans, sauce, and pasta or rice. Spread in baking dish, top with cheese, bake 15–20 min.'),
	(222, '67f6d3181ecadb49da60fcbf', '2025-04-09 15:26:27', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained)\n- 3 cloves garlic, minced (or 1 tsp garlic powder)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Olive oil\n- Salt, pepper, pinch of chili flakes\n- Optional: handful of chopped kale or spinach, squeeze of lemon\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté garlic in olive oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, broth, herbs, and seasonings.\n3. Simmer 15–20 minutes until thickened and cozy.\n4. Add greens at the end if using, and finish with lemon juice for brightness.'),
	(223, '67f6d365cbfc9cd17164d86a', '2025-04-09 15:26:25', 'Creamy without cream, and full of flavor.\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb pasta (short shapes like orecchiette, penne, or shells)\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 3 cloves garlic (minced or sliced)\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 tsp rosemary or thyme (dried or fresh)\n- 1/2 cup veggie or chicken broth (or pasta water)\n- Salt, pepper, chili flakes to taste\n- Optional: squeeze of lemon, grated Parmesan, or a handful of spinach\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Cook pasta in salted water until al dente. Save about 1/2 cup pasta water.\n2. While pasta cooks, heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat.\n3. Add garlic and herbs. Sauté until garlic is fragrant.\n4. Add cannellini beans and broth (or pasta water). Simmer 5–7 min until beans start to break down a bit and sauce thickens.\n5. Stir in cooked pasta. Toss to coat and warm through.\n6. Add lemon juice or Parmesan if using, and adjust seasoning.'),
	(224, '67f6d89c820310bb4d5b7dfe', '2025-04-09 15:29:30', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Cozy, Italian-inspired\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cooked chopped spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend one can of beans with broth + coconut milk. Simmer with second can and seasonings for 15–20 minutes. Add greens last if using.'),
	(225, '67f6d8d2bf3d8478b9410442', '2025-04-09 15:30:17', '**Type:** Casserole/Bake\n**Vibe:** Dairy-free Alfredo-ish\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: smoked paprika or Italian herbs\n- Optional: shredded cheddar on top\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans, coconut milk, and seasonings. Mix with pasta, pour into baking dish, top with cheese (if using), bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(226, '67f6d8ed0ba832c5d59c9c5b', '2025-04-28 21:45:22', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-rich and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, stir in beans + sauce, simmer 10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(227, '67f6d9453c6e3f0e54ecc6a9', '2025-04-09 15:32:18', '**Type:** One-pot (or two-pot)\n**Vibe:** Rustic & herby\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 can diced tomatoes\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- White rice (served with or cooked into the beans)\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer beans, tomatoes, seasonings together 15 min. Serve over cooked rice or cook rice directly in with extra liquid.'),
	(228, '67f6d9860b7fd3757b014d4a', '2025-04-09 15:33:21', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild & creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp turmeric\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: serve over rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients together for 15–20 min. Serve over rice or scoop with flatbread if you’ve got it.'),
	(229, '67f6d9aa58884dc595fe1691', '2025-04-27 21:29:03', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty & homey\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1–2 chicken breasts (cooked & chopped or shredded)\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Mashed potatoes (can be made with butter + coconut milk)\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, broth, and seasoning in a casserole dish. Top with mashed potatoes. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(230, '67f6db51765d2af8a6120b7d', '2025-04-09 15:41:00', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Rich, soft, almost risotto-like\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 2 cups broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté seasonings in olive oil, add rice and liquid, bring to boil. Add beans halfway through. Simmer covered 18–20 min. Stir at the end—it’ll get creamy!'),
	(231, '67f6db7c34cc1b5aba24924f', '2025-04-09 15:41:37', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Smooth and simple\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Thyme or rosemary\n- Optional: a handful of spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Blend half or all for a smooth texture.'),
	(232, '67f6db98db7791bf47f312e3', '2025-04-09 15:42:03', '**Type:** One-skillet meal\n**Vibe:** Hearty and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Onion powder, garlic powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Stir in beans and tomato sauce. Simmer for 5–10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(233, '67f6dbb11897fad863756c6b', '2025-04-09 15:42:29', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Mild and creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings. Toss with pasta, put in baking dish, top with cheese. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(234, '67f6dbca7dc8d6736fe0c669', '2025-04-09 15:42:55', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Creamy and lightly spiced\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Cumin, turmeric, chili powder (optional)\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning to taste. Serve hot.'),
	(235, '67f6dbf15835da0a7474d6a8', '2025-04-09 15:43:32', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cozy classic with a twist\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (cubed)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme\n- Optional: GF biscuit topping or mashed potatoes\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, sauce in baking dish. Top with biscuits or mash. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 min.'),
	(236, '67f6dc0b38817fdb9a7f5ccc', '2025-04-13 13:28:47', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty & meaty without meat\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/4 cup water\n- 1 tsp salt\n- 1 tsp Garlic\n- 1 tsp onion powder\n- 1tsp paprika\n- 1 tsp oregano\n- Optional: coconut milk splash at the end\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans & tomatoes, simmer 20–30 min. Great on its own or over pasta or rice.'),
	(237, '67f6e574478306dc9e9ca55c', '2025-04-09 16:24:13', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Optional: peas or frozen mixed veggies\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together 20 minutes until creamy. Add frozen veggies near the end. Serve hot over rice.'),
	(238, '67f6e5a37594122dcbc2377e', '2025-04-09 16:25:42', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-packed, saucy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n- Optional: frozen corn or peas\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with seasonings, stir in chickpeas, Ro-Tel, and veggies. Simmer for 10 minutes.'),
	(239, '67f6e6027c1618ec53193a84', '2025-04-09 16:27:00', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Creamy & veggie-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli + carrots (from a veggie mix)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano or thyme\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20–25 minutes. Adjust thickness with more broth or milk. Serve with a spoon and a blanket.'),
	(240, '67f6e6456e211ca1e4aa1d01', '2025-04-09 16:27:53', '**Type:** Creamy pasta\n**Vibe:** White sauce–style, dairy-free\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend chickpeas, coconut milk, and seasonings. Heat in a saucepan, stir in pasta. Top with cheese if desired. Creamy, cozy, and satisfying'),
	(241, '67f6e6733fb047dae933107e', '2025-04-09 16:28:40', '**Type:** Chili-style\n**Vibe:** Simple and spicy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn or mixed veg\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: top with cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20 minutes. Add cheese at the end if using. Serve in a bowl or over rice.'),
	(242, '67f6e6b89008710652e5ceae', '2025-04-09 16:29:49', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty, like a gratin\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 2 cups cooked diced potatoes\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Top with cheese (if using) and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes.'),
	(243, '67f6e6e42de01a2f2a95d602', '2025-04-09 16:30:25', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Warm, earthy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth with seasonings. Add chickpeas and veggies halfway through. Stir occasionally. Done in ~20 min.'),
	(244, '67f6e742e6f1c9d1c849f7d0', '2025-04-09 16:31:57', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Silky, earthy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Blend part of the beans for a creamy texture or leave chunky. Top with cheddar if you like.'),
	(245, '67f6e7823bceb1b3d8bcc968', '2025-04-09 16:33:03', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty and slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with seasonings. Add beans, tomato sauce, and veggies. Simmer until heated through. Serve solo or over rice.'),
	(246, '67f6e7a7c0bdb6909c3d367d', '2025-04-09 16:33:38', '**Type:** Pasta\n**Vibe:** Mild, creamy, and dreamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Optional: grated cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings until smooth. Heat gently, toss with pasta, and top with cheese if using.'),
	(247, '67f6e7c1f4b788ab03a88cf1', '2025-04-09 16:34:04', '**Type:** Oven-bake\n**Vibe:** Roasty and nourishing\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1.5 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 1/4 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary, salt\n- Optional: cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Bake at 375°F for 25–30 minutes until golden. Top with cheese if desired.'),
	(248, '67f6e7dc4583dbdd2be5be67', '2025-04-09 16:34:32', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild curry, plant-powered\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth or Ro-Tel\n- Cumin, garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans, liquid, and simmer 20 min. Serve with rice or as a stew.'),
	(249, '67f6e803175f15f0baeac4bf', '2025-04-09 16:35:02', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Rustic, creamy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- 1/4–1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheese for topping\n\n**How-to:**\nMix everything, transfer to a baking dish, top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes.'),
	(250, '67f6e81c3a17c51bd6839c7f', '2025-04-09 16:35:28', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen peas or green beans\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning and serve with a spoon and a smile.'),
	(251, '67f6e8831688ad96ae92de1b', '2025-06-02 17:33:29', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory & protein-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 3/4 teaspoon Garlic powder\n- 3/4 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/2 teaspoon tumeric\n- 1/4 teaspoon salt\n- Optional: frozen peas or carrots\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add beans and coconut milk, simmer 15–20 minutes. Serve over rice.'),
	(252, '67f6e8a24e9fd13663bf250d', '2025-04-09 16:37:46', '**Type:** Brothy soup\n**Vibe:** Lighter but filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2–1 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 20 minutes. Optional: blend a portion for a thicker texture.'),
	(253, '67f6e8c26dddd811aa4785a0', '2025-04-09 16:38:19', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy & cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nStir all ingredients together in a baking dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(254, '67f6fe57c9b34bebc5416b69', '2025-04-09 18:10:44', '**Type:** Stir-fry\n**Vibe:** Quick and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded jackfruit with spices, add beans and Ro-Tel. Stir-fry until warmed through. Serve over rice'),
	(255, '67f6fade968000a006f6d470', '2025-04-09 17:55:38', '**Type:** One-pot rice dish\n**Vibe:** Quick & flavorful\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen corn or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nCook everything together in a pot. Simmer 15–20 minutes until rice is done and beans are tender.'),
	(256, '67f6fb0e0c712bac84d6e895', '2025-04-09 17:56:26', '**Type:** One-skillet creamy meal\n**Vibe:** Unexpectedly delicious\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme or curry powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté broccoli briefly, then add kidney beans and coconut milk with seasonings. Simmer until everything is tender and creamy.'),
	(257, '67f6fb2d2e2d1f757637bfa8', '2025-04-09 17:56:57', '**Type:** Skillet hash\n**Vibe:** Sweet, savory, and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1–2 cups cubed sweet potatoes (frozen or pre-cooked)\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n- Optional: ground chicken or beef\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté sweet potatoes until browned and soft. Add beans (and meat, if using), season, and cook until warmed through.'),
	(258, '67f6fb610f93ed8503be7f75', '2025-04-09 17:57:50', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Rich, cozy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 lb ground beef (or ground chicken)\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground meat, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes, adding veggies if you like.'),
	(259, '67f6fc015ab7e5dd2c1d4a16', '2025-04-09 18:00:41', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Spicy and robust\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine everything in a pot and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a side of rice or top with cheese.'),
	(260, '67f6fc2720d00eb77da6f821', '2025-04-09 18:01:07', '**Type:** One-pot chili\n**Vibe:** Hearty, plant-based\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with seasonings, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 30 minutes. Serve with rice or cornbread if desired.'),
	(261, '67f6fc43a4ddded4136e8275', '2025-04-09 18:05:30', '**Type:** One-pan rice dish\n**Vibe:** Flavor-packed, filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth, then add beans and veggies halfway through. Simmer until rice is cooked and beans are tender.'),
	(262, '67f6fd48e0026eacba4fd400', '2025-04-09 18:05:55', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Hearty and cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and tomato sauce in a baking dish. Top with cheese and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(263, '67f6fd69a70a93ba954db476', '2025-04-09 18:06:30', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory and satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, then add beans and coconut milk. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(264, '67f6fd876ff8e5425018be54', '2025-04-09 18:06:58', '**Type:** One-pan curry\n**Vibe:** Creamy and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Ground chicken\n- Garlic/onion powder, curry powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground chicken with spices, then add beans and liquids. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve with rice.'),
	(265, '67f6fda74d30ab49c784ad5b', '2025-05-07 17:27:58', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Bold and hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 teaspoon Chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes. Serve over corn mash (aka polenta), or top with cheese if desired.'),
	(266, '67f6fded3a189d2d126507a9', '2025-04-09 18:08:43', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Simple, savory, and smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 chicken breasts, cooked and shredded\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded chicken with seasonings, then add beans and Ro-Tel. Simmer with coconut milk for 15 minutes until everything is warm and combined.'),
	(267, '67f6fe0eeb47261f077fc5bc', '2025-04-09 18:09:15', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Hearty and veggie-packed\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine all ingredients and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a slice of gluten-free bread or over rice if desired.'),
	(268, '67f6fe2faf8069db3ed70ff9', '2025-04-09 18:09:47', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy, cheesy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and Ro-Tel in a baking dish. Top with cheese if desired. Bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(269, '67f6fe8de3ffa0131aebcc34', '2025-04-09 18:11:28', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Simple and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nMix rice, beans, Ro-Tel, and coconut milk. Pour into a baking dish and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until rice is cooked and bubbly.'),
	(270, '67f6feb7dc439bf5eff6cd44', '2025-04-09 18:12:06', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Smoky and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, smoked paprika, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup broth\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground beef with spices, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 20–25 minutes until everything is cooked through.'),
	(271, '68005051861ebf2dfc1c351e', '2025-04-16 19:51:52', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp coconut oil\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel (or canned tomatoes + green chiles)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt to taste\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- Optional: frozen corn or mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Heat oil in skillet, add seasonings and Ro-Tel, cook 2–3 min.\n2. Add beans and frozen veggies (if using), cook until heated.\n3. Stir in cooked rice and simmer 5–10 minutes.'),
	(272, '680050b91ed28e261cc3dbb2', '2025-04-16 19:52:59', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 chicken breast (cubed)\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp paprika\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1–1.5 cups water or broth\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown chicken in oil. Add seasonings.\n2. Stir in tomatoes, beans, water/broth, and veggies.\n3. Simmer covered for 15–20 min.'),
	(273, '680050f9448a7574075a59ea', '2025-04-16 19:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit, drained & shredded\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/4 tsp oregano\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook jackfruit in a pan to brown slightly.\n2. Add seasonings, Ro-Tel, and pinto beans.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min, mash slightly if desired.'),
	(274, '6800511b1f2c891143a064db', '2025-04-16 19:54:00', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 2 cups water or broth\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté seasonings in oil for 1 min.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, veggies, and broth.\n3. Simmer 20–30 minutes until veggies are tender.'),
	(275, '68005183a8bc2730a5655f53', '2025-04-16 19:55:53', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp oregano\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: nutritional yeast or mild cheddar (if tolerated)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Blend or mash beans for smoother texture (optional).\n2. Heat oil and seasonings, then add beans and tomato sauce.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min. Serve over gluten-free pasta.'),
	(276, '680051a5d487414bc769ea25', '2025-04-16 19:56:21', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 tsp curry powder\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1 cup frozen veggies\n- 1 cup cooked rice or serve over it\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook spices in oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, and veggies. Simmer 10–15 min.\n3. Serve over rice or stir in to make a one-pot dish.'),
	(277, '6824bb4a783db57b9ed8e3ca', '2025-05-14 10:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 jar marinara sauce\n- Canned green beans or sweet peas\n- Italian seasoning\n- garlic powder\n- onion powder\n- salt\n- pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook the ground chicken in a pot until browned.\n2. Add marinara sauce and a bit of water to loosen.\n3. Stir in drained beans (all 3 types) and canned green beans or peas.\n4. Season well with Italian herbs and simmer until flavors blend.\n5. Serve hot either as a stew or scoop into warmed almond flour tortillas for wraps.\n6. Divide into three meals.'),
	(278, '6824babde9b3732c346f3c9d', '2025-05-14 10:53:17', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Tortillas chips\n- Chili Powder\n- Cumin\n- Garlic Powder\n- Onion Powder\n- Paprika\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown the ground beef in a skillet, drain excess fat.\n2. Add frozen mixed vegetables and cook until softened.\n3. Stir in drained black beans and season with chili powder, cumin, etc.\n4. Add a little tomato sauce or water to bind the mix.\n5. Layer over tortilla chips or crush chips on top for a crunchy topping.\n6. Portion out into three meals. Optionally serve with salsa or cheese (if available).\n   '),
	(279, '680051ccffdc026a527075ab', '2025-04-16 19:56:58', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can kidney beans (optional combo)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook all ingredients in a pot over medium heat.\n2. Simmer uncovered for 20–30 min to thicken.\n3. Serve as-is or over rice'),
	(280, '6824bbd5acc27f4664c20175', '2025-05-14 10:52:57', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef (or skip for a vegetarian version)\n- 1 can chickpeas or kidney beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Almond flour tortillas\n- Paprika\n- Cumin\n- Garlic powder\n- Salt\n- black pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté the ground beef (if using) until browned.\n2. Drain excess fat.\n3. Add frozen mixed vegetables and sauté until tender.\n4. Stir in drained beans (chickpeas or kidney beans).\n5. Season well with spices using paprika, cumin, garlic powder, and pepper.\n6. Cook until everything is heated through and slightly crispy.\n7. Spoon into almond flour tortillas and wrap. Serve warm or grilled slightly for a toasted wrap.'),
	(281, '65e35de41116a7a22e54b319', '2025-05-14 10:01:12', '**Ingredients for 3 medium crusts:**\n\n3 cups almond flour\n\n1 1/2 cups arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons baking powder\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons salt\n\n2 1/4 teaspoon oregano\n\n3/8 teaspoon black pepper\n\n4 eggs\n\n3/4 cups milk\n\n**Directions:**\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 425 degrees.\n2. Line a round pizza pan or cookie sheet with parchment paper. (I have 4 pizza pans so I can bake all three at once)\n3. Combine the dry ingredients in a large bowl. Whisk to blend together.\n4. Add eggs and milk to the dry ingredients. Mix well. The batter will be runny—not like typical pizza dough.\n5. Use a spatula to spread the batter evenly onto the pan in a circle shape.\n6. Bake the crust in the preheated oven for 8-12 minutes.\n7. Remove crust from oven and top with sauce and desired toppings. Or freeze the crust for later. Once cooled, place parchment paper between the crusts and they will store perfectly in a ziplock gallon freezer bag until ready to use. I also make sure the size of my circle stays within the range of a gallon bag for this reason.\n8. Bake for another 10-15 minutes with toppings.\n\n‌\n\n**Other Option: Ingredients for 1 large crust:**\n\n2 cups almond flour\n\n1 cup arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. baking powder\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. salt\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon oregano\n\n1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n\n3 eggs\n\n1/2 cup milk\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/](https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(282, '65e39452587a1979909f4a74', '2025-04-27 21:29:12', '**Serving: 24** **meatballs**\n\n### Ingredients\n\n- 2 pound ground beef\n- 2 large egg\n- 1 onion, minced or onion powder\n- 2 tablespoons tomato paste (can omit)\n- 4 tablespoons dijon mustard\n- 2 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 teaspoon celtic sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon baking soda\n\n### Instructions\n\n- In a large bowl, combine ground beef, egg, and onion\n- Mix in tomato paste, mustard, coconut flour, salt, pepper, and baking soda\n- Use a ¼ cup scoop to form meatballs (about 57 grams each)\n- Place meatballs on a parchment paper lined baking sheet\n- Bake at 350°F for 20-25 minutes, or until instant read thermometer reads 175°F\n- Serve with marinara sauce over spaghetti squash noodles or zucchini noodles\n\nSource: [https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/](https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(283, '65ea48c89c856f6ad662250b', '2025-04-27 21:24:32', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 1 to 1.5 cups kidney beans, cooked or canned\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoons cumin powder\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- Corn chips to serve this all on top of\n- Optional toppings: tomatoes, cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder \n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add spices.\n3. Add kidney beans.\n4. Serve meat and bean mixter over corn chips. Top with desired toppings.'),
	(284, '65e397521ddf77bca5c237fb', '2024-11-04 18:40:08', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder OR 1/2 tspn Chipotle seasoning (reduce to half tablespoon)\n- 1 pound ground beef or **1 can of jackfruit**\n- 28 ounces diced tomatoes (or 1 jar diced and 1 jar crushed)\n- 2 boxes of kidney beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper (reduce to 3/4 teaspoon)\n- Toppings: avocado, sour cream, grated cheddar cheese\n- Optional: Mix in 1-2 Seasoned Rice packets from Costco\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 15-20 minutes.\n5. Adjust seasoning with salt and pepper as needed.'),
	(285, '65e3a05c8c1b5970dcacc97d', '2024-03-11 17:58:55', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1 can of diced tomatoes\n- 2 boxes of pinto beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper\n- Corn tortillas (16 qty)\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 10 minutes.\n5. Fill tortillas, rolled up and into rectangular dish.\n6. Top with cheese.\n7. Bake at 350 degrees for 20 minutes.'),
	(286, '65e3a1e92948d057fe6ebd6d', '2025-04-27 21:21:14', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef, cooked and drained\n- 1 1/2 cups thinly slice potatoes, cooked and drained\n- 1 can coconut milk (entire can)\n- 1 cup milk (replace with water if we don’t have milk)\n- If needed, 1/2 cup water\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2-4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon sugar\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- If needed for thickening, 1 tablespoon tapioca. Mixed with a small amount of cold water before adding.\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook beef separately.\n2. Cook potatoes separately.\n3. To the cooked beef, add the milk and water and all the seasonings.\n4. If needed, add the tapioca thickener at this stage.\n5. Add the cooked sliced potatoes.'),
	(287, '65e3a89d761eefa02d605b06', '2025-05-10 18:41:34', 'Ingredients\n\n- Cubed chicken, cooked separately\n- Pasta, cooked separately\n- Broccoli florets, cooked separately\n- Cream sauce, cooked separately\n  - 1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n  - 1 teaspoon salt\n  - 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n  - 1/2 teaspoon sugar\n  - 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n  - 1 can of coconut milk-ONLY the thick part, drain the water\n  - 3-4 teaspoons of tapioca powder added to a very little splash of milk or cold water\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook the chicken, pasta and broccoli all separately.\n2. Mix the cream sauce ingredients together and bring to a slow boil.\n3. Combine all the ingredients together.'),
	(288, '65e3abc0f8cd991e2ff05bff', '2024-05-03 19:05:41', 'Ingredients:\n\n2 pounds ground beef\n4 teaspoons paprika\n3 teaspoons black pepper\n2 1/2 teaspoons salt\n2 2/3 teaspoon Maple Sugar or Sucanat Sugar\n1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper\n\nOptional: Lettuce, mayo, cheese, rotel\n\nDirections:\n\n1. Mix all spices together.\n2. Mix spices by hand tenderly into the meat so it doesn’t get too tough.\n3. Form 12 patties, flat like tortillas but also loosely packed so doesn’t dry out. (about 80 grams per patty)\n4. Preheat the pan on mid heat. Browning both sides of the patties but not cooking all the way through. Those become leftovers to freeze and cooked thoroughly as reheated for future meals.\n5. Thoroughly cook the remaining two patties for dinner that night.\n6. Make your burger with whatever toppings you prefer.'),
	(289, '65e3af887349307288afe8a6', '2025-04-27 21:20:59', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 6 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 3/4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 1 pound ground beef or turkey or jackfruit\n\n\nMashed potato ingredients:\n- 3 pounds potatoes, rinsed and cubed\n- 4 tablespoons butter\n- 1 cup milk\n- 1 1/2 cup grated Pecorino Romano cheese\n- 3/4 tablespoon sea salt\n- ground back pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat.\n2. Stir in the salt, pepper and thyme.\n3. Add the veggies and heat until cooked properly.\n4. In another pot, brown the ground meat.\n5. In a third pot, make the mashed potatoes. Add in the butter, milk cheese and salt and pepper after drained and mashed.\n6. Layer all the ingredients into a large dish. Veggies and meat stirred together. Mashed potatoes layered on top.'),
	(290, '67fc058a3968a44cf95a9b8c', '2025-04-27 21:21:31', 'Makes 6 burritos. Can prep insides ahead of time.\n\n- 2 sweet potatoes, peeled and cubed small (about 3-4 cups)\n- 1 red pepper, diced small\n- Coconut oil\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon chili powder\n- ½ teaspoon salt\n- ¼ teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 (15-ounce) can black beans, rinsed and drained\n- 1 cup shredded cheddar cheese\n- 12 tortillas as will likely need to double them up\n\nInstructions\n\n- Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. In a large bowl, toss together the sweet potatoes and red pepper with the oil, cumin, onion powder, chili powder, salt and pepper. Dump the coated veggies onto a large rimmed baking sheet and roast for 18-20 minutes, tossing halfway through. The vegetables should be tender but not mushy at the end of cooking time.\n- Let the vegetable mixture cool. Scrape the mixture into a large bowl and toss with the black beans. Taste the mixture and add additional salt and pepper to taste, if needed. Refrigerate the mixture until ready to assemble the burritos or use immediately.\n- Place 4 tortillas on a microwave-safe plate and cover with a damp paper towel. Microwave for 15-20 seconds until the tortillas are pliable. (Warm up 1/2 cupish of the mixture if premade) Place 1/4 cup or so of the mixture in the center of the tortilla and top with a sprinkle with shredded cheese. Fold in the sides of the tortilla and roll up. Place seam-side down on a baking sheet. Repeat with the remaining tortillas until you have all the burritos you need .\n- Bake in a 375 degree F oven for about 10-15 minutes, until heated through and the top of the tortilla is golden brown. Adjust the baking time as needed depending on if the filling has been refrigerated or not. For a softer tortilla, wrap each burrito in tin foil and heat through. Serve immediately.'),
	(291, '65ece37b52d21abd85f26e02', '2025-05-14 09:36:39', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 2 pound cubbed beef\n- 1/4 cup coconut flour\n- 2 teaspoon paprika\n- 4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 1 teaspoon oregano\n- 1 teaspoon basil\n- 1 teaspoon rosemary\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/4 teaspoon crushed red pepper\n- 1 head cauliflower, chopped\n- 4 large carrots, peeled and chopped\n- 2 bell peppers, chopped\n- 1 onion, chopped\n- 3 stalks of celery, chopped\n- 2 potatoes, chopped\n- 4 cups stock, chicken or beef\n- 1 jar whole tomatoes\n- 1 tablespoon arrowroot powder for thickening, if needed\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat oil in large pot over medium high heat.\n2. Combine coconut flour and spices in a large ziploc bag. And meat to the bag and shake until nicely coated.\n3. Add the seasoned meat to the skillet and brown for 3 minutes. Meat will continue to cook in sauce so browning meat is all you need to do.\n4. Add all vegetables and stir to combine.\n5. Cover and let veggies cook for a few minutes.\n6. Add stock and tomatoes. Stir and bring to a low boil.\n7. Lower heat and let simmer for 10-20. minutes.\n8. Add arrowroot powder to a small amount of cold water. Stir and then add to the stew, stirring to help thicken.'),
	(292, '65ece67dcbf220432b12ece8', '2024-03-09 17:02:16', 'Ingredients\n\n- 3 tablespoons butter\n- 1 large onion, chopped\n- 1 large red bell pepper, chopped\n- 2 medium poblano peppers, seeded and chopped\n- 1 jalapeno pepper, seeded and chopped\n- 2 cloves garlic, chopped\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 tablespoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 3/4 cups chicken stock\n- 1 1/2 cups crushed tomatoes\n- 4 ounces diced green chilies\n- 1 1/2 cup sour cream\n- 5 cups cooked, shredded chicken (substitute is jack fruit and white beans)\n- 4 cups cheddar cheese, grated\n- 16 corn tortillas\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees. Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and all peppers. Cook for about 8-10 minutes, until softened. Sitr in the garlic, chili powder, cumin, salt and cook for 1 minute.\n2. Sprinkle the coconut flour over the vegetable mixture and cook for 1 minute while stirring continuously. Stir in the stock and bring to a simmer for 4 minutes. Remove from the heat and stir in the tomatoes, chilies and sour cream.\n3. Place the chicken in a large bowl. Pour the vegetable mixture over the top and stir until combined.\n4. Place 8 tortillas on the bottom of a 13x9 dish. Top with half of the chicken mixture and then half of the cheese. Repeat with the remaining ingredients. Bake for 45-50 minutes until cheese is bubbly and the edges of the casserole are just turning golden brown.\n\n‌\n\nSource: Deliciouslyorganic.net'),
	(293, '65ecec7b734766a86f3ebd36', '2024-03-09 17:19:13', 'For the sauce:\n\n- 3 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 1/2 teaspoons coconut flour\n- 2 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon dried oregano\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 cups chicken stock\n- 12 ounces tomato paste\n- 1 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n\n#### For the Filling:\n\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 1 large yellow onion, chopped\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1/2 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n- 1 can of Pinto beans\n\n#### For the Wraps:\n\n- 1 recipe savory crepes, page 277 of [The Grain-Free Family Table ](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/the-grain-free-family-table/ "‌")or Siete grain-free tortillas (or corn tortillas)\n- 8 ounces raw cheddar, shredded\n\n### INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Place the coconut oil and coconut flour in a medium sauce pan over medium heat. Whisk constantly and cook until the coconut flour just turns golden brown, about 2 minutes. Add the chili powder, oregano and cumin and cook, stirring frequently until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Whisk in chicken stock, tomato paste and sea salt. Bring to a simmer over medium-low heat and cook until sauce begins to thicken, about 20 minutes.\n2. Place the coconut oil in a large sauté pan over medium heat. Swirl the pan to coat. Add the onion and cook, stirring frequently, until onion is translucent, about 5 minutes. Make a well in the center of the pan and add the cumin. Cook, stirring constantly until the cumin is fragrant, about 30 seconds. Stir cumin into the onions. Add the ground beef and salt. Cook, breaking up the beef with the back of a wooden spoon until beef is no longer pink.\n3. Preheat oven to 400ºF and adjust the rack to the middle position. Pour half the sauce in the bottom of an 11 x 7-inch baking dish and spread it out evenly. Place a crepe on the counter and top with 1/4 cup of the beef filling. Carefully roll the crepe around the beef and place it in the baking dish. Repeat with the remaining beef and crepes. Pour the remaining sauce on top of the enchiladas and sprinkle with the cheese. Bake for 25 minutes, or until golden brown and bubbly on top. Cool for 10 minutes. Serve.\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target "smartCard-inline")'),
	(294, '65ecf156ac509dcad1fe0753', '2024-03-09 17:35:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 4-lb whole chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil, melted\n- dash of salt\n- dash black pepper\n- 1/2 cup chicken broth\n\nInstructions\n\n1. Rinse the chicken and pat it dry. Place in baking pan. Drizzle with oil. Sprinkle on salt and pepper.\n2. Add the stock.\n3. Turn oven to 275 degrees and roast the chicken, covered, for about 3 hours.\n4. Increase to 375 degrees roasting for 30-45 minutes/\n5. Remove from the over allowing to rest 5-10 minutes before carving and serving.'),
	(295, '65ee0b619b77b54774c54f49', '2025-04-30 19:10:48', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 8 ounces baby spinach leaves (fresh or frozen)\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- Black pepper to taste\n- 1 package of mushrooms, sliced (optional)\n- 1/4 cup chopped walnuts, toasted (optional) [toast on a pan over medium heat for 4-5 minutes until golden brown]\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. Heat oil over medium heat in a large pot. Remove the seeds from the squash, scoop the flesh out and place in the pot. Add spinach leaves, cream and goat cheese. Toss well until goat cheese has melted and the mixture is hot.\n3. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with walnuts, if using.'),
	(296, '66b7c63aef984308441f4e1c', '2025-04-28 17:29:26', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 cans of salmon makes 14 patties\n- 3 eggs\n- about 2.5 cups of almond flour\n- Coconut oil for pan\n\nDirections\n\n1. Add salmon and eggs to a bowl and mix.\n2. Make 14 patties at 70 grams each\n3. Something here with the flour\n4. ‌\n5. Stove at 4.5'),
	(297, '67f6e86693b75b1c157d8e81', '2025-05-27 17:22:58', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel or 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 20–25 min. Add more liquid if needed. Serve as-is or over rice. Top with cheddar if desired.'),
	(298, '65ee10511a7846ac72bd44c3', '2024-03-10 15:10:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 spaghetti squash\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 6-8oz turkey bacon, sliced or chopped\n- 1 cup onion, diced\n- 1/2 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- Shredded cheddar cheese\n- Optional garnishes: shredded lettuce, tomato, nutritional yeast, black olives\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees. Slice squash lengthwise. Remove the seeds and guts and lay cut side down in a dish with water to cover sides up 1 inch. Roast for 43 minutes if put in right when preheat starts not after; until the squash is tender and pulls away intro strands easily.\n2. While the squash cooks, heat a large skillet on medium high.\n3. Cut 6-8 oz of sliced bacon in to cubes. Dice the onions. Mix together dry spices in a small dish.\n4. Melt the coconut oil in the preheated skillet. Add the bacon. Cook for 3-5 minutes.\n5. Add onions and saute with the bacon for 2-3 minutes or until the onions have softened slightly.\n6. Noe the ground beef gets added to the bacon and onion. Mix it well, sprinkle in the spices. Cook until ground beef is done.\n7. Harvest the squash and combine it with the meats. Stir all together.\n8. Top with cheese. Bake for 15 minutes and 375 degrees.\n9. Remove from oven and top with any optional ingredients.'),
	(299, '65ee228db885a5033c35e542', '2024-03-10 17:02:20', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 3/4 cup onion, diced\n- 1-2 marina sauce jars\n- coconut oil\n- 1 medium spaghetti squash\n- 2 medium zucchini\n- 8 oz grated cheddar cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon nutmeg\n- salt and pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees to cook squash for 43 minutes putting it in at start of preheat. To prep squash, cut lengthwise and remove string and seeds. Place face down in baking dish with water 1-inch up to the sides.\n2. Brown the ground beef and onions.\n3. Slice zucchini lengthwise into 1/8 inch slices.\n4. Once the spaghetti squash is cooked, shred the inside of the squash with a fork into a strainer. Gently press down on the squash to drain out some of the liquid.\n5. Mix the spaghetti squash with 2/3 of the grated cheese, nutmeg, salt and pepper. Set aside.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, build your lasagne. Zucchini slices on the bottom, spread half of the spaghetti squash mixture, spread half the meat mixture, finish with half of the tomato sauce. Repeat. Finish by adding the remaining zucchini slices (if you have any). Add the remaining cheese.\n7. Bake for 25-30 minutes.'),
	(300, '65ee2de69fd5eb92ee41ba40', '2024-03-10 17:15:42', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 28 oz jar spaghetti sauce\n- 3 medium zucchini or 1 eggplant, sliced 1/8 inch thick\n- sea salt\n- Cashew Ricotta Cheese (see that recipe card)\n- 16 oz shredded mozzarella cheese\n- 1/4 cup PR cheese\n- 1 large egg\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a medium skillet, brown meat. Drain. Add the marina sauce to the meat. Simmer on low while prepping the next steps.\n2. Slice the zucchini or eggplant into slices. Lightly salt the slices and set aside for 10 minutes. Salting it helps to take out the moisture. After 10 minutes, blot excess moisture with a paper towel.\n3. On a skillet, grill zucchini on each side until cooked, about 1-2 minutes per side. Place on a paper towel to soak any additional moisture.\n4. Preheat oven to 350 degrees.\n5. In medium bowl, mix the cashew ricotta, pr cheese and egg. Stir well.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, spread some sauce on the bottom. Layer the zucchini. Then ricotta mixture. Top with mozzarella. Repeat the process until all ingredients are used up. Top with sauce and mozzarella.\n7. Cover with foil and bake for 30 minutes.'),
	(301, '65ee2b079d6349ae5cd0a4ae', '2024-03-10 17:41:45', 'Note: For the veggies-can look for a frozen veggie blend to make this easier.\n\nIngredients (these ingredients are all doubled as this freezes well)\n\n- 8 tablespoon butter\n- 4 leeks, roughly chopped\n- 4 carrots, roughly chopped\n- 2 celery stalk, roughly chopped\n- 5 russet potatoes, diced\n- 6 zucchini, cut into 1 inch pieces\n- 8-10 cups chicken stock\n- 2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in the jumbo pot. Add leeks, carrots, celery. Low-medium heat, cover, cook for 20 minutes.\n2. Add potatoes and stock and thyme. Bring to a boil. Simmer for 10 minutes.\n3. Add zucchini. Simmer 15 more minutes. Until zucchini and potatoes are fork tender.\n4. Add salt and pepper.\n5. Using a hand immersion blender, puree the soup. Be careful not to fill the pot too high or this will be very messy.\n6. Season to taste with salt and pepper.'),
	(302, '65ee33402e06e43ef6df6ab4', '2024-03-10 17:40:35', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon butter\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoon dried italian seasoning\n- 6 cups chicken stock\n- 1 pound chicken thighs\n- 14 ounces diced tomatoes\n- 10 ounces frozen spinach leaves\n- Sea salt\n- PR cheese for sprinkling on top\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in a large pot over medium heat. Add garlic and italian seasoning. Pour in stock. Bring to a boil.\n2. Add chicken cooking for 12-15 minutes, until chicken is cooked through. Using a pair of tongs, remove the chicken placing on a cutting board.\n3. Add tomatoes and spinach to the soup and cook for 5-10 minutes.\n4. Chop chicken into bite-sized pieces. Season with sea salt.\n5. Ladle into bowls and garnish with PR cheese.'),
	(303, '65ee372e7bb627c87df43ca2', '2024-03-10 17:46:25', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 3 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 4 cups white beans\n- 4 cups kidney beans\n- 4 cups pinto beans\n- 4 cups chicken broth\n- cheddar cheese\n- salt and pepper to taste\n- Cayenne pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a large pot, add beans and broth and spices. Boil. Simmer, covered, 10 minutes.\n2. Blend with immersion blender.\n3. Serve with cheese on top.'),
	(304, '66804801d104693530f1c13c', '2024-06-29 12:44:39', 'Don\'t put nuggets in until preheat is done \nPlace parchment paper or equivalent in oven\nPreheat 425\nLay 4-6 nuggets in oven \nSet time for 16 minutes\nFlip nuggets over\nSet timer for another 6-7 minutes (check periodically for preferred brownness)\n\nIf you want veggie, we have mixed veggies, green beans, and broccoli. 1/2 to 1 C covered with water. Bring to boil, reduce heat to light boil for 3-4 minutes (broccoli may need an additional min or two)'),
	(305, '67e09ccb91874e7d03e8bac7', '2025-03-23 18:47:00', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1tsp Black pepper\n- 1/4 cup sunflower seeds, toasted (optional)\n- 1 Cup pasta per serving \n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with sunflower seeds, if using.\n3. Each serving can be done with a cup of penne pasta.'),
	(306, '67f6c4722785635c12d6bfef', '2025-04-09 14:03:49', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp chili powder\n- Salt + pepper to taste\n- Corn or flour tortillas\n  **Optional toppings:** diced tomato, avocado, cheese\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Heat a skillet, toss in black beans + spices, stir until warm and a little thickened.\n2. Warm tortillas.\n3. Spoon beans onto tortillas and pile on your toppings.'),
	(307, '67f6d1a82f24c4e9aa7fd634', '2025-04-09 15:00:02', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained)\n- 1 cup rice (white or brown)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes (with juice)\n- 1 bell pepper, chopped\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp cumin + 1/2 tsp smoked paprika (optional: chili powder, garlic)\n- Salt & pepper\n- Optional toppings: cheese, avocado, green onion, hot sauce\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion + pepper in a bit of oil until soft.\n2. Add spices, stir for a minute.\n3. Add rice, beans, tomatoes, and broth.\n4. Bring to a boil, then reduce to low, cover, and simmer until rice is cooked (about 20 min for white, 35-40 for brown).\n5. Fluff and top as you like!'),
	(308, '67f6d1f2c9c94bac53e7a203', '2025-04-09 15:01:07', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 large sweet potato, cubed\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie broth\n- 1 tsp cumin, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, 1/4 tsp cinnamon (optional but amazing)\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion until soft.\n2. Add sweet potato, beans, tomatoes, broth, and spices.\n3. Simmer until sweet potato is fork-tender (20–25 min).\n4. Taste, season, and top with avocado or a swirl of yogurt.'),
	(309, '67f6d2beff0244014051ceb1', '2025-04-09 15:04:22', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup rice\n- 1 can coconut milk (full-fat or light)\n- 1 cup water or broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp ginger powder\n- Salt to taste\n- Optional: lime, cilantro, chili flakes\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Dump it all in a pot.\n2. Bring to boil, then simmer covered 18–20 min until rice is done.\n3. Stir, taste, and finish with lime juice or chili flakes if you want a little kick.'),
	(310, '67f6d7a90dfe222116694fa7', '2025-04-09 15:25:31', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Weeknight protein bomb\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt, pepper\n- Optional: cooked rice or GF pasta to serve over\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add tomato sauce + black beans, simmer 5–10 min. Serve over rice or pasta. Add cheese if you want.'),
	(311, '67f6d7e733d4ebefa32d1be1', '2025-04-09 15:26:19', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Creamy + slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Optional: chili flakes, chopped spinach\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything 15 minutes. Blend half (optional) for a creamier texture. Garnish with a swirl of coconut milk or cheese.'),
	(312, '67f6d814dd2e1cc72fa318bd', '2025-04-09 15:27:11', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk **or** 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic & onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese for top\n\n**How-to:**\nMix cooked pasta, beans, sauce of choice, and seasonings. Pour into dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(313, '67f6d83b8b90154cd16b9174', '2025-04-09 15:27:46', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Meaty vegan stew\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded with hands or fork)\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 tsp each: garlic powder, onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add tomatoes + black beans. Simmer 20–30 min until thick. Great with rice or GF cornbread.'),
	(314, '67f6d86e51c3735b50f5af4e', '2025-04-09 15:28:38', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cheesy & hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Cooked GF pasta or rice\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Mix with beans, sauce, and pasta or rice. Spread in baking dish, top with cheese, bake 15–20 min.'),
	(315, '67f6d3181ecadb49da60fcbf', '2025-04-09 15:26:27', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained)\n- 3 cloves garlic, minced (or 1 tsp garlic powder)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Olive oil\n- Salt, pepper, pinch of chili flakes\n- Optional: handful of chopped kale or spinach, squeeze of lemon\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté garlic in olive oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, broth, herbs, and seasonings.\n3. Simmer 15–20 minutes until thickened and cozy.\n4. Add greens at the end if using, and finish with lemon juice for brightness.'),
	(316, '67f6d365cbfc9cd17164d86a', '2025-04-09 15:26:25', 'Creamy without cream, and full of flavor.\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb pasta (short shapes like orecchiette, penne, or shells)\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 3 cloves garlic (minced or sliced)\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 tsp rosemary or thyme (dried or fresh)\n- 1/2 cup veggie or chicken broth (or pasta water)\n- Salt, pepper, chili flakes to taste\n- Optional: squeeze of lemon, grated Parmesan, or a handful of spinach\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Cook pasta in salted water until al dente. Save about 1/2 cup pasta water.\n2. While pasta cooks, heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat.\n3. Add garlic and herbs. Sauté until garlic is fragrant.\n4. Add cannellini beans and broth (or pasta water). Simmer 5–7 min until beans start to break down a bit and sauce thickens.\n5. Stir in cooked pasta. Toss to coat and warm through.\n6. Add lemon juice or Parmesan if using, and adjust seasoning.'),
	(317, '67f6d89c820310bb4d5b7dfe', '2025-04-09 15:29:30', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Cozy, Italian-inspired\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cooked chopped spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend one can of beans with broth + coconut milk. Simmer with second can and seasonings for 15–20 minutes. Add greens last if using.'),
	(318, '67f6d8d2bf3d8478b9410442', '2025-04-09 15:30:17', '**Type:** Casserole/Bake\n**Vibe:** Dairy-free Alfredo-ish\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: smoked paprika or Italian herbs\n- Optional: shredded cheddar on top\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans, coconut milk, and seasonings. Mix with pasta, pour into baking dish, top with cheese (if using), bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(319, '67f6d8ed0ba832c5d59c9c5b', '2025-04-28 21:45:22', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-rich and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, stir in beans + sauce, simmer 10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(320, '67f6d9453c6e3f0e54ecc6a9', '2025-04-09 15:32:18', '**Type:** One-pot (or two-pot)\n**Vibe:** Rustic & herby\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 can diced tomatoes\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- White rice (served with or cooked into the beans)\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer beans, tomatoes, seasonings together 15 min. Serve over cooked rice or cook rice directly in with extra liquid.'),
	(321, '67f6d9860b7fd3757b014d4a', '2025-04-09 15:33:21', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild & creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp turmeric\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: serve over rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients together for 15–20 min. Serve over rice or scoop with flatbread if you’ve got it.'),
	(322, '67f6d9aa58884dc595fe1691', '2025-04-27 21:29:03', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty & homey\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1–2 chicken breasts (cooked & chopped or shredded)\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Mashed potatoes (can be made with butter + coconut milk)\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, broth, and seasoning in a casserole dish. Top with mashed potatoes. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(323, '67f6db51765d2af8a6120b7d', '2025-04-09 15:41:00', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Rich, soft, almost risotto-like\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 2 cups broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté seasonings in olive oil, add rice and liquid, bring to boil. Add beans halfway through. Simmer covered 18–20 min. Stir at the end—it’ll get creamy!'),
	(324, '67f6db7c34cc1b5aba24924f', '2025-04-09 15:41:37', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Smooth and simple\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Thyme or rosemary\n- Optional: a handful of spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Blend half or all for a smooth texture.'),
	(325, '67f6db98db7791bf47f312e3', '2025-04-09 15:42:03', '**Type:** One-skillet meal\n**Vibe:** Hearty and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Onion powder, garlic powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Stir in beans and tomato sauce. Simmer for 5–10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(326, '67f6dbb11897fad863756c6b', '2025-04-09 15:42:29', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Mild and creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings. Toss with pasta, put in baking dish, top with cheese. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(327, '67f6dbca7dc8d6736fe0c669', '2025-04-09 15:42:55', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Creamy and lightly spiced\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Cumin, turmeric, chili powder (optional)\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning to taste. Serve hot.'),
	(328, '67f6dbf15835da0a7474d6a8', '2025-04-09 15:43:32', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cozy classic with a twist\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (cubed)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme\n- Optional: GF biscuit topping or mashed potatoes\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, sauce in baking dish. Top with biscuits or mash. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 min.'),
	(329, '67f6dc0b38817fdb9a7f5ccc', '2025-04-13 13:28:47', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty & meaty without meat\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/4 cup water\n- 1 tsp salt\n- 1 tsp Garlic\n- 1 tsp onion powder\n- 1tsp paprika\n- 1 tsp oregano\n- Optional: coconut milk splash at the end\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans & tomatoes, simmer 20–30 min. Great on its own or over pasta or rice.'),
	(330, '67f6e574478306dc9e9ca55c', '2025-04-09 16:24:13', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Optional: peas or frozen mixed veggies\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together 20 minutes until creamy. Add frozen veggies near the end. Serve hot over rice.'),
	(331, '67f6e5a37594122dcbc2377e', '2025-04-09 16:25:42', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-packed, saucy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n- Optional: frozen corn or peas\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with seasonings, stir in chickpeas, Ro-Tel, and veggies. Simmer for 10 minutes.'),
	(332, '67f6e6027c1618ec53193a84', '2025-04-09 16:27:00', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Creamy & veggie-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli + carrots (from a veggie mix)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano or thyme\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20–25 minutes. Adjust thickness with more broth or milk. Serve with a spoon and a blanket.'),
	(333, '67f6e6456e211ca1e4aa1d01', '2025-04-09 16:27:53', '**Type:** Creamy pasta\n**Vibe:** White sauce–style, dairy-free\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend chickpeas, coconut milk, and seasonings. Heat in a saucepan, stir in pasta. Top with cheese if desired. Creamy, cozy, and satisfying'),
	(334, '67f6e6733fb047dae933107e', '2025-04-09 16:28:40', '**Type:** Chili-style\n**Vibe:** Simple and spicy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn or mixed veg\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: top with cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20 minutes. Add cheese at the end if using. Serve in a bowl or over rice.'),
	(335, '67f6e6b89008710652e5ceae', '2025-04-09 16:29:49', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty, like a gratin\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 2 cups cooked diced potatoes\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Top with cheese (if using) and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes.'),
	(336, '67f6e6e42de01a2f2a95d602', '2025-04-09 16:30:25', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Warm, earthy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth with seasonings. Add chickpeas and veggies halfway through. Stir occasionally. Done in ~20 min.'),
	(337, '67f6e742e6f1c9d1c849f7d0', '2025-04-09 16:31:57', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Silky, earthy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Blend part of the beans for a creamy texture or leave chunky. Top with cheddar if you like.'),
	(338, '67f6e7823bceb1b3d8bcc968', '2025-04-09 16:33:03', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty and slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with seasonings. Add beans, tomato sauce, and veggies. Simmer until heated through. Serve solo or over rice.'),
	(339, '67f6e7a7c0bdb6909c3d367d', '2025-04-09 16:33:38', '**Type:** Pasta\n**Vibe:** Mild, creamy, and dreamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Optional: grated cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings until smooth. Heat gently, toss with pasta, and top with cheese if using.'),
	(340, '67f6e7c1f4b788ab03a88cf1', '2025-04-09 16:34:04', '**Type:** Oven-bake\n**Vibe:** Roasty and nourishing\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1.5 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 1/4 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary, salt\n- Optional: cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Bake at 375°F for 25–30 minutes until golden. Top with cheese if desired.'),
	(341, '67f6e7dc4583dbdd2be5be67', '2025-04-09 16:34:32', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild curry, plant-powered\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth or Ro-Tel\n- Cumin, garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans, liquid, and simmer 20 min. Serve with rice or as a stew.'),
	(342, '67f6e803175f15f0baeac4bf', '2025-04-09 16:35:02', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Rustic, creamy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- 1/4–1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheese for topping\n\n**How-to:**\nMix everything, transfer to a baking dish, top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes.'),
	(343, '67f6e81c3a17c51bd6839c7f', '2025-04-09 16:35:28', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen peas or green beans\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning and serve with a spoon and a smile.'),
	(344, '67f6e8831688ad96ae92de1b', '2025-06-02 17:33:29', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory & protein-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 3/4 teaspoon Garlic powder\n- 3/4 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/2 teaspoon tumeric\n- 1/4 teaspoon salt\n- Optional: frozen peas or carrots\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add beans and coconut milk, simmer 15–20 minutes. Serve over rice.'),
	(345, '67f6e8a24e9fd13663bf250d', '2025-04-09 16:37:46', '**Type:** Brothy soup\n**Vibe:** Lighter but filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2–1 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 20 minutes. Optional: blend a portion for a thicker texture.'),
	(346, '67f6e8c26dddd811aa4785a0', '2025-04-09 16:38:19', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy & cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nStir all ingredients together in a baking dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(347, '67f6fe57c9b34bebc5416b69', '2025-04-09 18:10:44', '**Type:** Stir-fry\n**Vibe:** Quick and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded jackfruit with spices, add beans and Ro-Tel. Stir-fry until warmed through. Serve over rice'),
	(348, '67f6fade968000a006f6d470', '2025-04-09 17:55:38', '**Type:** One-pot rice dish\n**Vibe:** Quick & flavorful\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen corn or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nCook everything together in a pot. Simmer 15–20 minutes until rice is done and beans are tender.'),
	(349, '67f6fb0e0c712bac84d6e895', '2025-04-09 17:56:26', '**Type:** One-skillet creamy meal\n**Vibe:** Unexpectedly delicious\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme or curry powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté broccoli briefly, then add kidney beans and coconut milk with seasonings. Simmer until everything is tender and creamy.'),
	(350, '67f6fb2d2e2d1f757637bfa8', '2025-04-09 17:56:57', '**Type:** Skillet hash\n**Vibe:** Sweet, savory, and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1–2 cups cubed sweet potatoes (frozen or pre-cooked)\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n- Optional: ground chicken or beef\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté sweet potatoes until browned and soft. Add beans (and meat, if using), season, and cook until warmed through.'),
	(351, '67f6fb610f93ed8503be7f75', '2025-04-09 17:57:50', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Rich, cozy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 lb ground beef (or ground chicken)\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground meat, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes, adding veggies if you like.'),
	(352, '67f6fc015ab7e5dd2c1d4a16', '2025-04-09 18:00:41', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Spicy and robust\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine everything in a pot and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a side of rice or top with cheese.'),
	(353, '67f6fc2720d00eb77da6f821', '2025-04-09 18:01:07', '**Type:** One-pot chili\n**Vibe:** Hearty, plant-based\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with seasonings, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 30 minutes. Serve with rice or cornbread if desired.'),
	(354, '67f6fc43a4ddded4136e8275', '2025-04-09 18:05:30', '**Type:** One-pan rice dish\n**Vibe:** Flavor-packed, filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth, then add beans and veggies halfway through. Simmer until rice is cooked and beans are tender.'),
	(355, '67f6fd48e0026eacba4fd400', '2025-04-09 18:05:55', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Hearty and cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and tomato sauce in a baking dish. Top with cheese and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(356, '67f6fd69a70a93ba954db476', '2025-04-09 18:06:30', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory and satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, then add beans and coconut milk. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(357, '67f6fd876ff8e5425018be54', '2025-04-09 18:06:58', '**Type:** One-pan curry\n**Vibe:** Creamy and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Ground chicken\n- Garlic/onion powder, curry powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground chicken with spices, then add beans and liquids. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve with rice.'),
	(358, '67f6fda74d30ab49c784ad5b', '2025-05-07 17:27:58', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Bold and hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 teaspoon Chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes. Serve over corn mash (aka polenta), or top with cheese if desired.'),
	(359, '67f6fded3a189d2d126507a9', '2025-04-09 18:08:43', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Simple, savory, and smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 chicken breasts, cooked and shredded\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded chicken with seasonings, then add beans and Ro-Tel. Simmer with coconut milk for 15 minutes until everything is warm and combined.'),
	(360, '67f6fe0eeb47261f077fc5bc', '2025-04-09 18:09:15', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Hearty and veggie-packed\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine all ingredients and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a slice of gluten-free bread or over rice if desired.'),
	(361, '67f6fe2faf8069db3ed70ff9', '2025-04-09 18:09:47', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy, cheesy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and Ro-Tel in a baking dish. Top with cheese if desired. Bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(362, '67f6fe8de3ffa0131aebcc34', '2025-04-09 18:11:28', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Simple and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nMix rice, beans, Ro-Tel, and coconut milk. Pour into a baking dish and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until rice is cooked and bubbly.'),
	(363, '67f6feb7dc439bf5eff6cd44', '2025-04-09 18:12:06', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Smoky and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, smoked paprika, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup broth\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground beef with spices, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 20–25 minutes until everything is cooked through.'),
	(364, '68005051861ebf2dfc1c351e', '2025-04-16 19:51:52', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp coconut oil\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel (or canned tomatoes + green chiles)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt to taste\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- Optional: frozen corn or mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Heat oil in skillet, add seasonings and Ro-Tel, cook 2–3 min.\n2. Add beans and frozen veggies (if using), cook until heated.\n3. Stir in cooked rice and simmer 5–10 minutes.'),
	(365, '680050b91ed28e261cc3dbb2', '2025-04-16 19:52:59', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 chicken breast (cubed)\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp paprika\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1–1.5 cups water or broth\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown chicken in oil. Add seasonings.\n2. Stir in tomatoes, beans, water/broth, and veggies.\n3. Simmer covered for 15–20 min.'),
	(366, '680050f9448a7574075a59ea', '2025-04-16 19:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit, drained & shredded\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/4 tsp oregano\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook jackfruit in a pan to brown slightly.\n2. Add seasonings, Ro-Tel, and pinto beans.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min, mash slightly if desired.'),
	(367, '6800511b1f2c891143a064db', '2025-04-16 19:54:00', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 2 cups water or broth\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté seasonings in oil for 1 min.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, veggies, and broth.\n3. Simmer 20–30 minutes until veggies are tender.'),
	(368, '68005183a8bc2730a5655f53', '2025-04-16 19:55:53', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp oregano\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: nutritional yeast or mild cheddar (if tolerated)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Blend or mash beans for smoother texture (optional).\n2. Heat oil and seasonings, then add beans and tomato sauce.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min. Serve over gluten-free pasta.'),
	(369, '680051a5d487414bc769ea25', '2025-04-16 19:56:21', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 tsp curry powder\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1 cup frozen veggies\n- 1 cup cooked rice or serve over it\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook spices in oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, and veggies. Simmer 10–15 min.\n3. Serve over rice or stir in to make a one-pot dish.'),
	(370, '6824bb4a783db57b9ed8e3ca', '2025-05-14 10:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 jar marinara sauce\n- Canned green beans or sweet peas\n- Italian seasoning\n- garlic powder\n- onion powder\n- salt\n- pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook the ground chicken in a pot until browned.\n2. Add marinara sauce and a bit of water to loosen.\n3. Stir in drained beans (all 3 types) and canned green beans or peas.\n4. Season well with Italian herbs and simmer until flavors blend.\n5. Serve hot either as a stew or scoop into warmed almond flour tortillas for wraps.\n6. Divide into three meals.'),
	(371, '6824babde9b3732c346f3c9d', '2025-05-14 10:53:17', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Tortillas chips\n- Chili Powder\n- Cumin\n- Garlic Powder\n- Onion Powder\n- Paprika\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown the ground beef in a skillet, drain excess fat.\n2. Add frozen mixed vegetables and cook until softened.\n3. Stir in drained black beans and season with chili powder, cumin, etc.\n4. Add a little tomato sauce or water to bind the mix.\n5. Layer over tortilla chips or crush chips on top for a crunchy topping.\n6. Portion out into three meals. Optionally serve with salsa or cheese (if available).\n   '),
	(372, '680051ccffdc026a527075ab', '2025-04-16 19:56:58', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can kidney beans (optional combo)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook all ingredients in a pot over medium heat.\n2. Simmer uncovered for 20–30 min to thicken.\n3. Serve as-is or over rice'),
	(373, '6824bbd5acc27f4664c20175', '2025-05-14 10:52:57', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef (or skip for a vegetarian version)\n- 1 can chickpeas or kidney beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Almond flour tortillas\n- Paprika\n- Cumin\n- Garlic powder\n- Salt\n- black pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté the ground beef (if using) until browned.\n2. Drain excess fat.\n3. Add frozen mixed vegetables and sauté until tender.\n4. Stir in drained beans (chickpeas or kidney beans).\n5. Season well with spices using paprika, cumin, garlic powder, and pepper.\n6. Cook until everything is heated through and slightly crispy.\n7. Spoon into almond flour tortillas and wrap. Serve warm or grilled slightly for a toasted wrap.'),
	(374, '65e35de41116a7a22e54b319', '2025-05-14 10:01:12', '**Ingredients for 3 medium crusts:**\n\n3 cups almond flour\n\n1 1/2 cups arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons baking powder\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons salt\n\n2 1/4 teaspoon oregano\n\n3/8 teaspoon black pepper\n\n4 eggs\n\n3/4 cups milk\n\n**Directions:**\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 425 degrees.\n2. Line a round pizza pan or cookie sheet with parchment paper. (I have 4 pizza pans so I can bake all three at once)\n3. Combine the dry ingredients in a large bowl. Whisk to blend together.\n4. Add eggs and milk to the dry ingredients. Mix well. The batter will be runny—not like typical pizza dough.\n5. Use a spatula to spread the batter evenly onto the pan in a circle shape.\n6. Bake the crust in the preheated oven for 8-12 minutes.\n7. Remove crust from oven and top with sauce and desired toppings. Or freeze the crust for later. Once cooled, place parchment paper between the crusts and they will store perfectly in a ziplock gallon freezer bag until ready to use. I also make sure the size of my circle stays within the range of a gallon bag for this reason.\n8. Bake for another 10-15 minutes with toppings.\n\n‌\n\n**Other Option: Ingredients for 1 large crust:**\n\n2 cups almond flour\n\n1 cup arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. baking powder\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. salt\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon oregano\n\n1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n\n3 eggs\n\n1/2 cup milk\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/](https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(375, '65e39452587a1979909f4a74', '2025-04-27 21:29:12', '**Serving: 24** **meatballs**\n\n### Ingredients\n\n- 2 pound ground beef\n- 2 large egg\n- 1 onion, minced or onion powder\n- 2 tablespoons tomato paste (can omit)\n- 4 tablespoons dijon mustard\n- 2 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 teaspoon celtic sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon baking soda\n\n### Instructions\n\n- In a large bowl, combine ground beef, egg, and onion\n- Mix in tomato paste, mustard, coconut flour, salt, pepper, and baking soda\n- Use a ¼ cup scoop to form meatballs (about 57 grams each)\n- Place meatballs on a parchment paper lined baking sheet\n- Bake at 350°F for 20-25 minutes, or until instant read thermometer reads 175°F\n- Serve with marinara sauce over spaghetti squash noodles or zucchini noodles\n\nSource: [https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/](https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(376, '65ea48c89c856f6ad662250b', '2025-04-27 21:24:32', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 1 to 1.5 cups kidney beans, cooked or canned\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoons cumin powder\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- Corn chips to serve this all on top of\n- Optional toppings: tomatoes, cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder \n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add spices.\n3. Add kidney beans.\n4. Serve meat and bean mixter over corn chips. Top with desired toppings.'),
	(377, '65e397521ddf77bca5c237fb', '2024-11-04 18:40:08', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder OR 1/2 tspn Chipotle seasoning (reduce to half tablespoon)\n- 1 pound ground beef or **1 can of jackfruit**\n- 28 ounces diced tomatoes (or 1 jar diced and 1 jar crushed)\n- 2 boxes of kidney beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper (reduce to 3/4 teaspoon)\n- Toppings: avocado, sour cream, grated cheddar cheese\n- Optional: Mix in 1-2 Seasoned Rice packets from Costco\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 15-20 minutes.\n5. Adjust seasoning with salt and pepper as needed.'),
	(378, '65e3a05c8c1b5970dcacc97d', '2024-03-11 17:58:55', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1 can of diced tomatoes\n- 2 boxes of pinto beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper\n- Corn tortillas (16 qty)\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 10 minutes.\n5. Fill tortillas, rolled up and into rectangular dish.\n6. Top with cheese.\n7. Bake at 350 degrees for 20 minutes.'),
	(379, '65e3a1e92948d057fe6ebd6d', '2025-04-27 21:21:14', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef, cooked and drained\n- 1 1/2 cups thinly slice potatoes, cooked and drained\n- 1 can coconut milk (entire can)\n- 1 cup milk (replace with water if we don’t have milk)\n- If needed, 1/2 cup water\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2-4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon sugar\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- If needed for thickening, 1 tablespoon tapioca. Mixed with a small amount of cold water before adding.\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook beef separately.\n2. Cook potatoes separately.\n3. To the cooked beef, add the milk and water and all the seasonings.\n4. If needed, add the tapioca thickener at this stage.\n5. Add the cooked sliced potatoes.'),
	(380, '65e3a89d761eefa02d605b06', '2025-05-10 18:41:34', 'Ingredients\n\n- Cubed chicken, cooked separately\n- Pasta, cooked separately\n- Broccoli florets, cooked separately\n- Cream sauce, cooked separately\n  - 1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n  - 1 teaspoon salt\n  - 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n  - 1/2 teaspoon sugar\n  - 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n  - 1 can of coconut milk-ONLY the thick part, drain the water\n  - 3-4 teaspoons of tapioca powder added to a very little splash of milk or cold water\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook the chicken, pasta and broccoli all separately.\n2. Mix the cream sauce ingredients together and bring to a slow boil.\n3. Combine all the ingredients together.'),
	(381, '65e3abc0f8cd991e2ff05bff', '2024-05-03 19:05:41', 'Ingredients:\n\n2 pounds ground beef\n4 teaspoons paprika\n3 teaspoons black pepper\n2 1/2 teaspoons salt\n2 2/3 teaspoon Maple Sugar or Sucanat Sugar\n1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper\n\nOptional: Lettuce, mayo, cheese, rotel\n\nDirections:\n\n1. Mix all spices together.\n2. Mix spices by hand tenderly into the meat so it doesn’t get too tough.\n3. Form 12 patties, flat like tortillas but also loosely packed so doesn’t dry out. (about 80 grams per patty)\n4. Preheat the pan on mid heat. Browning both sides of the patties but not cooking all the way through. Those become leftovers to freeze and cooked thoroughly as reheated for future meals.\n5. Thoroughly cook the remaining two patties for dinner that night.\n6. Make your burger with whatever toppings you prefer.'),
	(382, '65e3af887349307288afe8a6', '2025-04-27 21:20:59', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 6 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 3/4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 1 pound ground beef or turkey or jackfruit\n\n\nMashed potato ingredients:\n- 3 pounds potatoes, rinsed and cubed\n- 4 tablespoons butter\n- 1 cup milk\n- 1 1/2 cup grated Pecorino Romano cheese\n- 3/4 tablespoon sea salt\n- ground back pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat.\n2. Stir in the salt, pepper and thyme.\n3. Add the veggies and heat until cooked properly.\n4. In another pot, brown the ground meat.\n5. In a third pot, make the mashed potatoes. Add in the butter, milk cheese and salt and pepper after drained and mashed.\n6. Layer all the ingredients into a large dish. Veggies and meat stirred together. Mashed potatoes layered on top.'),
	(383, '67fc058a3968a44cf95a9b8c', '2025-04-27 21:21:31', 'Makes 6 burritos. Can prep insides ahead of time.\n\n- 2 sweet potatoes, peeled and cubed small (about 3-4 cups)\n- 1 red pepper, diced small\n- Coconut oil\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon chili powder\n- ½ teaspoon salt\n- ¼ teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 (15-ounce) can black beans, rinsed and drained\n- 1 cup shredded cheddar cheese\n- 12 tortillas as will likely need to double them up\n\nInstructions\n\n- Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. In a large bowl, toss together the sweet potatoes and red pepper with the oil, cumin, onion powder, chili powder, salt and pepper. Dump the coated veggies onto a large rimmed baking sheet and roast for 18-20 minutes, tossing halfway through. The vegetables should be tender but not mushy at the end of cooking time.\n- Let the vegetable mixture cool. Scrape the mixture into a large bowl and toss with the black beans. Taste the mixture and add additional salt and pepper to taste, if needed. Refrigerate the mixture until ready to assemble the burritos or use immediately.\n- Place 4 tortillas on a microwave-safe plate and cover with a damp paper towel. Microwave for 15-20 seconds until the tortillas are pliable. (Warm up 1/2 cupish of the mixture if premade) Place 1/4 cup or so of the mixture in the center of the tortilla and top with a sprinkle with shredded cheese. Fold in the sides of the tortilla and roll up. Place seam-side down on a baking sheet. Repeat with the remaining tortillas until you have all the burritos you need .\n- Bake in a 375 degree F oven for about 10-15 minutes, until heated through and the top of the tortilla is golden brown. Adjust the baking time as needed depending on if the filling has been refrigerated or not. For a softer tortilla, wrap each burrito in tin foil and heat through. Serve immediately.'),
	(384, '65ece37b52d21abd85f26e02', '2025-05-14 09:36:39', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 2 pound cubbed beef\n- 1/4 cup coconut flour\n- 2 teaspoon paprika\n- 4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 1 teaspoon oregano\n- 1 teaspoon basil\n- 1 teaspoon rosemary\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/4 teaspoon crushed red pepper\n- 1 head cauliflower, chopped\n- 4 large carrots, peeled and chopped\n- 2 bell peppers, chopped\n- 1 onion, chopped\n- 3 stalks of celery, chopped\n- 2 potatoes, chopped\n- 4 cups stock, chicken or beef\n- 1 jar whole tomatoes\n- 1 tablespoon arrowroot powder for thickening, if needed\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat oil in large pot over medium high heat.\n2. Combine coconut flour and spices in a large ziploc bag. And meat to the bag and shake until nicely coated.\n3. Add the seasoned meat to the skillet and brown for 3 minutes. Meat will continue to cook in sauce so browning meat is all you need to do.\n4. Add all vegetables and stir to combine.\n5. Cover and let veggies cook for a few minutes.\n6. Add stock and tomatoes. Stir and bring to a low boil.\n7. Lower heat and let simmer for 10-20. minutes.\n8. Add arrowroot powder to a small amount of cold water. Stir and then add to the stew, stirring to help thicken.'),
	(385, '65ece67dcbf220432b12ece8', '2024-03-09 17:02:16', 'Ingredients\n\n- 3 tablespoons butter\n- 1 large onion, chopped\n- 1 large red bell pepper, chopped\n- 2 medium poblano peppers, seeded and chopped\n- 1 jalapeno pepper, seeded and chopped\n- 2 cloves garlic, chopped\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 tablespoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 3/4 cups chicken stock\n- 1 1/2 cups crushed tomatoes\n- 4 ounces diced green chilies\n- 1 1/2 cup sour cream\n- 5 cups cooked, shredded chicken (substitute is jack fruit and white beans)\n- 4 cups cheddar cheese, grated\n- 16 corn tortillas\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees. Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and all peppers. Cook for about 8-10 minutes, until softened. Sitr in the garlic, chili powder, cumin, salt and cook for 1 minute.\n2. Sprinkle the coconut flour over the vegetable mixture and cook for 1 minute while stirring continuously. Stir in the stock and bring to a simmer for 4 minutes. Remove from the heat and stir in the tomatoes, chilies and sour cream.\n3. Place the chicken in a large bowl. Pour the vegetable mixture over the top and stir until combined.\n4. Place 8 tortillas on the bottom of a 13x9 dish. Top with half of the chicken mixture and then half of the cheese. Repeat with the remaining ingredients. Bake for 45-50 minutes until cheese is bubbly and the edges of the casserole are just turning golden brown.\n\n‌\n\nSource: Deliciouslyorganic.net'),
	(386, '65ecec7b734766a86f3ebd36', '2024-03-09 17:19:13', 'For the sauce:\n\n- 3 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 1/2 teaspoons coconut flour\n- 2 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon dried oregano\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 cups chicken stock\n- 12 ounces tomato paste\n- 1 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n\n#### For the Filling:\n\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 1 large yellow onion, chopped\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1/2 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n- 1 can of Pinto beans\n\n#### For the Wraps:\n\n- 1 recipe savory crepes, page 277 of [The Grain-Free Family Table ](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/the-grain-free-family-table/ "‌")or Siete grain-free tortillas (or corn tortillas)\n- 8 ounces raw cheddar, shredded\n\n### INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Place the coconut oil and coconut flour in a medium sauce pan over medium heat. Whisk constantly and cook until the coconut flour just turns golden brown, about 2 minutes. Add the chili powder, oregano and cumin and cook, stirring frequently until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Whisk in chicken stock, tomato paste and sea salt. Bring to a simmer over medium-low heat and cook until sauce begins to thicken, about 20 minutes.\n2. Place the coconut oil in a large sauté pan over medium heat. Swirl the pan to coat. Add the onion and cook, stirring frequently, until onion is translucent, about 5 minutes. Make a well in the center of the pan and add the cumin. Cook, stirring constantly until the cumin is fragrant, about 30 seconds. Stir cumin into the onions. Add the ground beef and salt. Cook, breaking up the beef with the back of a wooden spoon until beef is no longer pink.\n3. Preheat oven to 400ºF and adjust the rack to the middle position. Pour half the sauce in the bottom of an 11 x 7-inch baking dish and spread it out evenly. Place a crepe on the counter and top with 1/4 cup of the beef filling. Carefully roll the crepe around the beef and place it in the baking dish. Repeat with the remaining beef and crepes. Pour the remaining sauce on top of the enchiladas and sprinkle with the cheese. Bake for 25 minutes, or until golden brown and bubbly on top. Cool for 10 minutes. Serve.\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target "smartCard-inline")'),
	(387, '65ecf156ac509dcad1fe0753', '2024-03-09 17:35:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 4-lb whole chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil, melted\n- dash of salt\n- dash black pepper\n- 1/2 cup chicken broth\n\nInstructions\n\n1. Rinse the chicken and pat it dry. Place in baking pan. Drizzle with oil. Sprinkle on salt and pepper.\n2. Add the stock.\n3. Turn oven to 275 degrees and roast the chicken, covered, for about 3 hours.\n4. Increase to 375 degrees roasting for 30-45 minutes/\n5. Remove from the over allowing to rest 5-10 minutes before carving and serving.'),
	(388, '65ee0b619b77b54774c54f49', '2025-04-30 19:10:48', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 8 ounces baby spinach leaves (fresh or frozen)\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- Black pepper to taste\n- 1 package of mushrooms, sliced (optional)\n- 1/4 cup chopped walnuts, toasted (optional) [toast on a pan over medium heat for 4-5 minutes until golden brown]\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. Heat oil over medium heat in a large pot. Remove the seeds from the squash, scoop the flesh out and place in the pot. Add spinach leaves, cream and goat cheese. Toss well until goat cheese has melted and the mixture is hot.\n3. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with walnuts, if using.'),
	(389, '66b7c63aef984308441f4e1c', '2025-04-28 17:29:26', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 cans of salmon makes 14 patties\n- 3 eggs\n- about 2.5 cups of almond flour\n- Coconut oil for pan\n\nDirections\n\n1. Add salmon and eggs to a bowl and mix.\n2. Make 14 patties at 70 grams each\n3. Something here with the flour\n4. ‌\n5. Stove at 4.5'),
	(390, '67f6e86693b75b1c157d8e81', '2025-05-27 17:22:58', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel or 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 20–25 min. Add more liquid if needed. Serve as-is or over rice. Top with cheddar if desired.'),
	(391, '65ee10511a7846ac72bd44c3', '2024-03-10 15:10:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 spaghetti squash\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 6-8oz turkey bacon, sliced or chopped\n- 1 cup onion, diced\n- 1/2 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- Shredded cheddar cheese\n- Optional garnishes: shredded lettuce, tomato, nutritional yeast, black olives\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees. Slice squash lengthwise. Remove the seeds and guts and lay cut side down in a dish with water to cover sides up 1 inch. Roast for 43 minutes if put in right when preheat starts not after; until the squash is tender and pulls away intro strands easily.\n2. While the squash cooks, heat a large skillet on medium high.\n3. Cut 6-8 oz of sliced bacon in to cubes. Dice the onions. Mix together dry spices in a small dish.\n4. Melt the coconut oil in the preheated skillet. Add the bacon. Cook for 3-5 minutes.\n5. Add onions and saute with the bacon for 2-3 minutes or until the onions have softened slightly.\n6. Noe the ground beef gets added to the bacon and onion. Mix it well, sprinkle in the spices. Cook until ground beef is done.\n7. Harvest the squash and combine it with the meats. Stir all together.\n8. Top with cheese. Bake for 15 minutes and 375 degrees.\n9. Remove from oven and top with any optional ingredients.'),
	(392, '65ee228db885a5033c35e542', '2024-03-10 17:02:20', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 3/4 cup onion, diced\n- 1-2 marina sauce jars\n- coconut oil\n- 1 medium spaghetti squash\n- 2 medium zucchini\n- 8 oz grated cheddar cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon nutmeg\n- salt and pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees to cook squash for 43 minutes putting it in at start of preheat. To prep squash, cut lengthwise and remove string and seeds. Place face down in baking dish with water 1-inch up to the sides.\n2. Brown the ground beef and onions.\n3. Slice zucchini lengthwise into 1/8 inch slices.\n4. Once the spaghetti squash is cooked, shred the inside of the squash with a fork into a strainer. Gently press down on the squash to drain out some of the liquid.\n5. Mix the spaghetti squash with 2/3 of the grated cheese, nutmeg, salt and pepper. Set aside.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, build your lasagne. Zucchini slices on the bottom, spread half of the spaghetti squash mixture, spread half the meat mixture, finish with half of the tomato sauce. Repeat. Finish by adding the remaining zucchini slices (if you have any). Add the remaining cheese.\n7. Bake for 25-30 minutes.'),
	(393, '65ee2de69fd5eb92ee41ba40', '2024-03-10 17:15:42', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 28 oz jar spaghetti sauce\n- 3 medium zucchini or 1 eggplant, sliced 1/8 inch thick\n- sea salt\n- Cashew Ricotta Cheese (see that recipe card)\n- 16 oz shredded mozzarella cheese\n- 1/4 cup PR cheese\n- 1 large egg\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a medium skillet, brown meat. Drain. Add the marina sauce to the meat. Simmer on low while prepping the next steps.\n2. Slice the zucchini or eggplant into slices. Lightly salt the slices and set aside for 10 minutes. Salting it helps to take out the moisture. After 10 minutes, blot excess moisture with a paper towel.\n3. On a skillet, grill zucchini on each side until cooked, about 1-2 minutes per side. Place on a paper towel to soak any additional moisture.\n4. Preheat oven to 350 degrees.\n5. In medium bowl, mix the cashew ricotta, pr cheese and egg. Stir well.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, spread some sauce on the bottom. Layer the zucchini. Then ricotta mixture. Top with mozzarella. Repeat the process until all ingredients are used up. Top with sauce and mozzarella.\n7. Cover with foil and bake for 30 minutes.'),
	(394, '65ee2b079d6349ae5cd0a4ae', '2024-03-10 17:41:45', 'Note: For the veggies-can look for a frozen veggie blend to make this easier.\n\nIngredients (these ingredients are all doubled as this freezes well)\n\n- 8 tablespoon butter\n- 4 leeks, roughly chopped\n- 4 carrots, roughly chopped\n- 2 celery stalk, roughly chopped\n- 5 russet potatoes, diced\n- 6 zucchini, cut into 1 inch pieces\n- 8-10 cups chicken stock\n- 2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in the jumbo pot. Add leeks, carrots, celery. Low-medium heat, cover, cook for 20 minutes.\n2. Add potatoes and stock and thyme. Bring to a boil. Simmer for 10 minutes.\n3. Add zucchini. Simmer 15 more minutes. Until zucchini and potatoes are fork tender.\n4. Add salt and pepper.\n5. Using a hand immersion blender, puree the soup. Be careful not to fill the pot too high or this will be very messy.\n6. Season to taste with salt and pepper.'),
	(395, '65ee33402e06e43ef6df6ab4', '2024-03-10 17:40:35', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon butter\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoon dried italian seasoning\n- 6 cups chicken stock\n- 1 pound chicken thighs\n- 14 ounces diced tomatoes\n- 10 ounces frozen spinach leaves\n- Sea salt\n- PR cheese for sprinkling on top\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in a large pot over medium heat. Add garlic and italian seasoning. Pour in stock. Bring to a boil.\n2. Add chicken cooking for 12-15 minutes, until chicken is cooked through. Using a pair of tongs, remove the chicken placing on a cutting board.\n3. Add tomatoes and spinach to the soup and cook for 5-10 minutes.\n4. Chop chicken into bite-sized pieces. Season with sea salt.\n5. Ladle into bowls and garnish with PR cheese.'),
	(396, '65ee372e7bb627c87df43ca2', '2024-03-10 17:46:25', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 3 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 4 cups white beans\n- 4 cups kidney beans\n- 4 cups pinto beans\n- 4 cups chicken broth\n- cheddar cheese\n- salt and pepper to taste\n- Cayenne pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a large pot, add beans and broth and spices. Boil. Simmer, covered, 10 minutes.\n2. Blend with immersion blender.\n3. Serve with cheese on top.'),
	(397, '66804801d104693530f1c13c', '2024-06-29 12:44:39', 'Don\'t put nuggets in until preheat is done \nPlace parchment paper or equivalent in oven\nPreheat 425\nLay 4-6 nuggets in oven \nSet time for 16 minutes\nFlip nuggets over\nSet timer for another 6-7 minutes (check periodically for preferred brownness)\n\nIf you want veggie, we have mixed veggies, green beans, and broccoli. 1/2 to 1 C covered with water. Bring to boil, reduce heat to light boil for 3-4 minutes (broccoli may need an additional min or two)'),
	(398, '67e09ccb91874e7d03e8bac7', '2025-03-23 18:47:00', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1tsp Black pepper\n- 1/4 cup sunflower seeds, toasted (optional)\n- 1 Cup pasta per serving \n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with sunflower seeds, if using.\n3. Each serving can be done with a cup of penne pasta.'),
	(399, '67f6c4722785635c12d6bfef', '2025-04-09 14:03:49', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp chili powder\n- Salt + pepper to taste\n- Corn or flour tortillas\n  **Optional toppings:** diced tomato, avocado, cheese\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Heat a skillet, toss in black beans + spices, stir until warm and a little thickened.\n2. Warm tortillas.\n3. Spoon beans onto tortillas and pile on your toppings.'),
	(400, '67f6d1a82f24c4e9aa7fd634', '2025-04-09 15:00:02', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained)\n- 1 cup rice (white or brown)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes (with juice)\n- 1 bell pepper, chopped\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp cumin + 1/2 tsp smoked paprika (optional: chili powder, garlic)\n- Salt & pepper\n- Optional toppings: cheese, avocado, green onion, hot sauce\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion + pepper in a bit of oil until soft.\n2. Add spices, stir for a minute.\n3. Add rice, beans, tomatoes, and broth.\n4. Bring to a boil, then reduce to low, cover, and simmer until rice is cooked (about 20 min for white, 35-40 for brown).\n5. Fluff and top as you like!'),
	(401, '67f6d1f2c9c94bac53e7a203', '2025-04-09 15:01:07', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 large sweet potato, cubed\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie broth\n- 1 tsp cumin, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, 1/4 tsp cinnamon (optional but amazing)\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion until soft.\n2. Add sweet potato, beans, tomatoes, broth, and spices.\n3. Simmer until sweet potato is fork-tender (20–25 min).\n4. Taste, season, and top with avocado or a swirl of yogurt.'),
	(402, '67f6d2beff0244014051ceb1', '2025-04-09 15:04:22', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup rice\n- 1 can coconut milk (full-fat or light)\n- 1 cup water or broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp ginger powder\n- Salt to taste\n- Optional: lime, cilantro, chili flakes\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Dump it all in a pot.\n2. Bring to boil, then simmer covered 18–20 min until rice is done.\n3. Stir, taste, and finish with lime juice or chili flakes if you want a little kick.'),
	(403, '67f6d7a90dfe222116694fa7', '2025-04-09 15:25:31', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Weeknight protein bomb\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt, pepper\n- Optional: cooked rice or GF pasta to serve over\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add tomato sauce + black beans, simmer 5–10 min. Serve over rice or pasta. Add cheese if you want.'),
	(404, '67f6d7e733d4ebefa32d1be1', '2025-04-09 15:26:19', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Creamy + slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Optional: chili flakes, chopped spinach\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything 15 minutes. Blend half (optional) for a creamier texture. Garnish with a swirl of coconut milk or cheese.'),
	(405, '67f6d814dd2e1cc72fa318bd', '2025-04-09 15:27:11', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk **or** 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic & onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese for top\n\n**How-to:**\nMix cooked pasta, beans, sauce of choice, and seasonings. Pour into dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(406, '67f6d83b8b90154cd16b9174', '2025-04-09 15:27:46', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Meaty vegan stew\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded with hands or fork)\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 tsp each: garlic powder, onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add tomatoes + black beans. Simmer 20–30 min until thick. Great with rice or GF cornbread.'),
	(407, '67f6d86e51c3735b50f5af4e', '2025-04-09 15:28:38', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cheesy & hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Cooked GF pasta or rice\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Mix with beans, sauce, and pasta or rice. Spread in baking dish, top with cheese, bake 15–20 min.'),
	(408, '67f6d3181ecadb49da60fcbf', '2025-04-09 15:26:27', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained)\n- 3 cloves garlic, minced (or 1 tsp garlic powder)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Olive oil\n- Salt, pepper, pinch of chili flakes\n- Optional: handful of chopped kale or spinach, squeeze of lemon\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté garlic in olive oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, broth, herbs, and seasonings.\n3. Simmer 15–20 minutes until thickened and cozy.\n4. Add greens at the end if using, and finish with lemon juice for brightness.'),
	(409, '67f6d365cbfc9cd17164d86a', '2025-04-09 15:26:25', 'Creamy without cream, and full of flavor.\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb pasta (short shapes like orecchiette, penne, or shells)\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 3 cloves garlic (minced or sliced)\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 tsp rosemary or thyme (dried or fresh)\n- 1/2 cup veggie or chicken broth (or pasta water)\n- Salt, pepper, chili flakes to taste\n- Optional: squeeze of lemon, grated Parmesan, or a handful of spinach\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Cook pasta in salted water until al dente. Save about 1/2 cup pasta water.\n2. While pasta cooks, heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat.\n3. Add garlic and herbs. Sauté until garlic is fragrant.\n4. Add cannellini beans and broth (or pasta water). Simmer 5–7 min until beans start to break down a bit and sauce thickens.\n5. Stir in cooked pasta. Toss to coat and warm through.\n6. Add lemon juice or Parmesan if using, and adjust seasoning.'),
	(410, '67f6d89c820310bb4d5b7dfe', '2025-04-09 15:29:30', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Cozy, Italian-inspired\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cooked chopped spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend one can of beans with broth + coconut milk. Simmer with second can and seasonings for 15–20 minutes. Add greens last if using.'),
	(411, '67f6d8d2bf3d8478b9410442', '2025-04-09 15:30:17', '**Type:** Casserole/Bake\n**Vibe:** Dairy-free Alfredo-ish\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: smoked paprika or Italian herbs\n- Optional: shredded cheddar on top\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans, coconut milk, and seasonings. Mix with pasta, pour into baking dish, top with cheese (if using), bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(412, '67f6d8ed0ba832c5d59c9c5b', '2025-04-28 21:45:22', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-rich and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, stir in beans + sauce, simmer 10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(413, '67f6d9453c6e3f0e54ecc6a9', '2025-04-09 15:32:18', '**Type:** One-pot (or two-pot)\n**Vibe:** Rustic & herby\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 can diced tomatoes\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- White rice (served with or cooked into the beans)\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer beans, tomatoes, seasonings together 15 min. Serve over cooked rice or cook rice directly in with extra liquid.'),
	(414, '67f6d9860b7fd3757b014d4a', '2025-04-09 15:33:21', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild & creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp turmeric\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: serve over rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients together for 15–20 min. Serve over rice or scoop with flatbread if you’ve got it.'),
	(415, '67f6d9aa58884dc595fe1691', '2025-04-27 21:29:03', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty & homey\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1–2 chicken breasts (cooked & chopped or shredded)\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Mashed potatoes (can be made with butter + coconut milk)\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, broth, and seasoning in a casserole dish. Top with mashed potatoes. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(416, '67f6db51765d2af8a6120b7d', '2025-04-09 15:41:00', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Rich, soft, almost risotto-like\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 2 cups broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté seasonings in olive oil, add rice and liquid, bring to boil. Add beans halfway through. Simmer covered 18–20 min. Stir at the end—it’ll get creamy!'),
	(417, '67f6db7c34cc1b5aba24924f', '2025-04-09 15:41:37', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Smooth and simple\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Thyme or rosemary\n- Optional: a handful of spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Blend half or all for a smooth texture.'),
	(418, '67f6db98db7791bf47f312e3', '2025-04-09 15:42:03', '**Type:** One-skillet meal\n**Vibe:** Hearty and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Onion powder, garlic powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Stir in beans and tomato sauce. Simmer for 5–10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(419, '67f6dbb11897fad863756c6b', '2025-04-09 15:42:29', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Mild and creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings. Toss with pasta, put in baking dish, top with cheese. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(420, '67f6dbca7dc8d6736fe0c669', '2025-04-09 15:42:55', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Creamy and lightly spiced\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Cumin, turmeric, chili powder (optional)\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning to taste. Serve hot.'),
	(421, '67f6dbf15835da0a7474d6a8', '2025-04-09 15:43:32', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cozy classic with a twist\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (cubed)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme\n- Optional: GF biscuit topping or mashed potatoes\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, sauce in baking dish. Top with biscuits or mash. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 min.'),
	(422, '67f6dc0b38817fdb9a7f5ccc', '2025-04-13 13:28:47', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty & meaty without meat\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/4 cup water\n- 1 tsp salt\n- 1 tsp Garlic\n- 1 tsp onion powder\n- 1tsp paprika\n- 1 tsp oregano\n- Optional: coconut milk splash at the end\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans & tomatoes, simmer 20–30 min. Great on its own or over pasta or rice.'),
	(423, '67f6e574478306dc9e9ca55c', '2025-04-09 16:24:13', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Optional: peas or frozen mixed veggies\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together 20 minutes until creamy. Add frozen veggies near the end. Serve hot over rice.'),
	(424, '67f6e5a37594122dcbc2377e', '2025-04-09 16:25:42', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-packed, saucy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n- Optional: frozen corn or peas\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with seasonings, stir in chickpeas, Ro-Tel, and veggies. Simmer for 10 minutes.'),
	(425, '67f6e6027c1618ec53193a84', '2025-04-09 16:27:00', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Creamy & veggie-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli + carrots (from a veggie mix)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano or thyme\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20–25 minutes. Adjust thickness with more broth or milk. Serve with a spoon and a blanket.'),
	(426, '67f6e6456e211ca1e4aa1d01', '2025-04-09 16:27:53', '**Type:** Creamy pasta\n**Vibe:** White sauce–style, dairy-free\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend chickpeas, coconut milk, and seasonings. Heat in a saucepan, stir in pasta. Top with cheese if desired. Creamy, cozy, and satisfying'),
	(427, '67f6e6733fb047dae933107e', '2025-04-09 16:28:40', '**Type:** Chili-style\n**Vibe:** Simple and spicy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn or mixed veg\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: top with cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20 minutes. Add cheese at the end if using. Serve in a bowl or over rice.'),
	(428, '67f6e6b89008710652e5ceae', '2025-04-09 16:29:49', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty, like a gratin\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 2 cups cooked diced potatoes\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Top with cheese (if using) and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes.'),
	(429, '67f6e6e42de01a2f2a95d602', '2025-04-09 16:30:25', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Warm, earthy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth with seasonings. Add chickpeas and veggies halfway through. Stir occasionally. Done in ~20 min.'),
	(430, '67f6e742e6f1c9d1c849f7d0', '2025-04-09 16:31:57', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Silky, earthy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Blend part of the beans for a creamy texture or leave chunky. Top with cheddar if you like.'),
	(431, '67f6e7823bceb1b3d8bcc968', '2025-04-09 16:33:03', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty and slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with seasonings. Add beans, tomato sauce, and veggies. Simmer until heated through. Serve solo or over rice.'),
	(432, '67f6e7a7c0bdb6909c3d367d', '2025-04-09 16:33:38', '**Type:** Pasta\n**Vibe:** Mild, creamy, and dreamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Optional: grated cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings until smooth. Heat gently, toss with pasta, and top with cheese if using.'),
	(433, '67f6e7c1f4b788ab03a88cf1', '2025-04-09 16:34:04', '**Type:** Oven-bake\n**Vibe:** Roasty and nourishing\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1.5 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 1/4 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary, salt\n- Optional: cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Bake at 375°F for 25–30 minutes until golden. Top with cheese if desired.'),
	(434, '67f6e7dc4583dbdd2be5be67', '2025-04-09 16:34:32', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild curry, plant-powered\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth or Ro-Tel\n- Cumin, garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans, liquid, and simmer 20 min. Serve with rice or as a stew.'),
	(435, '67f6e803175f15f0baeac4bf', '2025-04-09 16:35:02', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Rustic, creamy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- 1/4–1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheese for topping\n\n**How-to:**\nMix everything, transfer to a baking dish, top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes.'),
	(436, '67f6e81c3a17c51bd6839c7f', '2025-04-09 16:35:28', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen peas or green beans\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning and serve with a spoon and a smile.'),
	(437, '67f6e8831688ad96ae92de1b', '2025-06-02 17:33:29', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory & protein-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 3/4 teaspoon Garlic powder\n- 3/4 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/2 teaspoon tumeric\n- 1/4 teaspoon salt\n- Optional: frozen peas or carrots\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add beans and coconut milk, simmer 15–20 minutes. Serve over rice.'),
	(438, '67f6e8a24e9fd13663bf250d', '2025-04-09 16:37:46', '**Type:** Brothy soup\n**Vibe:** Lighter but filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2–1 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 20 minutes. Optional: blend a portion for a thicker texture.'),
	(439, '67f6e8c26dddd811aa4785a0', '2025-04-09 16:38:19', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy & cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nStir all ingredients together in a baking dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(440, '67f6fe57c9b34bebc5416b69', '2025-04-09 18:10:44', '**Type:** Stir-fry\n**Vibe:** Quick and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded jackfruit with spices, add beans and Ro-Tel. Stir-fry until warmed through. Serve over rice'),
	(441, '67f6fade968000a006f6d470', '2025-04-09 17:55:38', '**Type:** One-pot rice dish\n**Vibe:** Quick & flavorful\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen corn or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nCook everything together in a pot. Simmer 15–20 minutes until rice is done and beans are tender.'),
	(442, '67f6fb0e0c712bac84d6e895', '2025-04-09 17:56:26', '**Type:** One-skillet creamy meal\n**Vibe:** Unexpectedly delicious\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme or curry powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté broccoli briefly, then add kidney beans and coconut milk with seasonings. Simmer until everything is tender and creamy.'),
	(443, '67f6fb2d2e2d1f757637bfa8', '2025-04-09 17:56:57', '**Type:** Skillet hash\n**Vibe:** Sweet, savory, and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1–2 cups cubed sweet potatoes (frozen or pre-cooked)\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n- Optional: ground chicken or beef\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté sweet potatoes until browned and soft. Add beans (and meat, if using), season, and cook until warmed through.'),
	(444, '67f6fb610f93ed8503be7f75', '2025-04-09 17:57:50', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Rich, cozy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 lb ground beef (or ground chicken)\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground meat, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes, adding veggies if you like.'),
	(445, '67f6fc015ab7e5dd2c1d4a16', '2025-04-09 18:00:41', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Spicy and robust\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine everything in a pot and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a side of rice or top with cheese.'),
	(446, '67f6fc2720d00eb77da6f821', '2025-04-09 18:01:07', '**Type:** One-pot chili\n**Vibe:** Hearty, plant-based\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with seasonings, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 30 minutes. Serve with rice or cornbread if desired.'),
	(447, '67f6fc43a4ddded4136e8275', '2025-04-09 18:05:30', '**Type:** One-pan rice dish\n**Vibe:** Flavor-packed, filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth, then add beans and veggies halfway through. Simmer until rice is cooked and beans are tender.'),
	(448, '67f6fd48e0026eacba4fd400', '2025-04-09 18:05:55', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Hearty and cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and tomato sauce in a baking dish. Top with cheese and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(449, '67f6fd69a70a93ba954db476', '2025-04-09 18:06:30', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory and satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, then add beans and coconut milk. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(450, '67f6fd876ff8e5425018be54', '2025-04-09 18:06:58', '**Type:** One-pan curry\n**Vibe:** Creamy and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Ground chicken\n- Garlic/onion powder, curry powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground chicken with spices, then add beans and liquids. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve with rice.'),
	(451, '67f6fda74d30ab49c784ad5b', '2025-05-07 17:27:58', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Bold and hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 teaspoon Chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes. Serve over corn mash (aka polenta), or top with cheese if desired.'),
	(452, '67f6fded3a189d2d126507a9', '2025-04-09 18:08:43', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Simple, savory, and smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 chicken breasts, cooked and shredded\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded chicken with seasonings, then add beans and Ro-Tel. Simmer with coconut milk for 15 minutes until everything is warm and combined.'),
	(453, '67f6fe0eeb47261f077fc5bc', '2025-04-09 18:09:15', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Hearty and veggie-packed\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine all ingredients and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a slice of gluten-free bread or over rice if desired.'),
	(454, '67f6fe2faf8069db3ed70ff9', '2025-04-09 18:09:47', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy, cheesy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and Ro-Tel in a baking dish. Top with cheese if desired. Bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(455, '67f6fe8de3ffa0131aebcc34', '2025-04-09 18:11:28', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Simple and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nMix rice, beans, Ro-Tel, and coconut milk. Pour into a baking dish and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until rice is cooked and bubbly.'),
	(456, '67f6feb7dc439bf5eff6cd44', '2025-04-09 18:12:06', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Smoky and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, smoked paprika, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup broth\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground beef with spices, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 20–25 minutes until everything is cooked through.'),
	(457, '68005051861ebf2dfc1c351e', '2025-04-16 19:51:52', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp coconut oil\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel (or canned tomatoes + green chiles)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt to taste\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- Optional: frozen corn or mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Heat oil in skillet, add seasonings and Ro-Tel, cook 2–3 min.\n2. Add beans and frozen veggies (if using), cook until heated.\n3. Stir in cooked rice and simmer 5–10 minutes.'),
	(458, '680050b91ed28e261cc3dbb2', '2025-04-16 19:52:59', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 chicken breast (cubed)\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp paprika\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1–1.5 cups water or broth\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown chicken in oil. Add seasonings.\n2. Stir in tomatoes, beans, water/broth, and veggies.\n3. Simmer covered for 15–20 min.'),
	(459, '680050f9448a7574075a59ea', '2025-04-16 19:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit, drained & shredded\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/4 tsp oregano\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook jackfruit in a pan to brown slightly.\n2. Add seasonings, Ro-Tel, and pinto beans.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min, mash slightly if desired.'),
	(460, '6800511b1f2c891143a064db', '2025-04-16 19:54:00', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 2 cups water or broth\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté seasonings in oil for 1 min.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, veggies, and broth.\n3. Simmer 20–30 minutes until veggies are tender.'),
	(461, '68005183a8bc2730a5655f53', '2025-04-16 19:55:53', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp oregano\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: nutritional yeast or mild cheddar (if tolerated)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Blend or mash beans for smoother texture (optional).\n2. Heat oil and seasonings, then add beans and tomato sauce.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min. Serve over gluten-free pasta.'),
	(462, '680051a5d487414bc769ea25', '2025-04-16 19:56:21', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 tsp curry powder\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1 cup frozen veggies\n- 1 cup cooked rice or serve over it\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook spices in oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, and veggies. Simmer 10–15 min.\n3. Serve over rice or stir in to make a one-pot dish.'),
	(463, '6824bb4a783db57b9ed8e3ca', '2025-05-14 10:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 jar marinara sauce\n- Canned green beans or sweet peas\n- Italian seasoning\n- garlic powder\n- onion powder\n- salt\n- pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook the ground chicken in a pot until browned.\n2. Add marinara sauce and a bit of water to loosen.\n3. Stir in drained beans (all 3 types) and canned green beans or peas.\n4. Season well with Italian herbs and simmer until flavors blend.\n5. Serve hot either as a stew or scoop into warmed almond flour tortillas for wraps.\n6. Divide into three meals.'),
	(464, '6824babde9b3732c346f3c9d', '2025-05-14 10:53:17', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Tortillas chips\n- Chili Powder\n- Cumin\n- Garlic Powder\n- Onion Powder\n- Paprika\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown the ground beef in a skillet, drain excess fat.\n2. Add frozen mixed vegetables and cook until softened.\n3. Stir in drained black beans and season with chili powder, cumin, etc.\n4. Add a little tomato sauce or water to bind the mix.\n5. Layer over tortilla chips or crush chips on top for a crunchy topping.\n6. Portion out into three meals. Optionally serve with salsa or cheese (if available).\n   '),
	(465, '680051ccffdc026a527075ab', '2025-04-16 19:56:58', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can kidney beans (optional combo)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook all ingredients in a pot over medium heat.\n2. Simmer uncovered for 20–30 min to thicken.\n3. Serve as-is or over rice'),
	(466, '6824bbd5acc27f4664c20175', '2025-05-14 10:52:57', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef (or skip for a vegetarian version)\n- 1 can chickpeas or kidney beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Almond flour tortillas\n- Paprika\n- Cumin\n- Garlic powder\n- Salt\n- black pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté the ground beef (if using) until browned.\n2. Drain excess fat.\n3. Add frozen mixed vegetables and sauté until tender.\n4. Stir in drained beans (chickpeas or kidney beans).\n5. Season well with spices using paprika, cumin, garlic powder, and pepper.\n6. Cook until everything is heated through and slightly crispy.\n7. Spoon into almond flour tortillas and wrap. Serve warm or grilled slightly for a toasted wrap.'),
	(467, '65e35de41116a7a22e54b319', '2025-05-14 10:01:12', '**Ingredients for 3 medium crusts:**\n\n3 cups almond flour\n\n1 1/2 cups arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons baking powder\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons salt\n\n2 1/4 teaspoon oregano\n\n3/8 teaspoon black pepper\n\n4 eggs\n\n3/4 cups milk\n\n**Directions:**\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 425 degrees.\n2. Line a round pizza pan or cookie sheet with parchment paper. (I have 4 pizza pans so I can bake all three at once)\n3. Combine the dry ingredients in a large bowl. Whisk to blend together.\n4. Add eggs and milk to the dry ingredients. Mix well. The batter will be runny—not like typical pizza dough.\n5. Use a spatula to spread the batter evenly onto the pan in a circle shape.\n6. Bake the crust in the preheated oven for 8-12 minutes.\n7. Remove crust from oven and top with sauce and desired toppings. Or freeze the crust for later. Once cooled, place parchment paper between the crusts and they will store perfectly in a ziplock gallon freezer bag until ready to use. I also make sure the size of my circle stays within the range of a gallon bag for this reason.\n8. Bake for another 10-15 minutes with toppings.\n\n‌\n\n**Other Option: Ingredients for 1 large crust:**\n\n2 cups almond flour\n\n1 cup arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. baking powder\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. salt\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon oregano\n\n1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n\n3 eggs\n\n1/2 cup milk\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/](https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(468, '65e39452587a1979909f4a74', '2025-04-27 21:29:12', '**Serving: 24** **meatballs**\n\n### Ingredients\n\n- 2 pound ground beef\n- 2 large egg\n- 1 onion, minced or onion powder\n- 2 tablespoons tomato paste (can omit)\n- 4 tablespoons dijon mustard\n- 2 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 teaspoon celtic sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon baking soda\n\n### Instructions\n\n- In a large bowl, combine ground beef, egg, and onion\n- Mix in tomato paste, mustard, coconut flour, salt, pepper, and baking soda\n- Use a ¼ cup scoop to form meatballs (about 57 grams each)\n- Place meatballs on a parchment paper lined baking sheet\n- Bake at 350°F for 20-25 minutes, or until instant read thermometer reads 175°F\n- Serve with marinara sauce over spaghetti squash noodles or zucchini noodles\n\nSource: [https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/](https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(469, '65ea48c89c856f6ad662250b', '2025-04-27 21:24:32', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 1 to 1.5 cups kidney beans, cooked or canned\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoons cumin powder\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- Corn chips to serve this all on top of\n- Optional toppings: tomatoes, cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder \n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add spices.\n3. Add kidney beans.\n4. Serve meat and bean mixter over corn chips. Top with desired toppings.'),
	(470, '65e397521ddf77bca5c237fb', '2024-11-04 18:40:08', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder OR 1/2 tspn Chipotle seasoning (reduce to half tablespoon)\n- 1 pound ground beef or **1 can of jackfruit**\n- 28 ounces diced tomatoes (or 1 jar diced and 1 jar crushed)\n- 2 boxes of kidney beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper (reduce to 3/4 teaspoon)\n- Toppings: avocado, sour cream, grated cheddar cheese\n- Optional: Mix in 1-2 Seasoned Rice packets from Costco\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 15-20 minutes.\n5. Adjust seasoning with salt and pepper as needed.'),
	(471, '65e3a05c8c1b5970dcacc97d', '2024-03-11 17:58:55', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1 can of diced tomatoes\n- 2 boxes of pinto beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper\n- Corn tortillas (16 qty)\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 10 minutes.\n5. Fill tortillas, rolled up and into rectangular dish.\n6. Top with cheese.\n7. Bake at 350 degrees for 20 minutes.'),
	(472, '65e3a1e92948d057fe6ebd6d', '2025-04-27 21:21:14', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef, cooked and drained\n- 1 1/2 cups thinly slice potatoes, cooked and drained\n- 1 can coconut milk (entire can)\n- 1 cup milk (replace with water if we don’t have milk)\n- If needed, 1/2 cup water\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2-4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon sugar\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- If needed for thickening, 1 tablespoon tapioca. Mixed with a small amount of cold water before adding.\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook beef separately.\n2. Cook potatoes separately.\n3. To the cooked beef, add the milk and water and all the seasonings.\n4. If needed, add the tapioca thickener at this stage.\n5. Add the cooked sliced potatoes.'),
	(473, '65e3a89d761eefa02d605b06', '2025-05-10 18:41:34', 'Ingredients\n\n- Cubed chicken, cooked separately\n- Pasta, cooked separately\n- Broccoli florets, cooked separately\n- Cream sauce, cooked separately\n  - 1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n  - 1 teaspoon salt\n  - 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n  - 1/2 teaspoon sugar\n  - 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n  - 1 can of coconut milk-ONLY the thick part, drain the water\n  - 3-4 teaspoons of tapioca powder added to a very little splash of milk or cold water\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook the chicken, pasta and broccoli all separately.\n2. Mix the cream sauce ingredients together and bring to a slow boil.\n3. Combine all the ingredients together.'),
	(474, '65e3abc0f8cd991e2ff05bff', '2024-05-03 19:05:41', 'Ingredients:\n\n2 pounds ground beef\n4 teaspoons paprika\n3 teaspoons black pepper\n2 1/2 teaspoons salt\n2 2/3 teaspoon Maple Sugar or Sucanat Sugar\n1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper\n\nOptional: Lettuce, mayo, cheese, rotel\n\nDirections:\n\n1. Mix all spices together.\n2. Mix spices by hand tenderly into the meat so it doesn’t get too tough.\n3. Form 12 patties, flat like tortillas but also loosely packed so doesn’t dry out. (about 80 grams per patty)\n4. Preheat the pan on mid heat. Browning both sides of the patties but not cooking all the way through. Those become leftovers to freeze and cooked thoroughly as reheated for future meals.\n5. Thoroughly cook the remaining two patties for dinner that night.\n6. Make your burger with whatever toppings you prefer.'),
	(475, '65e3af887349307288afe8a6', '2025-04-27 21:20:59', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 6 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 3/4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 1 pound ground beef or turkey or jackfruit\n\n\nMashed potato ingredients:\n- 3 pounds potatoes, rinsed and cubed\n- 4 tablespoons butter\n- 1 cup milk\n- 1 1/2 cup grated Pecorino Romano cheese\n- 3/4 tablespoon sea salt\n- ground back pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat.\n2. Stir in the salt, pepper and thyme.\n3. Add the veggies and heat until cooked properly.\n4. In another pot, brown the ground meat.\n5. In a third pot, make the mashed potatoes. Add in the butter, milk cheese and salt and pepper after drained and mashed.\n6. Layer all the ingredients into a large dish. Veggies and meat stirred together. Mashed potatoes layered on top.'),
	(476, '67fc058a3968a44cf95a9b8c', '2025-04-27 21:21:31', 'Makes 6 burritos. Can prep insides ahead of time.\n\n- 2 sweet potatoes, peeled and cubed small (about 3-4 cups)\n- 1 red pepper, diced small\n- Coconut oil\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon chili powder\n- ½ teaspoon salt\n- ¼ teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 (15-ounce) can black beans, rinsed and drained\n- 1 cup shredded cheddar cheese\n- 12 tortillas as will likely need to double them up\n\nInstructions\n\n- Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. In a large bowl, toss together the sweet potatoes and red pepper with the oil, cumin, onion powder, chili powder, salt and pepper. Dump the coated veggies onto a large rimmed baking sheet and roast for 18-20 minutes, tossing halfway through. The vegetables should be tender but not mushy at the end of cooking time.\n- Let the vegetable mixture cool. Scrape the mixture into a large bowl and toss with the black beans. Taste the mixture and add additional salt and pepper to taste, if needed. Refrigerate the mixture until ready to assemble the burritos or use immediately.\n- Place 4 tortillas on a microwave-safe plate and cover with a damp paper towel. Microwave for 15-20 seconds until the tortillas are pliable. (Warm up 1/2 cupish of the mixture if premade) Place 1/4 cup or so of the mixture in the center of the tortilla and top with a sprinkle with shredded cheese. Fold in the sides of the tortilla and roll up. Place seam-side down on a baking sheet. Repeat with the remaining tortillas until you have all the burritos you need .\n- Bake in a 375 degree F oven for about 10-15 minutes, until heated through and the top of the tortilla is golden brown. Adjust the baking time as needed depending on if the filling has been refrigerated or not. For a softer tortilla, wrap each burrito in tin foil and heat through. Serve immediately.'),
	(477, '65ece37b52d21abd85f26e02', '2025-05-14 09:36:39', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 2 pound cubbed beef\n- 1/4 cup coconut flour\n- 2 teaspoon paprika\n- 4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 1 teaspoon oregano\n- 1 teaspoon basil\n- 1 teaspoon rosemary\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/4 teaspoon crushed red pepper\n- 1 head cauliflower, chopped\n- 4 large carrots, peeled and chopped\n- 2 bell peppers, chopped\n- 1 onion, chopped\n- 3 stalks of celery, chopped\n- 2 potatoes, chopped\n- 4 cups stock, chicken or beef\n- 1 jar whole tomatoes\n- 1 tablespoon arrowroot powder for thickening, if needed\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat oil in large pot over medium high heat.\n2. Combine coconut flour and spices in a large ziploc bag. And meat to the bag and shake until nicely coated.\n3. Add the seasoned meat to the skillet and brown for 3 minutes. Meat will continue to cook in sauce so browning meat is all you need to do.\n4. Add all vegetables and stir to combine.\n5. Cover and let veggies cook for a few minutes.\n6. Add stock and tomatoes. Stir and bring to a low boil.\n7. Lower heat and let simmer for 10-20. minutes.\n8. Add arrowroot powder to a small amount of cold water. Stir and then add to the stew, stirring to help thicken.'),
	(478, '65ece67dcbf220432b12ece8', '2024-03-09 17:02:16', 'Ingredients\n\n- 3 tablespoons butter\n- 1 large onion, chopped\n- 1 large red bell pepper, chopped\n- 2 medium poblano peppers, seeded and chopped\n- 1 jalapeno pepper, seeded and chopped\n- 2 cloves garlic, chopped\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 tablespoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 3/4 cups chicken stock\n- 1 1/2 cups crushed tomatoes\n- 4 ounces diced green chilies\n- 1 1/2 cup sour cream\n- 5 cups cooked, shredded chicken (substitute is jack fruit and white beans)\n- 4 cups cheddar cheese, grated\n- 16 corn tortillas\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees. Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and all peppers. Cook for about 8-10 minutes, until softened. Sitr in the garlic, chili powder, cumin, salt and cook for 1 minute.\n2. Sprinkle the coconut flour over the vegetable mixture and cook for 1 minute while stirring continuously. Stir in the stock and bring to a simmer for 4 minutes. Remove from the heat and stir in the tomatoes, chilies and sour cream.\n3. Place the chicken in a large bowl. Pour the vegetable mixture over the top and stir until combined.\n4. Place 8 tortillas on the bottom of a 13x9 dish. Top with half of the chicken mixture and then half of the cheese. Repeat with the remaining ingredients. Bake for 45-50 minutes until cheese is bubbly and the edges of the casserole are just turning golden brown.\n\n‌\n\nSource: Deliciouslyorganic.net'),
	(479, '65ecec7b734766a86f3ebd36', '2024-03-09 17:19:13', 'For the sauce:\n\n- 3 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 1/2 teaspoons coconut flour\n- 2 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon dried oregano\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 cups chicken stock\n- 12 ounces tomato paste\n- 1 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n\n#### For the Filling:\n\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 1 large yellow onion, chopped\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1/2 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n- 1 can of Pinto beans\n\n#### For the Wraps:\n\n- 1 recipe savory crepes, page 277 of [The Grain-Free Family Table ](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/the-grain-free-family-table/ "‌")or Siete grain-free tortillas (or corn tortillas)\n- 8 ounces raw cheddar, shredded\n\n### INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Place the coconut oil and coconut flour in a medium sauce pan over medium heat. Whisk constantly and cook until the coconut flour just turns golden brown, about 2 minutes. Add the chili powder, oregano and cumin and cook, stirring frequently until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Whisk in chicken stock, tomato paste and sea salt. Bring to a simmer over medium-low heat and cook until sauce begins to thicken, about 20 minutes.\n2. Place the coconut oil in a large sauté pan over medium heat. Swirl the pan to coat. Add the onion and cook, stirring frequently, until onion is translucent, about 5 minutes. Make a well in the center of the pan and add the cumin. Cook, stirring constantly until the cumin is fragrant, about 30 seconds. Stir cumin into the onions. Add the ground beef and salt. Cook, breaking up the beef with the back of a wooden spoon until beef is no longer pink.\n3. Preheat oven to 400ºF and adjust the rack to the middle position. Pour half the sauce in the bottom of an 11 x 7-inch baking dish and spread it out evenly. Place a crepe on the counter and top with 1/4 cup of the beef filling. Carefully roll the crepe around the beef and place it in the baking dish. Repeat with the remaining beef and crepes. Pour the remaining sauce on top of the enchiladas and sprinkle with the cheese. Bake for 25 minutes, or until golden brown and bubbly on top. Cool for 10 minutes. Serve.\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target "smartCard-inline")'),
	(480, '65ecf156ac509dcad1fe0753', '2024-03-09 17:35:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 4-lb whole chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil, melted\n- dash of salt\n- dash black pepper\n- 1/2 cup chicken broth\n\nInstructions\n\n1. Rinse the chicken and pat it dry. Place in baking pan. Drizzle with oil. Sprinkle on salt and pepper.\n2. Add the stock.\n3. Turn oven to 275 degrees and roast the chicken, covered, for about 3 hours.\n4. Increase to 375 degrees roasting for 30-45 minutes/\n5. Remove from the over allowing to rest 5-10 minutes before carving and serving.'),
	(481, '65ee0b619b77b54774c54f49', '2025-04-30 19:10:48', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 8 ounces baby spinach leaves (fresh or frozen)\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- Black pepper to taste\n- 1 package of mushrooms, sliced (optional)\n- 1/4 cup chopped walnuts, toasted (optional) [toast on a pan over medium heat for 4-5 minutes until golden brown]\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. Heat oil over medium heat in a large pot. Remove the seeds from the squash, scoop the flesh out and place in the pot. Add spinach leaves, cream and goat cheese. Toss well until goat cheese has melted and the mixture is hot.\n3. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with walnuts, if using.'),
	(482, '66b7c63aef984308441f4e1c', '2025-04-28 17:29:26', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 cans of salmon makes 14 patties\n- 3 eggs\n- about 2.5 cups of almond flour\n- Coconut oil for pan\n\nDirections\n\n1. Add salmon and eggs to a bowl and mix.\n2. Make 14 patties at 70 grams each\n3. Something here with the flour\n4. ‌\n5. Stove at 4.5'),
	(483, '67f6e86693b75b1c157d8e81', '2025-05-27 17:22:58', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel or 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 20–25 min. Add more liquid if needed. Serve as-is or over rice. Top with cheddar if desired.'),
	(484, '65ee10511a7846ac72bd44c3', '2024-03-10 15:10:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 spaghetti squash\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 6-8oz turkey bacon, sliced or chopped\n- 1 cup onion, diced\n- 1/2 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- Shredded cheddar cheese\n- Optional garnishes: shredded lettuce, tomato, nutritional yeast, black olives\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees. Slice squash lengthwise. Remove the seeds and guts and lay cut side down in a dish with water to cover sides up 1 inch. Roast for 43 minutes if put in right when preheat starts not after; until the squash is tender and pulls away intro strands easily.\n2. While the squash cooks, heat a large skillet on medium high.\n3. Cut 6-8 oz of sliced bacon in to cubes. Dice the onions. Mix together dry spices in a small dish.\n4. Melt the coconut oil in the preheated skillet. Add the bacon. Cook for 3-5 minutes.\n5. Add onions and saute with the bacon for 2-3 minutes or until the onions have softened slightly.\n6. Noe the ground beef gets added to the bacon and onion. Mix it well, sprinkle in the spices. Cook until ground beef is done.\n7. Harvest the squash and combine it with the meats. Stir all together.\n8. Top with cheese. Bake for 15 minutes and 375 degrees.\n9. Remove from oven and top with any optional ingredients.'),
	(485, '65ee228db885a5033c35e542', '2024-03-10 17:02:20', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 3/4 cup onion, diced\n- 1-2 marina sauce jars\n- coconut oil\n- 1 medium spaghetti squash\n- 2 medium zucchini\n- 8 oz grated cheddar cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon nutmeg\n- salt and pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees to cook squash for 43 minutes putting it in at start of preheat. To prep squash, cut lengthwise and remove string and seeds. Place face down in baking dish with water 1-inch up to the sides.\n2. Brown the ground beef and onions.\n3. Slice zucchini lengthwise into 1/8 inch slices.\n4. Once the spaghetti squash is cooked, shred the inside of the squash with a fork into a strainer. Gently press down on the squash to drain out some of the liquid.\n5. Mix the spaghetti squash with 2/3 of the grated cheese, nutmeg, salt and pepper. Set aside.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, build your lasagne. Zucchini slices on the bottom, spread half of the spaghetti squash mixture, spread half the meat mixture, finish with half of the tomato sauce. Repeat. Finish by adding the remaining zucchini slices (if you have any). Add the remaining cheese.\n7. Bake for 25-30 minutes.'),
	(486, '65ee2de69fd5eb92ee41ba40', '2024-03-10 17:15:42', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 28 oz jar spaghetti sauce\n- 3 medium zucchini or 1 eggplant, sliced 1/8 inch thick\n- sea salt\n- Cashew Ricotta Cheese (see that recipe card)\n- 16 oz shredded mozzarella cheese\n- 1/4 cup PR cheese\n- 1 large egg\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a medium skillet, brown meat. Drain. Add the marina sauce to the meat. Simmer on low while prepping the next steps.\n2. Slice the zucchini or eggplant into slices. Lightly salt the slices and set aside for 10 minutes. Salting it helps to take out the moisture. After 10 minutes, blot excess moisture with a paper towel.\n3. On a skillet, grill zucchini on each side until cooked, about 1-2 minutes per side. Place on a paper towel to soak any additional moisture.\n4. Preheat oven to 350 degrees.\n5. In medium bowl, mix the cashew ricotta, pr cheese and egg. Stir well.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, spread some sauce on the bottom. Layer the zucchini. Then ricotta mixture. Top with mozzarella. Repeat the process until all ingredients are used up. Top with sauce and mozzarella.\n7. Cover with foil and bake for 30 minutes.'),
	(487, '65ee2b079d6349ae5cd0a4ae', '2024-03-10 17:41:45', 'Note: For the veggies-can look for a frozen veggie blend to make this easier.\n\nIngredients (these ingredients are all doubled as this freezes well)\n\n- 8 tablespoon butter\n- 4 leeks, roughly chopped\n- 4 carrots, roughly chopped\n- 2 celery stalk, roughly chopped\n- 5 russet potatoes, diced\n- 6 zucchini, cut into 1 inch pieces\n- 8-10 cups chicken stock\n- 2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in the jumbo pot. Add leeks, carrots, celery. Low-medium heat, cover, cook for 20 minutes.\n2. Add potatoes and stock and thyme. Bring to a boil. Simmer for 10 minutes.\n3. Add zucchini. Simmer 15 more minutes. Until zucchini and potatoes are fork tender.\n4. Add salt and pepper.\n5. Using a hand immersion blender, puree the soup. Be careful not to fill the pot too high or this will be very messy.\n6. Season to taste with salt and pepper.'),
	(488, '65ee33402e06e43ef6df6ab4', '2024-03-10 17:40:35', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon butter\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoon dried italian seasoning\n- 6 cups chicken stock\n- 1 pound chicken thighs\n- 14 ounces diced tomatoes\n- 10 ounces frozen spinach leaves\n- Sea salt\n- PR cheese for sprinkling on top\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in a large pot over medium heat. Add garlic and italian seasoning. Pour in stock. Bring to a boil.\n2. Add chicken cooking for 12-15 minutes, until chicken is cooked through. Using a pair of tongs, remove the chicken placing on a cutting board.\n3. Add tomatoes and spinach to the soup and cook for 5-10 minutes.\n4. Chop chicken into bite-sized pieces. Season with sea salt.\n5. Ladle into bowls and garnish with PR cheese.'),
	(489, '65ee372e7bb627c87df43ca2', '2024-03-10 17:46:25', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 3 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 4 cups white beans\n- 4 cups kidney beans\n- 4 cups pinto beans\n- 4 cups chicken broth\n- cheddar cheese\n- salt and pepper to taste\n- Cayenne pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a large pot, add beans and broth and spices. Boil. Simmer, covered, 10 minutes.\n2. Blend with immersion blender.\n3. Serve with cheese on top.'),
	(490, '66804801d104693530f1c13c', '2024-06-29 12:44:39', 'Don\'t put nuggets in until preheat is done \nPlace parchment paper or equivalent in oven\nPreheat 425\nLay 4-6 nuggets in oven \nSet time for 16 minutes\nFlip nuggets over\nSet timer for another 6-7 minutes (check periodically for preferred brownness)\n\nIf you want veggie, we have mixed veggies, green beans, and broccoli. 1/2 to 1 C covered with water. Bring to boil, reduce heat to light boil for 3-4 minutes (broccoli may need an additional min or two)'),
	(491, '67e09ccb91874e7d03e8bac7', '2025-03-23 18:47:00', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1tsp Black pepper\n- 1/4 cup sunflower seeds, toasted (optional)\n- 1 Cup pasta per serving \n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with sunflower seeds, if using.\n3. Each serving can be done with a cup of penne pasta.'),
	(492, '67f6c4722785635c12d6bfef', '2025-04-09 14:03:49', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp chili powder\n- Salt + pepper to taste\n- Corn or flour tortillas\n  **Optional toppings:** diced tomato, avocado, cheese\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Heat a skillet, toss in black beans + spices, stir until warm and a little thickened.\n2. Warm tortillas.\n3. Spoon beans onto tortillas and pile on your toppings.'),
	(493, '67f6d1a82f24c4e9aa7fd634', '2025-04-09 15:00:02', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained)\n- 1 cup rice (white or brown)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes (with juice)\n- 1 bell pepper, chopped\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp cumin + 1/2 tsp smoked paprika (optional: chili powder, garlic)\n- Salt & pepper\n- Optional toppings: cheese, avocado, green onion, hot sauce\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion + pepper in a bit of oil until soft.\n2. Add spices, stir for a minute.\n3. Add rice, beans, tomatoes, and broth.\n4. Bring to a boil, then reduce to low, cover, and simmer until rice is cooked (about 20 min for white, 35-40 for brown).\n5. Fluff and top as you like!'),
	(494, '67f6d1f2c9c94bac53e7a203', '2025-04-09 15:01:07', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 large sweet potato, cubed\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie broth\n- 1 tsp cumin, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, 1/4 tsp cinnamon (optional but amazing)\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion until soft.\n2. Add sweet potato, beans, tomatoes, broth, and spices.\n3. Simmer until sweet potato is fork-tender (20–25 min).\n4. Taste, season, and top with avocado or a swirl of yogurt.'),
	(495, '67f6d2beff0244014051ceb1', '2025-04-09 15:04:22', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup rice\n- 1 can coconut milk (full-fat or light)\n- 1 cup water or broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp ginger powder\n- Salt to taste\n- Optional: lime, cilantro, chili flakes\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Dump it all in a pot.\n2. Bring to boil, then simmer covered 18–20 min until rice is done.\n3. Stir, taste, and finish with lime juice or chili flakes if you want a little kick.'),
	(496, '67f6d7a90dfe222116694fa7', '2025-04-09 15:25:31', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Weeknight protein bomb\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt, pepper\n- Optional: cooked rice or GF pasta to serve over\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add tomato sauce + black beans, simmer 5–10 min. Serve over rice or pasta. Add cheese if you want.'),
	(497, '67f6d7e733d4ebefa32d1be1', '2025-04-09 15:26:19', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Creamy + slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Optional: chili flakes, chopped spinach\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything 15 minutes. Blend half (optional) for a creamier texture. Garnish with a swirl of coconut milk or cheese.'),
	(498, '67f6d814dd2e1cc72fa318bd', '2025-04-09 15:27:11', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk **or** 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic & onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese for top\n\n**How-to:**\nMix cooked pasta, beans, sauce of choice, and seasonings. Pour into dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(499, '67f6d83b8b90154cd16b9174', '2025-04-09 15:27:46', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Meaty vegan stew\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded with hands or fork)\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 tsp each: garlic powder, onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add tomatoes + black beans. Simmer 20–30 min until thick. Great with rice or GF cornbread.'),
	(500, '67f6d86e51c3735b50f5af4e', '2025-04-09 15:28:38', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cheesy & hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Cooked GF pasta or rice\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Mix with beans, sauce, and pasta or rice. Spread in baking dish, top with cheese, bake 15–20 min.'),
	(501, '67f6d3181ecadb49da60fcbf', '2025-04-09 15:26:27', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained)\n- 3 cloves garlic, minced (or 1 tsp garlic powder)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Olive oil\n- Salt, pepper, pinch of chili flakes\n- Optional: handful of chopped kale or spinach, squeeze of lemon\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté garlic in olive oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, broth, herbs, and seasonings.\n3. Simmer 15–20 minutes until thickened and cozy.\n4. Add greens at the end if using, and finish with lemon juice for brightness.'),
	(502, '67f6d365cbfc9cd17164d86a', '2025-04-09 15:26:25', 'Creamy without cream, and full of flavor.\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb pasta (short shapes like orecchiette, penne, or shells)\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 3 cloves garlic (minced or sliced)\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 tsp rosemary or thyme (dried or fresh)\n- 1/2 cup veggie or chicken broth (or pasta water)\n- Salt, pepper, chili flakes to taste\n- Optional: squeeze of lemon, grated Parmesan, or a handful of spinach\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Cook pasta in salted water until al dente. Save about 1/2 cup pasta water.\n2. While pasta cooks, heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat.\n3. Add garlic and herbs. Sauté until garlic is fragrant.\n4. Add cannellini beans and broth (or pasta water). Simmer 5–7 min until beans start to break down a bit and sauce thickens.\n5. Stir in cooked pasta. Toss to coat and warm through.\n6. Add lemon juice or Parmesan if using, and adjust seasoning.'),
	(503, '67f6d89c820310bb4d5b7dfe', '2025-04-09 15:29:30', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Cozy, Italian-inspired\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cooked chopped spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend one can of beans with broth + coconut milk. Simmer with second can and seasonings for 15–20 minutes. Add greens last if using.'),
	(504, '67f6d8d2bf3d8478b9410442', '2025-04-09 15:30:17', '**Type:** Casserole/Bake\n**Vibe:** Dairy-free Alfredo-ish\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: smoked paprika or Italian herbs\n- Optional: shredded cheddar on top\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans, coconut milk, and seasonings. Mix with pasta, pour into baking dish, top with cheese (if using), bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(505, '67f6d8ed0ba832c5d59c9c5b', '2025-04-28 21:45:22', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-rich and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, stir in beans + sauce, simmer 10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(506, '67f6d9453c6e3f0e54ecc6a9', '2025-04-09 15:32:18', '**Type:** One-pot (or two-pot)\n**Vibe:** Rustic & herby\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 can diced tomatoes\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- White rice (served with or cooked into the beans)\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer beans, tomatoes, seasonings together 15 min. Serve over cooked rice or cook rice directly in with extra liquid.'),
	(507, '67f6d9860b7fd3757b014d4a', '2025-04-09 15:33:21', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild & creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp turmeric\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: serve over rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients together for 15–20 min. Serve over rice or scoop with flatbread if you’ve got it.'),
	(508, '67f6d9aa58884dc595fe1691', '2025-04-27 21:29:03', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty & homey\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1–2 chicken breasts (cooked & chopped or shredded)\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Mashed potatoes (can be made with butter + coconut milk)\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, broth, and seasoning in a casserole dish. Top with mashed potatoes. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(509, '67f6db51765d2af8a6120b7d', '2025-04-09 15:41:00', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Rich, soft, almost risotto-like\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 2 cups broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté seasonings in olive oil, add rice and liquid, bring to boil. Add beans halfway through. Simmer covered 18–20 min. Stir at the end—it’ll get creamy!'),
	(510, '67f6db7c34cc1b5aba24924f', '2025-04-09 15:41:37', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Smooth and simple\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Thyme or rosemary\n- Optional: a handful of spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Blend half or all for a smooth texture.'),
	(511, '67f6db98db7791bf47f312e3', '2025-04-09 15:42:03', '**Type:** One-skillet meal\n**Vibe:** Hearty and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Onion powder, garlic powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Stir in beans and tomato sauce. Simmer for 5–10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(512, '67f6dbb11897fad863756c6b', '2025-04-09 15:42:29', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Mild and creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings. Toss with pasta, put in baking dish, top with cheese. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(513, '67f6dbca7dc8d6736fe0c669', '2025-04-09 15:42:55', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Creamy and lightly spiced\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Cumin, turmeric, chili powder (optional)\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning to taste. Serve hot.'),
	(514, '67f6dbf15835da0a7474d6a8', '2025-04-09 15:43:32', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cozy classic with a twist\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (cubed)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme\n- Optional: GF biscuit topping or mashed potatoes\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, sauce in baking dish. Top with biscuits or mash. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 min.'),
	(515, '67f6dc0b38817fdb9a7f5ccc', '2025-04-13 13:28:47', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty & meaty without meat\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/4 cup water\n- 1 tsp salt\n- 1 tsp Garlic\n- 1 tsp onion powder\n- 1tsp paprika\n- 1 tsp oregano\n- Optional: coconut milk splash at the end\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans & tomatoes, simmer 20–30 min. Great on its own or over pasta or rice.'),
	(516, '67f6e574478306dc9e9ca55c', '2025-04-09 16:24:13', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Optional: peas or frozen mixed veggies\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together 20 minutes until creamy. Add frozen veggies near the end. Serve hot over rice.'),
	(517, '67f6e5a37594122dcbc2377e', '2025-04-09 16:25:42', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-packed, saucy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n- Optional: frozen corn or peas\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with seasonings, stir in chickpeas, Ro-Tel, and veggies. Simmer for 10 minutes.'),
	(518, '67f6e6027c1618ec53193a84', '2025-04-09 16:27:00', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Creamy & veggie-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli + carrots (from a veggie mix)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano or thyme\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20–25 minutes. Adjust thickness with more broth or milk. Serve with a spoon and a blanket.'),
	(519, '67f6e6456e211ca1e4aa1d01', '2025-04-09 16:27:53', '**Type:** Creamy pasta\n**Vibe:** White sauce–style, dairy-free\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend chickpeas, coconut milk, and seasonings. Heat in a saucepan, stir in pasta. Top with cheese if desired. Creamy, cozy, and satisfying'),
	(520, '67f6e6733fb047dae933107e', '2025-04-09 16:28:40', '**Type:** Chili-style\n**Vibe:** Simple and spicy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn or mixed veg\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: top with cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20 minutes. Add cheese at the end if using. Serve in a bowl or over rice.'),
	(521, '67f6e6b89008710652e5ceae', '2025-04-09 16:29:49', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty, like a gratin\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 2 cups cooked diced potatoes\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Top with cheese (if using) and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes.'),
	(522, '67f6e6e42de01a2f2a95d602', '2025-04-09 16:30:25', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Warm, earthy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth with seasonings. Add chickpeas and veggies halfway through. Stir occasionally. Done in ~20 min.'),
	(523, '67f6e742e6f1c9d1c849f7d0', '2025-04-09 16:31:57', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Silky, earthy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Blend part of the beans for a creamy texture or leave chunky. Top with cheddar if you like.'),
	(524, '67f6e7823bceb1b3d8bcc968', '2025-04-09 16:33:03', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty and slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with seasonings. Add beans, tomato sauce, and veggies. Simmer until heated through. Serve solo or over rice.'),
	(525, '67f6e7a7c0bdb6909c3d367d', '2025-04-09 16:33:38', '**Type:** Pasta\n**Vibe:** Mild, creamy, and dreamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Optional: grated cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings until smooth. Heat gently, toss with pasta, and top with cheese if using.'),
	(526, '67f6e7c1f4b788ab03a88cf1', '2025-04-09 16:34:04', '**Type:** Oven-bake\n**Vibe:** Roasty and nourishing\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1.5 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 1/4 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary, salt\n- Optional: cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Bake at 375°F for 25–30 minutes until golden. Top with cheese if desired.'),
	(527, '67f6e7dc4583dbdd2be5be67', '2025-04-09 16:34:32', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild curry, plant-powered\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth or Ro-Tel\n- Cumin, garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans, liquid, and simmer 20 min. Serve with rice or as a stew.'),
	(528, '67f6e803175f15f0baeac4bf', '2025-04-09 16:35:02', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Rustic, creamy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- 1/4–1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheese for topping\n\n**How-to:**\nMix everything, transfer to a baking dish, top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes.'),
	(529, '67f6e81c3a17c51bd6839c7f', '2025-04-09 16:35:28', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen peas or green beans\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning and serve with a spoon and a smile.'),
	(530, '67f6e8831688ad96ae92de1b', '2025-06-02 17:33:29', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory & protein-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 3/4 teaspoon Garlic powder\n- 3/4 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/2 teaspoon tumeric\n- 1/4 teaspoon salt\n- Optional: frozen peas or carrots\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add beans and coconut milk, simmer 15–20 minutes. Serve over rice.'),
	(531, '67f6e8a24e9fd13663bf250d', '2025-04-09 16:37:46', '**Type:** Brothy soup\n**Vibe:** Lighter but filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2–1 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 20 minutes. Optional: blend a portion for a thicker texture.'),
	(532, '67f6e8c26dddd811aa4785a0', '2025-04-09 16:38:19', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy & cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nStir all ingredients together in a baking dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(533, '67f6fe57c9b34bebc5416b69', '2025-04-09 18:10:44', '**Type:** Stir-fry\n**Vibe:** Quick and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded jackfruit with spices, add beans and Ro-Tel. Stir-fry until warmed through. Serve over rice'),
	(534, '67f6fade968000a006f6d470', '2025-04-09 17:55:38', '**Type:** One-pot rice dish\n**Vibe:** Quick & flavorful\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen corn or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nCook everything together in a pot. Simmer 15–20 minutes until rice is done and beans are tender.'),
	(535, '67f6fb0e0c712bac84d6e895', '2025-04-09 17:56:26', '**Type:** One-skillet creamy meal\n**Vibe:** Unexpectedly delicious\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme or curry powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté broccoli briefly, then add kidney beans and coconut milk with seasonings. Simmer until everything is tender and creamy.'),
	(536, '67f6fb2d2e2d1f757637bfa8', '2025-04-09 17:56:57', '**Type:** Skillet hash\n**Vibe:** Sweet, savory, and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1–2 cups cubed sweet potatoes (frozen or pre-cooked)\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n- Optional: ground chicken or beef\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté sweet potatoes until browned and soft. Add beans (and meat, if using), season, and cook until warmed through.'),
	(537, '67f6fb610f93ed8503be7f75', '2025-04-09 17:57:50', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Rich, cozy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 lb ground beef (or ground chicken)\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground meat, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes, adding veggies if you like.'),
	(538, '67f6fc015ab7e5dd2c1d4a16', '2025-04-09 18:00:41', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Spicy and robust\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine everything in a pot and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a side of rice or top with cheese.'),
	(539, '67f6fc2720d00eb77da6f821', '2025-04-09 18:01:07', '**Type:** One-pot chili\n**Vibe:** Hearty, plant-based\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with seasonings, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 30 minutes. Serve with rice or cornbread if desired.'),
	(540, '67f6fc43a4ddded4136e8275', '2025-04-09 18:05:30', '**Type:** One-pan rice dish\n**Vibe:** Flavor-packed, filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth, then add beans and veggies halfway through. Simmer until rice is cooked and beans are tender.'),
	(541, '67f6fd48e0026eacba4fd400', '2025-04-09 18:05:55', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Hearty and cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and tomato sauce in a baking dish. Top with cheese and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(542, '67f6fd69a70a93ba954db476', '2025-04-09 18:06:30', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory and satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, then add beans and coconut milk. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(543, '67f6fd876ff8e5425018be54', '2025-04-09 18:06:58', '**Type:** One-pan curry\n**Vibe:** Creamy and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Ground chicken\n- Garlic/onion powder, curry powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground chicken with spices, then add beans and liquids. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve with rice.'),
	(544, '67f6fda74d30ab49c784ad5b', '2025-05-07 17:27:58', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Bold and hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 teaspoon Chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes. Serve over corn mash (aka polenta), or top with cheese if desired.'),
	(545, '67f6fded3a189d2d126507a9', '2025-04-09 18:08:43', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Simple, savory, and smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 chicken breasts, cooked and shredded\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded chicken with seasonings, then add beans and Ro-Tel. Simmer with coconut milk for 15 minutes until everything is warm and combined.'),
	(546, '67f6fe0eeb47261f077fc5bc', '2025-04-09 18:09:15', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Hearty and veggie-packed\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine all ingredients and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a slice of gluten-free bread or over rice if desired.'),
	(547, '67f6fe2faf8069db3ed70ff9', '2025-04-09 18:09:47', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy, cheesy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and Ro-Tel in a baking dish. Top with cheese if desired. Bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(548, '67f6fe8de3ffa0131aebcc34', '2025-04-09 18:11:28', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Simple and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nMix rice, beans, Ro-Tel, and coconut milk. Pour into a baking dish and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until rice is cooked and bubbly.'),
	(549, '67f6feb7dc439bf5eff6cd44', '2025-04-09 18:12:06', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Smoky and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, smoked paprika, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup broth\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground beef with spices, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 20–25 minutes until everything is cooked through.'),
	(550, '68005051861ebf2dfc1c351e', '2025-04-16 19:51:52', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp coconut oil\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel (or canned tomatoes + green chiles)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt to taste\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- Optional: frozen corn or mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Heat oil in skillet, add seasonings and Ro-Tel, cook 2–3 min.\n2. Add beans and frozen veggies (if using), cook until heated.\n3. Stir in cooked rice and simmer 5–10 minutes.'),
	(551, '680050b91ed28e261cc3dbb2', '2025-04-16 19:52:59', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 chicken breast (cubed)\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp paprika\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1–1.5 cups water or broth\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown chicken in oil. Add seasonings.\n2. Stir in tomatoes, beans, water/broth, and veggies.\n3. Simmer covered for 15–20 min.'),
	(552, '680050f9448a7574075a59ea', '2025-04-16 19:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit, drained & shredded\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/4 tsp oregano\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook jackfruit in a pan to brown slightly.\n2. Add seasonings, Ro-Tel, and pinto beans.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min, mash slightly if desired.'),
	(553, '6800511b1f2c891143a064db', '2025-04-16 19:54:00', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 2 cups water or broth\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté seasonings in oil for 1 min.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, veggies, and broth.\n3. Simmer 20–30 minutes until veggies are tender.'),
	(554, '68005183a8bc2730a5655f53', '2025-04-16 19:55:53', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp oregano\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: nutritional yeast or mild cheddar (if tolerated)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Blend or mash beans for smoother texture (optional).\n2. Heat oil and seasonings, then add beans and tomato sauce.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min. Serve over gluten-free pasta.'),
	(555, '680051a5d487414bc769ea25', '2025-04-16 19:56:21', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 tsp curry powder\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1 cup frozen veggies\n- 1 cup cooked rice or serve over it\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook spices in oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, and veggies. Simmer 10–15 min.\n3. Serve over rice or stir in to make a one-pot dish.'),
	(556, '6824bb4a783db57b9ed8e3ca', '2025-05-14 10:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 jar marinara sauce\n- Canned green beans or sweet peas\n- Italian seasoning\n- garlic powder\n- onion powder\n- salt\n- pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook the ground chicken in a pot until browned.\n2. Add marinara sauce and a bit of water to loosen.\n3. Stir in drained beans (all 3 types) and canned green beans or peas.\n4. Season well with Italian herbs and simmer until flavors blend.\n5. Serve hot either as a stew or scoop into warmed almond flour tortillas for wraps.\n6. Divide into three meals.'),
	(557, '6824babde9b3732c346f3c9d', '2025-05-14 10:53:17', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Tortillas chips\n- Chili Powder\n- Cumin\n- Garlic Powder\n- Onion Powder\n- Paprika\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown the ground beef in a skillet, drain excess fat.\n2. Add frozen mixed vegetables and cook until softened.\n3. Stir in drained black beans and season with chili powder, cumin, etc.\n4. Add a little tomato sauce or water to bind the mix.\n5. Layer over tortilla chips or crush chips on top for a crunchy topping.\n6. Portion out into three meals. Optionally serve with salsa or cheese (if available).\n   '),
	(558, '680051ccffdc026a527075ab', '2025-04-16 19:56:58', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can kidney beans (optional combo)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook all ingredients in a pot over medium heat.\n2. Simmer uncovered for 20–30 min to thicken.\n3. Serve as-is or over rice'),
	(559, '6824bbd5acc27f4664c20175', '2025-05-14 10:52:57', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef (or skip for a vegetarian version)\n- 1 can chickpeas or kidney beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Almond flour tortillas\n- Paprika\n- Cumin\n- Garlic powder\n- Salt\n- black pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté the ground beef (if using) until browned.\n2. Drain excess fat.\n3. Add frozen mixed vegetables and sauté until tender.\n4. Stir in drained beans (chickpeas or kidney beans).\n5. Season well with spices using paprika, cumin, garlic powder, and pepper.\n6. Cook until everything is heated through and slightly crispy.\n7. Spoon into almond flour tortillas and wrap. Serve warm or grilled slightly for a toasted wrap.'),
	(560, '65e35de41116a7a22e54b319', '2025-05-14 10:01:12', '**Ingredients for 3 medium crusts:**\n\n3 cups almond flour\n\n1 1/2 cups arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons baking powder\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons salt\n\n2 1/4 teaspoon oregano\n\n3/8 teaspoon black pepper\n\n4 eggs\n\n3/4 cups milk\n\n**Directions:**\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 425 degrees.\n2. Line a round pizza pan or cookie sheet with parchment paper. (I have 4 pizza pans so I can bake all three at once)\n3. Combine the dry ingredients in a large bowl. Whisk to blend together.\n4. Add eggs and milk to the dry ingredients. Mix well. The batter will be runny—not like typical pizza dough.\n5. Use a spatula to spread the batter evenly onto the pan in a circle shape.\n6. Bake the crust in the preheated oven for 8-12 minutes.\n7. Remove crust from oven and top with sauce and desired toppings. Or freeze the crust for later. Once cooled, place parchment paper between the crusts and they will store perfectly in a ziplock gallon freezer bag until ready to use. I also make sure the size of my circle stays within the range of a gallon bag for this reason.\n8. Bake for another 10-15 minutes with toppings.\n\n‌\n\n**Other Option: Ingredients for 1 large crust:**\n\n2 cups almond flour\n\n1 cup arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. baking powder\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. salt\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon oregano\n\n1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n\n3 eggs\n\n1/2 cup milk\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/](https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(561, '65e39452587a1979909f4a74', '2025-04-27 21:29:12', '**Serving: 24** **meatballs**\n\n### Ingredients\n\n- 2 pound ground beef\n- 2 large egg\n- 1 onion, minced or onion powder\n- 2 tablespoons tomato paste (can omit)\n- 4 tablespoons dijon mustard\n- 2 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 teaspoon celtic sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon baking soda\n\n### Instructions\n\n- In a large bowl, combine ground beef, egg, and onion\n- Mix in tomato paste, mustard, coconut flour, salt, pepper, and baking soda\n- Use a ¼ cup scoop to form meatballs (about 57 grams each)\n- Place meatballs on a parchment paper lined baking sheet\n- Bake at 350°F for 20-25 minutes, or until instant read thermometer reads 175°F\n- Serve with marinara sauce over spaghetti squash noodles or zucchini noodles\n\nSource: [https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/](https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(562, '65ea48c89c856f6ad662250b', '2025-04-27 21:24:32', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 1 to 1.5 cups kidney beans, cooked or canned\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoons cumin powder\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- Corn chips to serve this all on top of\n- Optional toppings: tomatoes, cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder \n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add spices.\n3. Add kidney beans.\n4. Serve meat and bean mixter over corn chips. Top with desired toppings.'),
	(563, '65e397521ddf77bca5c237fb', '2024-11-04 18:40:08', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder OR 1/2 tspn Chipotle seasoning (reduce to half tablespoon)\n- 1 pound ground beef or **1 can of jackfruit**\n- 28 ounces diced tomatoes (or 1 jar diced and 1 jar crushed)\n- 2 boxes of kidney beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper (reduce to 3/4 teaspoon)\n- Toppings: avocado, sour cream, grated cheddar cheese\n- Optional: Mix in 1-2 Seasoned Rice packets from Costco\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 15-20 minutes.\n5. Adjust seasoning with salt and pepper as needed.'),
	(564, '65e3a05c8c1b5970dcacc97d', '2024-03-11 17:58:55', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1 can of diced tomatoes\n- 2 boxes of pinto beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper\n- Corn tortillas (16 qty)\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 10 minutes.\n5. Fill tortillas, rolled up and into rectangular dish.\n6. Top with cheese.\n7. Bake at 350 degrees for 20 minutes.'),
	(565, '65e3a1e92948d057fe6ebd6d', '2025-04-27 21:21:14', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef, cooked and drained\n- 1 1/2 cups thinly slice potatoes, cooked and drained\n- 1 can coconut milk (entire can)\n- 1 cup milk (replace with water if we don’t have milk)\n- If needed, 1/2 cup water\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2-4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon sugar\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- If needed for thickening, 1 tablespoon tapioca. Mixed with a small amount of cold water before adding.\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook beef separately.\n2. Cook potatoes separately.\n3. To the cooked beef, add the milk and water and all the seasonings.\n4. If needed, add the tapioca thickener at this stage.\n5. Add the cooked sliced potatoes.'),
	(566, '65e3a89d761eefa02d605b06', '2025-05-10 18:41:34', 'Ingredients\n\n- Cubed chicken, cooked separately\n- Pasta, cooked separately\n- Broccoli florets, cooked separately\n- Cream sauce, cooked separately\n  - 1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n  - 1 teaspoon salt\n  - 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n  - 1/2 teaspoon sugar\n  - 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n  - 1 can of coconut milk-ONLY the thick part, drain the water\n  - 3-4 teaspoons of tapioca powder added to a very little splash of milk or cold water\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook the chicken, pasta and broccoli all separately.\n2. Mix the cream sauce ingredients together and bring to a slow boil.\n3. Combine all the ingredients together.'),
	(567, '65e3abc0f8cd991e2ff05bff', '2024-05-03 19:05:41', 'Ingredients:\n\n2 pounds ground beef\n4 teaspoons paprika\n3 teaspoons black pepper\n2 1/2 teaspoons salt\n2 2/3 teaspoon Maple Sugar or Sucanat Sugar\n1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper\n\nOptional: Lettuce, mayo, cheese, rotel\n\nDirections:\n\n1. Mix all spices together.\n2. Mix spices by hand tenderly into the meat so it doesn’t get too tough.\n3. Form 12 patties, flat like tortillas but also loosely packed so doesn’t dry out. (about 80 grams per patty)\n4. Preheat the pan on mid heat. Browning both sides of the patties but not cooking all the way through. Those become leftovers to freeze and cooked thoroughly as reheated for future meals.\n5. Thoroughly cook the remaining two patties for dinner that night.\n6. Make your burger with whatever toppings you prefer.'),
	(568, '65e3af887349307288afe8a6', '2025-04-27 21:20:59', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 6 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 3/4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 1 pound ground beef or turkey or jackfruit\n\n\nMashed potato ingredients:\n- 3 pounds potatoes, rinsed and cubed\n- 4 tablespoons butter\n- 1 cup milk\n- 1 1/2 cup grated Pecorino Romano cheese\n- 3/4 tablespoon sea salt\n- ground back pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat.\n2. Stir in the salt, pepper and thyme.\n3. Add the veggies and heat until cooked properly.\n4. In another pot, brown the ground meat.\n5. In a third pot, make the mashed potatoes. Add in the butter, milk cheese and salt and pepper after drained and mashed.\n6. Layer all the ingredients into a large dish. Veggies and meat stirred together. Mashed potatoes layered on top.'),
	(569, '67fc058a3968a44cf95a9b8c', '2025-04-27 21:21:31', 'Makes 6 burritos. Can prep insides ahead of time.\n\n- 2 sweet potatoes, peeled and cubed small (about 3-4 cups)\n- 1 red pepper, diced small\n- Coconut oil\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon chili powder\n- ½ teaspoon salt\n- ¼ teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 (15-ounce) can black beans, rinsed and drained\n- 1 cup shredded cheddar cheese\n- 12 tortillas as will likely need to double them up\n\nInstructions\n\n- Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. In a large bowl, toss together the sweet potatoes and red pepper with the oil, cumin, onion powder, chili powder, salt and pepper. Dump the coated veggies onto a large rimmed baking sheet and roast for 18-20 minutes, tossing halfway through. The vegetables should be tender but not mushy at the end of cooking time.\n- Let the vegetable mixture cool. Scrape the mixture into a large bowl and toss with the black beans. Taste the mixture and add additional salt and pepper to taste, if needed. Refrigerate the mixture until ready to assemble the burritos or use immediately.\n- Place 4 tortillas on a microwave-safe plate and cover with a damp paper towel. Microwave for 15-20 seconds until the tortillas are pliable. (Warm up 1/2 cupish of the mixture if premade) Place 1/4 cup or so of the mixture in the center of the tortilla and top with a sprinkle with shredded cheese. Fold in the sides of the tortilla and roll up. Place seam-side down on a baking sheet. Repeat with the remaining tortillas until you have all the burritos you need .\n- Bake in a 375 degree F oven for about 10-15 minutes, until heated through and the top of the tortilla is golden brown. Adjust the baking time as needed depending on if the filling has been refrigerated or not. For a softer tortilla, wrap each burrito in tin foil and heat through. Serve immediately.'),
	(570, '65ece37b52d21abd85f26e02', '2025-05-14 09:36:39', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 2 pound cubbed beef\n- 1/4 cup coconut flour\n- 2 teaspoon paprika\n- 4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 1 teaspoon oregano\n- 1 teaspoon basil\n- 1 teaspoon rosemary\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/4 teaspoon crushed red pepper\n- 1 head cauliflower, chopped\n- 4 large carrots, peeled and chopped\n- 2 bell peppers, chopped\n- 1 onion, chopped\n- 3 stalks of celery, chopped\n- 2 potatoes, chopped\n- 4 cups stock, chicken or beef\n- 1 jar whole tomatoes\n- 1 tablespoon arrowroot powder for thickening, if needed\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat oil in large pot over medium high heat.\n2. Combine coconut flour and spices in a large ziploc bag. And meat to the bag and shake until nicely coated.\n3. Add the seasoned meat to the skillet and brown for 3 minutes. Meat will continue to cook in sauce so browning meat is all you need to do.\n4. Add all vegetables and stir to combine.\n5. Cover and let veggies cook for a few minutes.\n6. Add stock and tomatoes. Stir and bring to a low boil.\n7. Lower heat and let simmer for 10-20. minutes.\n8. Add arrowroot powder to a small amount of cold water. Stir and then add to the stew, stirring to help thicken.'),
	(571, '65ece67dcbf220432b12ece8', '2024-03-09 17:02:16', 'Ingredients\n\n- 3 tablespoons butter\n- 1 large onion, chopped\n- 1 large red bell pepper, chopped\n- 2 medium poblano peppers, seeded and chopped\n- 1 jalapeno pepper, seeded and chopped\n- 2 cloves garlic, chopped\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 tablespoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 3/4 cups chicken stock\n- 1 1/2 cups crushed tomatoes\n- 4 ounces diced green chilies\n- 1 1/2 cup sour cream\n- 5 cups cooked, shredded chicken (substitute is jack fruit and white beans)\n- 4 cups cheddar cheese, grated\n- 16 corn tortillas\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees. Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and all peppers. Cook for about 8-10 minutes, until softened. Sitr in the garlic, chili powder, cumin, salt and cook for 1 minute.\n2. Sprinkle the coconut flour over the vegetable mixture and cook for 1 minute while stirring continuously. Stir in the stock and bring to a simmer for 4 minutes. Remove from the heat and stir in the tomatoes, chilies and sour cream.\n3. Place the chicken in a large bowl. Pour the vegetable mixture over the top and stir until combined.\n4. Place 8 tortillas on the bottom of a 13x9 dish. Top with half of the chicken mixture and then half of the cheese. Repeat with the remaining ingredients. Bake for 45-50 minutes until cheese is bubbly and the edges of the casserole are just turning golden brown.\n\n‌\n\nSource: Deliciouslyorganic.net'),
	(572, '65ecec7b734766a86f3ebd36', '2024-03-09 17:19:13', 'For the sauce:\n\n- 3 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 1/2 teaspoons coconut flour\n- 2 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon dried oregano\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 cups chicken stock\n- 12 ounces tomato paste\n- 1 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n\n#### For the Filling:\n\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 1 large yellow onion, chopped\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1/2 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n- 1 can of Pinto beans\n\n#### For the Wraps:\n\n- 1 recipe savory crepes, page 277 of [The Grain-Free Family Table ](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/the-grain-free-family-table/ "‌")or Siete grain-free tortillas (or corn tortillas)\n- 8 ounces raw cheddar, shredded\n\n### INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Place the coconut oil and coconut flour in a medium sauce pan over medium heat. Whisk constantly and cook until the coconut flour just turns golden brown, about 2 minutes. Add the chili powder, oregano and cumin and cook, stirring frequently until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Whisk in chicken stock, tomato paste and sea salt. Bring to a simmer over medium-low heat and cook until sauce begins to thicken, about 20 minutes.\n2. Place the coconut oil in a large sauté pan over medium heat. Swirl the pan to coat. Add the onion and cook, stirring frequently, until onion is translucent, about 5 minutes. Make a well in the center of the pan and add the cumin. Cook, stirring constantly until the cumin is fragrant, about 30 seconds. Stir cumin into the onions. Add the ground beef and salt. Cook, breaking up the beef with the back of a wooden spoon until beef is no longer pink.\n3. Preheat oven to 400ºF and adjust the rack to the middle position. Pour half the sauce in the bottom of an 11 x 7-inch baking dish and spread it out evenly. Place a crepe on the counter and top with 1/4 cup of the beef filling. Carefully roll the crepe around the beef and place it in the baking dish. Repeat with the remaining beef and crepes. Pour the remaining sauce on top of the enchiladas and sprinkle with the cheese. Bake for 25 minutes, or until golden brown and bubbly on top. Cool for 10 minutes. Serve.\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target "smartCard-inline")'),
	(573, '65ecf156ac509dcad1fe0753', '2024-03-09 17:35:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 4-lb whole chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil, melted\n- dash of salt\n- dash black pepper\n- 1/2 cup chicken broth\n\nInstructions\n\n1. Rinse the chicken and pat it dry. Place in baking pan. Drizzle with oil. Sprinkle on salt and pepper.\n2. Add the stock.\n3. Turn oven to 275 degrees and roast the chicken, covered, for about 3 hours.\n4. Increase to 375 degrees roasting for 30-45 minutes/\n5. Remove from the over allowing to rest 5-10 minutes before carving and serving.'),
	(574, '65ee0b619b77b54774c54f49', '2025-04-30 19:10:48', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 8 ounces baby spinach leaves (fresh or frozen)\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- Black pepper to taste\n- 1 package of mushrooms, sliced (optional)\n- 1/4 cup chopped walnuts, toasted (optional) [toast on a pan over medium heat for 4-5 minutes until golden brown]\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. Heat oil over medium heat in a large pot. Remove the seeds from the squash, scoop the flesh out and place in the pot. Add spinach leaves, cream and goat cheese. Toss well until goat cheese has melted and the mixture is hot.\n3. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with walnuts, if using.'),
	(575, '66b7c63aef984308441f4e1c', '2025-04-28 17:29:26', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 cans of salmon makes 14 patties\n- 3 eggs\n- about 2.5 cups of almond flour\n- Coconut oil for pan\n\nDirections\n\n1. Add salmon and eggs to a bowl and mix.\n2. Make 14 patties at 70 grams each\n3. Something here with the flour\n4. ‌\n5. Stove at 4.5'),
	(576, '67f6e86693b75b1c157d8e81', '2025-05-27 17:22:58', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel or 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 20–25 min. Add more liquid if needed. Serve as-is or over rice. Top with cheddar if desired.'),
	(577, '65ee10511a7846ac72bd44c3', '2024-03-10 15:10:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 spaghetti squash\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 6-8oz turkey bacon, sliced or chopped\n- 1 cup onion, diced\n- 1/2 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- Shredded cheddar cheese\n- Optional garnishes: shredded lettuce, tomato, nutritional yeast, black olives\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees. Slice squash lengthwise. Remove the seeds and guts and lay cut side down in a dish with water to cover sides up 1 inch. Roast for 43 minutes if put in right when preheat starts not after; until the squash is tender and pulls away intro strands easily.\n2. While the squash cooks, heat a large skillet on medium high.\n3. Cut 6-8 oz of sliced bacon in to cubes. Dice the onions. Mix together dry spices in a small dish.\n4. Melt the coconut oil in the preheated skillet. Add the bacon. Cook for 3-5 minutes.\n5. Add onions and saute with the bacon for 2-3 minutes or until the onions have softened slightly.\n6. Noe the ground beef gets added to the bacon and onion. Mix it well, sprinkle in the spices. Cook until ground beef is done.\n7. Harvest the squash and combine it with the meats. Stir all together.\n8. Top with cheese. Bake for 15 minutes and 375 degrees.\n9. Remove from oven and top with any optional ingredients.'),
	(578, '65ee228db885a5033c35e542', '2024-03-10 17:02:20', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 3/4 cup onion, diced\n- 1-2 marina sauce jars\n- coconut oil\n- 1 medium spaghetti squash\n- 2 medium zucchini\n- 8 oz grated cheddar cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon nutmeg\n- salt and pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees to cook squash for 43 minutes putting it in at start of preheat. To prep squash, cut lengthwise and remove string and seeds. Place face down in baking dish with water 1-inch up to the sides.\n2. Brown the ground beef and onions.\n3. Slice zucchini lengthwise into 1/8 inch slices.\n4. Once the spaghetti squash is cooked, shred the inside of the squash with a fork into a strainer. Gently press down on the squash to drain out some of the liquid.\n5. Mix the spaghetti squash with 2/3 of the grated cheese, nutmeg, salt and pepper. Set aside.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, build your lasagne. Zucchini slices on the bottom, spread half of the spaghetti squash mixture, spread half the meat mixture, finish with half of the tomato sauce. Repeat. Finish by adding the remaining zucchini slices (if you have any). Add the remaining cheese.\n7. Bake for 25-30 minutes.'),
	(579, '65ee2de69fd5eb92ee41ba40', '2024-03-10 17:15:42', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 28 oz jar spaghetti sauce\n- 3 medium zucchini or 1 eggplant, sliced 1/8 inch thick\n- sea salt\n- Cashew Ricotta Cheese (see that recipe card)\n- 16 oz shredded mozzarella cheese\n- 1/4 cup PR cheese\n- 1 large egg\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a medium skillet, brown meat. Drain. Add the marina sauce to the meat. Simmer on low while prepping the next steps.\n2. Slice the zucchini or eggplant into slices. Lightly salt the slices and set aside for 10 minutes. Salting it helps to take out the moisture. After 10 minutes, blot excess moisture with a paper towel.\n3. On a skillet, grill zucchini on each side until cooked, about 1-2 minutes per side. Place on a paper towel to soak any additional moisture.\n4. Preheat oven to 350 degrees.\n5. In medium bowl, mix the cashew ricotta, pr cheese and egg. Stir well.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, spread some sauce on the bottom. Layer the zucchini. Then ricotta mixture. Top with mozzarella. Repeat the process until all ingredients are used up. Top with sauce and mozzarella.\n7. Cover with foil and bake for 30 minutes.'),
	(580, '65ee2b079d6349ae5cd0a4ae', '2024-03-10 17:41:45', 'Note: For the veggies-can look for a frozen veggie blend to make this easier.\n\nIngredients (these ingredients are all doubled as this freezes well)\n\n- 8 tablespoon butter\n- 4 leeks, roughly chopped\n- 4 carrots, roughly chopped\n- 2 celery stalk, roughly chopped\n- 5 russet potatoes, diced\n- 6 zucchini, cut into 1 inch pieces\n- 8-10 cups chicken stock\n- 2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in the jumbo pot. Add leeks, carrots, celery. Low-medium heat, cover, cook for 20 minutes.\n2. Add potatoes and stock and thyme. Bring to a boil. Simmer for 10 minutes.\n3. Add zucchini. Simmer 15 more minutes. Until zucchini and potatoes are fork tender.\n4. Add salt and pepper.\n5. Using a hand immersion blender, puree the soup. Be careful not to fill the pot too high or this will be very messy.\n6. Season to taste with salt and pepper.'),
	(581, '65ee33402e06e43ef6df6ab4', '2024-03-10 17:40:35', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon butter\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoon dried italian seasoning\n- 6 cups chicken stock\n- 1 pound chicken thighs\n- 14 ounces diced tomatoes\n- 10 ounces frozen spinach leaves\n- Sea salt\n- PR cheese for sprinkling on top\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in a large pot over medium heat. Add garlic and italian seasoning. Pour in stock. Bring to a boil.\n2. Add chicken cooking for 12-15 minutes, until chicken is cooked through. Using a pair of tongs, remove the chicken placing on a cutting board.\n3. Add tomatoes and spinach to the soup and cook for 5-10 minutes.\n4. Chop chicken into bite-sized pieces. Season with sea salt.\n5. Ladle into bowls and garnish with PR cheese.'),
	(582, '65ee372e7bb627c87df43ca2', '2024-03-10 17:46:25', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 3 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 4 cups white beans\n- 4 cups kidney beans\n- 4 cups pinto beans\n- 4 cups chicken broth\n- cheddar cheese\n- salt and pepper to taste\n- Cayenne pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a large pot, add beans and broth and spices. Boil. Simmer, covered, 10 minutes.\n2. Blend with immersion blender.\n3. Serve with cheese on top.'),
	(583, '66804801d104693530f1c13c', '2024-06-29 12:44:39', 'Don\'t put nuggets in until preheat is done \nPlace parchment paper or equivalent in oven\nPreheat 425\nLay 4-6 nuggets in oven \nSet time for 16 minutes\nFlip nuggets over\nSet timer for another 6-7 minutes (check periodically for preferred brownness)\n\nIf you want veggie, we have mixed veggies, green beans, and broccoli. 1/2 to 1 C covered with water. Bring to boil, reduce heat to light boil for 3-4 minutes (broccoli may need an additional min or two)'),
	(584, '67e09ccb91874e7d03e8bac7', '2025-03-23 18:47:00', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1tsp Black pepper\n- 1/4 cup sunflower seeds, toasted (optional)\n- 1 Cup pasta per serving \n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with sunflower seeds, if using.\n3. Each serving can be done with a cup of penne pasta.'),
	(585, '67f6c4722785635c12d6bfef', '2025-04-09 14:03:49', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp chili powder\n- Salt + pepper to taste\n- Corn or flour tortillas\n  **Optional toppings:** diced tomato, avocado, cheese\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Heat a skillet, toss in black beans + spices, stir until warm and a little thickened.\n2. Warm tortillas.\n3. Spoon beans onto tortillas and pile on your toppings.'),
	(586, '67f6d1a82f24c4e9aa7fd634', '2025-04-09 15:00:02', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained)\n- 1 cup rice (white or brown)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes (with juice)\n- 1 bell pepper, chopped\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp cumin + 1/2 tsp smoked paprika (optional: chili powder, garlic)\n- Salt & pepper\n- Optional toppings: cheese, avocado, green onion, hot sauce\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion + pepper in a bit of oil until soft.\n2. Add spices, stir for a minute.\n3. Add rice, beans, tomatoes, and broth.\n4. Bring to a boil, then reduce to low, cover, and simmer until rice is cooked (about 20 min for white, 35-40 for brown).\n5. Fluff and top as you like!'),
	(587, '67f6d1f2c9c94bac53e7a203', '2025-04-09 15:01:07', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 large sweet potato, cubed\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie broth\n- 1 tsp cumin, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, 1/4 tsp cinnamon (optional but amazing)\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion until soft.\n2. Add sweet potato, beans, tomatoes, broth, and spices.\n3. Simmer until sweet potato is fork-tender (20–25 min).\n4. Taste, season, and top with avocado or a swirl of yogurt.'),
	(588, '67f6d2beff0244014051ceb1', '2025-04-09 15:04:22', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup rice\n- 1 can coconut milk (full-fat or light)\n- 1 cup water or broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp ginger powder\n- Salt to taste\n- Optional: lime, cilantro, chili flakes\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Dump it all in a pot.\n2. Bring to boil, then simmer covered 18–20 min until rice is done.\n3. Stir, taste, and finish with lime juice or chili flakes if you want a little kick.'),
	(589, '67f6d7a90dfe222116694fa7', '2025-04-09 15:25:31', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Weeknight protein bomb\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt, pepper\n- Optional: cooked rice or GF pasta to serve over\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add tomato sauce + black beans, simmer 5–10 min. Serve over rice or pasta. Add cheese if you want.'),
	(590, '67f6d7e733d4ebefa32d1be1', '2025-04-09 15:26:19', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Creamy + slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Optional: chili flakes, chopped spinach\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything 15 minutes. Blend half (optional) for a creamier texture. Garnish with a swirl of coconut milk or cheese.'),
	(591, '67f6d814dd2e1cc72fa318bd', '2025-04-09 15:27:11', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk **or** 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic & onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese for top\n\n**How-to:**\nMix cooked pasta, beans, sauce of choice, and seasonings. Pour into dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(592, '67f6d83b8b90154cd16b9174', '2025-04-09 15:27:46', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Meaty vegan stew\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded with hands or fork)\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 tsp each: garlic powder, onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add tomatoes + black beans. Simmer 20–30 min until thick. Great with rice or GF cornbread.'),
	(593, '67f6d86e51c3735b50f5af4e', '2025-04-09 15:28:38', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cheesy & hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Cooked GF pasta or rice\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Mix with beans, sauce, and pasta or rice. Spread in baking dish, top with cheese, bake 15–20 min.'),
	(594, '67f6d3181ecadb49da60fcbf', '2025-04-09 15:26:27', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained)\n- 3 cloves garlic, minced (or 1 tsp garlic powder)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Olive oil\n- Salt, pepper, pinch of chili flakes\n- Optional: handful of chopped kale or spinach, squeeze of lemon\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté garlic in olive oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, broth, herbs, and seasonings.\n3. Simmer 15–20 minutes until thickened and cozy.\n4. Add greens at the end if using, and finish with lemon juice for brightness.'),
	(595, '67f6d365cbfc9cd17164d86a', '2025-04-09 15:26:25', 'Creamy without cream, and full of flavor.\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb pasta (short shapes like orecchiette, penne, or shells)\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 3 cloves garlic (minced or sliced)\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 tsp rosemary or thyme (dried or fresh)\n- 1/2 cup veggie or chicken broth (or pasta water)\n- Salt, pepper, chili flakes to taste\n- Optional: squeeze of lemon, grated Parmesan, or a handful of spinach\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Cook pasta in salted water until al dente. Save about 1/2 cup pasta water.\n2. While pasta cooks, heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat.\n3. Add garlic and herbs. Sauté until garlic is fragrant.\n4. Add cannellini beans and broth (or pasta water). Simmer 5–7 min until beans start to break down a bit and sauce thickens.\n5. Stir in cooked pasta. Toss to coat and warm through.\n6. Add lemon juice or Parmesan if using, and adjust seasoning.'),
	(596, '67f6d89c820310bb4d5b7dfe', '2025-04-09 15:29:30', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Cozy, Italian-inspired\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cooked chopped spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend one can of beans with broth + coconut milk. Simmer with second can and seasonings for 15–20 minutes. Add greens last if using.'),
	(597, '67f6d8d2bf3d8478b9410442', '2025-04-09 15:30:17', '**Type:** Casserole/Bake\n**Vibe:** Dairy-free Alfredo-ish\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: smoked paprika or Italian herbs\n- Optional: shredded cheddar on top\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans, coconut milk, and seasonings. Mix with pasta, pour into baking dish, top with cheese (if using), bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(598, '67f6d8ed0ba832c5d59c9c5b', '2025-04-28 21:45:22', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-rich and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, stir in beans + sauce, simmer 10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(599, '67f6d9453c6e3f0e54ecc6a9', '2025-04-09 15:32:18', '**Type:** One-pot (or two-pot)\n**Vibe:** Rustic & herby\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 can diced tomatoes\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- White rice (served with or cooked into the beans)\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer beans, tomatoes, seasonings together 15 min. Serve over cooked rice or cook rice directly in with extra liquid.'),
	(600, '67f6d9860b7fd3757b014d4a', '2025-04-09 15:33:21', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild & creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp turmeric\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: serve over rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients together for 15–20 min. Serve over rice or scoop with flatbread if you’ve got it.'),
	(601, '67f6d9aa58884dc595fe1691', '2025-04-27 21:29:03', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty & homey\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1–2 chicken breasts (cooked & chopped or shredded)\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Mashed potatoes (can be made with butter + coconut milk)\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, broth, and seasoning in a casserole dish. Top with mashed potatoes. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(602, '67f6db51765d2af8a6120b7d', '2025-04-09 15:41:00', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Rich, soft, almost risotto-like\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 2 cups broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté seasonings in olive oil, add rice and liquid, bring to boil. Add beans halfway through. Simmer covered 18–20 min. Stir at the end—it’ll get creamy!'),
	(603, '67f6db7c34cc1b5aba24924f', '2025-04-09 15:41:37', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Smooth and simple\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Thyme or rosemary\n- Optional: a handful of spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Blend half or all for a smooth texture.'),
	(604, '67f6db98db7791bf47f312e3', '2025-04-09 15:42:03', '**Type:** One-skillet meal\n**Vibe:** Hearty and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Onion powder, garlic powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Stir in beans and tomato sauce. Simmer for 5–10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(605, '67f6dbb11897fad863756c6b', '2025-04-09 15:42:29', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Mild and creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings. Toss with pasta, put in baking dish, top with cheese. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(606, '67f6dbca7dc8d6736fe0c669', '2025-04-09 15:42:55', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Creamy and lightly spiced\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Cumin, turmeric, chili powder (optional)\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning to taste. Serve hot.'),
	(607, '67f6dbf15835da0a7474d6a8', '2025-04-09 15:43:32', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cozy classic with a twist\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (cubed)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme\n- Optional: GF biscuit topping or mashed potatoes\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, sauce in baking dish. Top with biscuits or mash. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 min.'),
	(608, '67f6dc0b38817fdb9a7f5ccc', '2025-04-13 13:28:47', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty & meaty without meat\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/4 cup water\n- 1 tsp salt\n- 1 tsp Garlic\n- 1 tsp onion powder\n- 1tsp paprika\n- 1 tsp oregano\n- Optional: coconut milk splash at the end\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans & tomatoes, simmer 20–30 min. Great on its own or over pasta or rice.'),
	(609, '67f6e574478306dc9e9ca55c', '2025-04-09 16:24:13', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Optional: peas or frozen mixed veggies\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together 20 minutes until creamy. Add frozen veggies near the end. Serve hot over rice.'),
	(610, '67f6e5a37594122dcbc2377e', '2025-04-09 16:25:42', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-packed, saucy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n- Optional: frozen corn or peas\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with seasonings, stir in chickpeas, Ro-Tel, and veggies. Simmer for 10 minutes.'),
	(611, '67f6e6027c1618ec53193a84', '2025-04-09 16:27:00', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Creamy & veggie-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli + carrots (from a veggie mix)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano or thyme\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20–25 minutes. Adjust thickness with more broth or milk. Serve with a spoon and a blanket.'),
	(612, '67f6e6456e211ca1e4aa1d01', '2025-04-09 16:27:53', '**Type:** Creamy pasta\n**Vibe:** White sauce–style, dairy-free\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend chickpeas, coconut milk, and seasonings. Heat in a saucepan, stir in pasta. Top with cheese if desired. Creamy, cozy, and satisfying'),
	(613, '67f6e6733fb047dae933107e', '2025-04-09 16:28:40', '**Type:** Chili-style\n**Vibe:** Simple and spicy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn or mixed veg\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: top with cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20 minutes. Add cheese at the end if using. Serve in a bowl or over rice.'),
	(614, '67f6e6b89008710652e5ceae', '2025-04-09 16:29:49', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty, like a gratin\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 2 cups cooked diced potatoes\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Top with cheese (if using) and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes.'),
	(615, '67f6e6e42de01a2f2a95d602', '2025-04-09 16:30:25', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Warm, earthy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth with seasonings. Add chickpeas and veggies halfway through. Stir occasionally. Done in ~20 min.'),
	(616, '67f6e742e6f1c9d1c849f7d0', '2025-04-09 16:31:57', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Silky, earthy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Blend part of the beans for a creamy texture or leave chunky. Top with cheddar if you like.'),
	(617, '67f6e7823bceb1b3d8bcc968', '2025-04-09 16:33:03', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty and slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with seasonings. Add beans, tomato sauce, and veggies. Simmer until heated through. Serve solo or over rice.'),
	(618, '67f6e7a7c0bdb6909c3d367d', '2025-04-09 16:33:38', '**Type:** Pasta\n**Vibe:** Mild, creamy, and dreamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Optional: grated cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings until smooth. Heat gently, toss with pasta, and top with cheese if using.'),
	(619, '67f6e7c1f4b788ab03a88cf1', '2025-04-09 16:34:04', '**Type:** Oven-bake\n**Vibe:** Roasty and nourishing\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1.5 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 1/4 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary, salt\n- Optional: cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Bake at 375°F for 25–30 minutes until golden. Top with cheese if desired.'),
	(620, '67f6e7dc4583dbdd2be5be67', '2025-04-09 16:34:32', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild curry, plant-powered\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth or Ro-Tel\n- Cumin, garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans, liquid, and simmer 20 min. Serve with rice or as a stew.'),
	(621, '67f6e803175f15f0baeac4bf', '2025-04-09 16:35:02', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Rustic, creamy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- 1/4–1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheese for topping\n\n**How-to:**\nMix everything, transfer to a baking dish, top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes.'),
	(622, '67f6e81c3a17c51bd6839c7f', '2025-04-09 16:35:28', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen peas or green beans\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning and serve with a spoon and a smile.'),
	(623, '67f6e8831688ad96ae92de1b', '2025-06-02 17:33:29', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory & protein-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 3/4 teaspoon Garlic powder\n- 3/4 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/2 teaspoon tumeric\n- 1/4 teaspoon salt\n- Optional: frozen peas or carrots\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add beans and coconut milk, simmer 15–20 minutes. Serve over rice.'),
	(624, '67f6e8a24e9fd13663bf250d', '2025-04-09 16:37:46', '**Type:** Brothy soup\n**Vibe:** Lighter but filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2–1 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 20 minutes. Optional: blend a portion for a thicker texture.'),
	(625, '67f6e8c26dddd811aa4785a0', '2025-04-09 16:38:19', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy & cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nStir all ingredients together in a baking dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(626, '67f6fe57c9b34bebc5416b69', '2025-04-09 18:10:44', '**Type:** Stir-fry\n**Vibe:** Quick and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded jackfruit with spices, add beans and Ro-Tel. Stir-fry until warmed through. Serve over rice'),
	(627, '67f6fade968000a006f6d470', '2025-04-09 17:55:38', '**Type:** One-pot rice dish\n**Vibe:** Quick & flavorful\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen corn or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nCook everything together in a pot. Simmer 15–20 minutes until rice is done and beans are tender.'),
	(628, '67f6fb0e0c712bac84d6e895', '2025-04-09 17:56:26', '**Type:** One-skillet creamy meal\n**Vibe:** Unexpectedly delicious\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme or curry powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté broccoli briefly, then add kidney beans and coconut milk with seasonings. Simmer until everything is tender and creamy.'),
	(629, '67f6fb2d2e2d1f757637bfa8', '2025-04-09 17:56:57', '**Type:** Skillet hash\n**Vibe:** Sweet, savory, and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1–2 cups cubed sweet potatoes (frozen or pre-cooked)\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n- Optional: ground chicken or beef\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté sweet potatoes until browned and soft. Add beans (and meat, if using), season, and cook until warmed through.'),
	(630, '67f6fb610f93ed8503be7f75', '2025-04-09 17:57:50', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Rich, cozy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 lb ground beef (or ground chicken)\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground meat, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes, adding veggies if you like.'),
	(631, '67f6fc015ab7e5dd2c1d4a16', '2025-04-09 18:00:41', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Spicy and robust\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine everything in a pot and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a side of rice or top with cheese.'),
	(632, '67f6fc2720d00eb77da6f821', '2025-04-09 18:01:07', '**Type:** One-pot chili\n**Vibe:** Hearty, plant-based\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with seasonings, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 30 minutes. Serve with rice or cornbread if desired.'),
	(633, '67f6fc43a4ddded4136e8275', '2025-04-09 18:05:30', '**Type:** One-pan rice dish\n**Vibe:** Flavor-packed, filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth, then add beans and veggies halfway through. Simmer until rice is cooked and beans are tender.'),
	(634, '67f6fd48e0026eacba4fd400', '2025-04-09 18:05:55', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Hearty and cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and tomato sauce in a baking dish. Top with cheese and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(635, '67f6fd69a70a93ba954db476', '2025-04-09 18:06:30', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory and satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, then add beans and coconut milk. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(636, '67f6fd876ff8e5425018be54', '2025-04-09 18:06:58', '**Type:** One-pan curry\n**Vibe:** Creamy and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Ground chicken\n- Garlic/onion powder, curry powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground chicken with spices, then add beans and liquids. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve with rice.'),
	(637, '67f6fda74d30ab49c784ad5b', '2025-05-07 17:27:58', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Bold and hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 teaspoon Chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes. Serve over corn mash (aka polenta), or top with cheese if desired.'),
	(638, '67f6fded3a189d2d126507a9', '2025-04-09 18:08:43', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Simple, savory, and smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 chicken breasts, cooked and shredded\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded chicken with seasonings, then add beans and Ro-Tel. Simmer with coconut milk for 15 minutes until everything is warm and combined.'),
	(639, '67f6fe0eeb47261f077fc5bc', '2025-04-09 18:09:15', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Hearty and veggie-packed\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine all ingredients and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a slice of gluten-free bread or over rice if desired.'),
	(640, '67f6fe2faf8069db3ed70ff9', '2025-04-09 18:09:47', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy, cheesy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and Ro-Tel in a baking dish. Top with cheese if desired. Bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(641, '67f6fe8de3ffa0131aebcc34', '2025-04-09 18:11:28', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Simple and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nMix rice, beans, Ro-Tel, and coconut milk. Pour into a baking dish and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until rice is cooked and bubbly.'),
	(642, '67f6feb7dc439bf5eff6cd44', '2025-04-09 18:12:06', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Smoky and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, smoked paprika, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup broth\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground beef with spices, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 20–25 minutes until everything is cooked through.'),
	(643, '68005051861ebf2dfc1c351e', '2025-04-16 19:51:52', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp coconut oil\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel (or canned tomatoes + green chiles)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt to taste\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- Optional: frozen corn or mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Heat oil in skillet, add seasonings and Ro-Tel, cook 2–3 min.\n2. Add beans and frozen veggies (if using), cook until heated.\n3. Stir in cooked rice and simmer 5–10 minutes.'),
	(644, '680050b91ed28e261cc3dbb2', '2025-04-16 19:52:59', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 chicken breast (cubed)\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp paprika\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1–1.5 cups water or broth\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown chicken in oil. Add seasonings.\n2. Stir in tomatoes, beans, water/broth, and veggies.\n3. Simmer covered for 15–20 min.'),
	(645, '680050f9448a7574075a59ea', '2025-04-16 19:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit, drained & shredded\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/4 tsp oregano\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook jackfruit in a pan to brown slightly.\n2. Add seasonings, Ro-Tel, and pinto beans.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min, mash slightly if desired.'),
	(646, '6800511b1f2c891143a064db', '2025-04-16 19:54:00', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 2 cups water or broth\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté seasonings in oil for 1 min.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, veggies, and broth.\n3. Simmer 20–30 minutes until veggies are tender.'),
	(647, '68005183a8bc2730a5655f53', '2025-04-16 19:55:53', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp oregano\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: nutritional yeast or mild cheddar (if tolerated)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Blend or mash beans for smoother texture (optional).\n2. Heat oil and seasonings, then add beans and tomato sauce.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min. Serve over gluten-free pasta.'),
	(648, '680051a5d487414bc769ea25', '2025-04-16 19:56:21', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 tsp curry powder\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1 cup frozen veggies\n- 1 cup cooked rice or serve over it\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook spices in oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, and veggies. Simmer 10–15 min.\n3. Serve over rice or stir in to make a one-pot dish.'),
	(649, '6824bb4a783db57b9ed8e3ca', '2025-05-14 10:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 jar marinara sauce\n- Canned green beans or sweet peas\n- Italian seasoning\n- garlic powder\n- onion powder\n- salt\n- pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook the ground chicken in a pot until browned.\n2. Add marinara sauce and a bit of water to loosen.\n3. Stir in drained beans (all 3 types) and canned green beans or peas.\n4. Season well with Italian herbs and simmer until flavors blend.\n5. Serve hot either as a stew or scoop into warmed almond flour tortillas for wraps.\n6. Divide into three meals.'),
	(650, '6824babde9b3732c346f3c9d', '2025-05-14 10:53:17', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Tortillas chips\n- Chili Powder\n- Cumin\n- Garlic Powder\n- Onion Powder\n- Paprika\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown the ground beef in a skillet, drain excess fat.\n2. Add frozen mixed vegetables and cook until softened.\n3. Stir in drained black beans and season with chili powder, cumin, etc.\n4. Add a little tomato sauce or water to bind the mix.\n5. Layer over tortilla chips or crush chips on top for a crunchy topping.\n6. Portion out into three meals. Optionally serve with salsa or cheese (if available).\n   '),
	(651, '680051ccffdc026a527075ab', '2025-04-16 19:56:58', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can kidney beans (optional combo)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook all ingredients in a pot over medium heat.\n2. Simmer uncovered for 20–30 min to thicken.\n3. Serve as-is or over rice'),
	(652, '6824bbd5acc27f4664c20175', '2025-05-14 10:52:57', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef (or skip for a vegetarian version)\n- 1 can chickpeas or kidney beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Almond flour tortillas\n- Paprika\n- Cumin\n- Garlic powder\n- Salt\n- black pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté the ground beef (if using) until browned.\n2. Drain excess fat.\n3. Add frozen mixed vegetables and sauté until tender.\n4. Stir in drained beans (chickpeas or kidney beans).\n5. Season well with spices using paprika, cumin, garlic powder, and pepper.\n6. Cook until everything is heated through and slightly crispy.\n7. Spoon into almond flour tortillas and wrap. Serve warm or grilled slightly for a toasted wrap.'),
	(653, '65e35de41116a7a22e54b319', '2025-05-14 10:01:12', '**Ingredients for 3 medium crusts:**\n\n3 cups almond flour\n\n1 1/2 cups arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons baking powder\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons salt\n\n2 1/4 teaspoon oregano\n\n3/8 teaspoon black pepper\n\n4 eggs\n\n3/4 cups milk\n\n**Directions:**\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 425 degrees.\n2. Line a round pizza pan or cookie sheet with parchment paper. (I have 4 pizza pans so I can bake all three at once)\n3. Combine the dry ingredients in a large bowl. Whisk to blend together.\n4. Add eggs and milk to the dry ingredients. Mix well. The batter will be runny—not like typical pizza dough.\n5. Use a spatula to spread the batter evenly onto the pan in a circle shape.\n6. Bake the crust in the preheated oven for 8-12 minutes.\n7. Remove crust from oven and top with sauce and desired toppings. Or freeze the crust for later. Once cooled, place parchment paper between the crusts and they will store perfectly in a ziplock gallon freezer bag until ready to use. I also make sure the size of my circle stays within the range of a gallon bag for this reason.\n8. Bake for another 10-15 minutes with toppings.\n\n‌\n\n**Other Option: Ingredients for 1 large crust:**\n\n2 cups almond flour\n\n1 cup arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. baking powder\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. salt\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon oregano\n\n1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n\n3 eggs\n\n1/2 cup milk\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/](https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(654, '65e39452587a1979909f4a74', '2025-04-27 21:29:12', '**Serving: 24** **meatballs**\n\n### Ingredients\n\n- 2 pound ground beef\n- 2 large egg\n- 1 onion, minced or onion powder\n- 2 tablespoons tomato paste (can omit)\n- 4 tablespoons dijon mustard\n- 2 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 teaspoon celtic sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon baking soda\n\n### Instructions\n\n- In a large bowl, combine ground beef, egg, and onion\n- Mix in tomato paste, mustard, coconut flour, salt, pepper, and baking soda\n- Use a ¼ cup scoop to form meatballs (about 57 grams each)\n- Place meatballs on a parchment paper lined baking sheet\n- Bake at 350°F for 20-25 minutes, or until instant read thermometer reads 175°F\n- Serve with marinara sauce over spaghetti squash noodles or zucchini noodles\n\nSource: [https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/](https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(655, '65ea48c89c856f6ad662250b', '2025-04-27 21:24:32', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 1 to 1.5 cups kidney beans, cooked or canned\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoons cumin powder\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- Corn chips to serve this all on top of\n- Optional toppings: tomatoes, cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder \n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add spices.\n3. Add kidney beans.\n4. Serve meat and bean mixter over corn chips. Top with desired toppings.'),
	(656, '65e397521ddf77bca5c237fb', '2024-11-04 18:40:08', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder OR 1/2 tspn Chipotle seasoning (reduce to half tablespoon)\n- 1 pound ground beef or **1 can of jackfruit**\n- 28 ounces diced tomatoes (or 1 jar diced and 1 jar crushed)\n- 2 boxes of kidney beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper (reduce to 3/4 teaspoon)\n- Toppings: avocado, sour cream, grated cheddar cheese\n- Optional: Mix in 1-2 Seasoned Rice packets from Costco\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 15-20 minutes.\n5. Adjust seasoning with salt and pepper as needed.'),
	(657, '65e3a05c8c1b5970dcacc97d', '2024-03-11 17:58:55', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1 can of diced tomatoes\n- 2 boxes of pinto beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper\n- Corn tortillas (16 qty)\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 10 minutes.\n5. Fill tortillas, rolled up and into rectangular dish.\n6. Top with cheese.\n7. Bake at 350 degrees for 20 minutes.'),
	(658, '65e3a1e92948d057fe6ebd6d', '2025-04-27 21:21:14', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef, cooked and drained\n- 1 1/2 cups thinly slice potatoes, cooked and drained\n- 1 can coconut milk (entire can)\n- 1 cup milk (replace with water if we don’t have milk)\n- If needed, 1/2 cup water\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2-4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon sugar\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- If needed for thickening, 1 tablespoon tapioca. Mixed with a small amount of cold water before adding.\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook beef separately.\n2. Cook potatoes separately.\n3. To the cooked beef, add the milk and water and all the seasonings.\n4. If needed, add the tapioca thickener at this stage.\n5. Add the cooked sliced potatoes.'),
	(659, '65e3a89d761eefa02d605b06', '2025-05-10 18:41:34', 'Ingredients\n\n- Cubed chicken, cooked separately\n- Pasta, cooked separately\n- Broccoli florets, cooked separately\n- Cream sauce, cooked separately\n  - 1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n  - 1 teaspoon salt\n  - 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n  - 1/2 teaspoon sugar\n  - 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n  - 1 can of coconut milk-ONLY the thick part, drain the water\n  - 3-4 teaspoons of tapioca powder added to a very little splash of milk or cold water\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook the chicken, pasta and broccoli all separately.\n2. Mix the cream sauce ingredients together and bring to a slow boil.\n3. Combine all the ingredients together.'),
	(660, '65e3abc0f8cd991e2ff05bff', '2024-05-03 19:05:41', 'Ingredients:\n\n2 pounds ground beef\n4 teaspoons paprika\n3 teaspoons black pepper\n2 1/2 teaspoons salt\n2 2/3 teaspoon Maple Sugar or Sucanat Sugar\n1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper\n\nOptional: Lettuce, mayo, cheese, rotel\n\nDirections:\n\n1. Mix all spices together.\n2. Mix spices by hand tenderly into the meat so it doesn’t get too tough.\n3. Form 12 patties, flat like tortillas but also loosely packed so doesn’t dry out. (about 80 grams per patty)\n4. Preheat the pan on mid heat. Browning both sides of the patties but not cooking all the way through. Those become leftovers to freeze and cooked thoroughly as reheated for future meals.\n5. Thoroughly cook the remaining two patties for dinner that night.\n6. Make your burger with whatever toppings you prefer.'),
	(661, '65e3af887349307288afe8a6', '2025-04-27 21:20:59', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 6 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 3/4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 1 pound ground beef or turkey or jackfruit\n\n\nMashed potato ingredients:\n- 3 pounds potatoes, rinsed and cubed\n- 4 tablespoons butter\n- 1 cup milk\n- 1 1/2 cup grated Pecorino Romano cheese\n- 3/4 tablespoon sea salt\n- ground back pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat.\n2. Stir in the salt, pepper and thyme.\n3. Add the veggies and heat until cooked properly.\n4. In another pot, brown the ground meat.\n5. In a third pot, make the mashed potatoes. Add in the butter, milk cheese and salt and pepper after drained and mashed.\n6. Layer all the ingredients into a large dish. Veggies and meat stirred together. Mashed potatoes layered on top.'),
	(662, '67fc058a3968a44cf95a9b8c', '2025-04-27 21:21:31', 'Makes 6 burritos. Can prep insides ahead of time.\n\n- 2 sweet potatoes, peeled and cubed small (about 3-4 cups)\n- 1 red pepper, diced small\n- Coconut oil\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon chili powder\n- ½ teaspoon salt\n- ¼ teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 (15-ounce) can black beans, rinsed and drained\n- 1 cup shredded cheddar cheese\n- 12 tortillas as will likely need to double them up\n\nInstructions\n\n- Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. In a large bowl, toss together the sweet potatoes and red pepper with the oil, cumin, onion powder, chili powder, salt and pepper. Dump the coated veggies onto a large rimmed baking sheet and roast for 18-20 minutes, tossing halfway through. The vegetables should be tender but not mushy at the end of cooking time.\n- Let the vegetable mixture cool. Scrape the mixture into a large bowl and toss with the black beans. Taste the mixture and add additional salt and pepper to taste, if needed. Refrigerate the mixture until ready to assemble the burritos or use immediately.\n- Place 4 tortillas on a microwave-safe plate and cover with a damp paper towel. Microwave for 15-20 seconds until the tortillas are pliable. (Warm up 1/2 cupish of the mixture if premade) Place 1/4 cup or so of the mixture in the center of the tortilla and top with a sprinkle with shredded cheese. Fold in the sides of the tortilla and roll up. Place seam-side down on a baking sheet. Repeat with the remaining tortillas until you have all the burritos you need .\n- Bake in a 375 degree F oven for about 10-15 minutes, until heated through and the top of the tortilla is golden brown. Adjust the baking time as needed depending on if the filling has been refrigerated or not. For a softer tortilla, wrap each burrito in tin foil and heat through. Serve immediately.'),
	(663, '65ece37b52d21abd85f26e02', '2025-05-14 09:36:39', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 2 pound cubbed beef\n- 1/4 cup coconut flour\n- 2 teaspoon paprika\n- 4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 1 teaspoon oregano\n- 1 teaspoon basil\n- 1 teaspoon rosemary\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/4 teaspoon crushed red pepper\n- 1 head cauliflower, chopped\n- 4 large carrots, peeled and chopped\n- 2 bell peppers, chopped\n- 1 onion, chopped\n- 3 stalks of celery, chopped\n- 2 potatoes, chopped\n- 4 cups stock, chicken or beef\n- 1 jar whole tomatoes\n- 1 tablespoon arrowroot powder for thickening, if needed\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat oil in large pot over medium high heat.\n2. Combine coconut flour and spices in a large ziploc bag. And meat to the bag and shake until nicely coated.\n3. Add the seasoned meat to the skillet and brown for 3 minutes. Meat will continue to cook in sauce so browning meat is all you need to do.\n4. Add all vegetables and stir to combine.\n5. Cover and let veggies cook for a few minutes.\n6. Add stock and tomatoes. Stir and bring to a low boil.\n7. Lower heat and let simmer for 10-20. minutes.\n8. Add arrowroot powder to a small amount of cold water. Stir and then add to the stew, stirring to help thicken.'),
	(664, '65ece67dcbf220432b12ece8', '2024-03-09 17:02:16', 'Ingredients\n\n- 3 tablespoons butter\n- 1 large onion, chopped\n- 1 large red bell pepper, chopped\n- 2 medium poblano peppers, seeded and chopped\n- 1 jalapeno pepper, seeded and chopped\n- 2 cloves garlic, chopped\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 tablespoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 3/4 cups chicken stock\n- 1 1/2 cups crushed tomatoes\n- 4 ounces diced green chilies\n- 1 1/2 cup sour cream\n- 5 cups cooked, shredded chicken (substitute is jack fruit and white beans)\n- 4 cups cheddar cheese, grated\n- 16 corn tortillas\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees. Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and all peppers. Cook for about 8-10 minutes, until softened. Sitr in the garlic, chili powder, cumin, salt and cook for 1 minute.\n2. Sprinkle the coconut flour over the vegetable mixture and cook for 1 minute while stirring continuously. Stir in the stock and bring to a simmer for 4 minutes. Remove from the heat and stir in the tomatoes, chilies and sour cream.\n3. Place the chicken in a large bowl. Pour the vegetable mixture over the top and stir until combined.\n4. Place 8 tortillas on the bottom of a 13x9 dish. Top with half of the chicken mixture and then half of the cheese. Repeat with the remaining ingredients. Bake for 45-50 minutes until cheese is bubbly and the edges of the casserole are just turning golden brown.\n\n‌\n\nSource: Deliciouslyorganic.net'),
	(665, '65ecec7b734766a86f3ebd36', '2024-03-09 17:19:13', 'For the sauce:\n\n- 3 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 1/2 teaspoons coconut flour\n- 2 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon dried oregano\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 cups chicken stock\n- 12 ounces tomato paste\n- 1 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n\n#### For the Filling:\n\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 1 large yellow onion, chopped\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1/2 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n- 1 can of Pinto beans\n\n#### For the Wraps:\n\n- 1 recipe savory crepes, page 277 of [The Grain-Free Family Table ](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/the-grain-free-family-table/ "‌")or Siete grain-free tortillas (or corn tortillas)\n- 8 ounces raw cheddar, shredded\n\n### INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Place the coconut oil and coconut flour in a medium sauce pan over medium heat. Whisk constantly and cook until the coconut flour just turns golden brown, about 2 minutes. Add the chili powder, oregano and cumin and cook, stirring frequently until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Whisk in chicken stock, tomato paste and sea salt. Bring to a simmer over medium-low heat and cook until sauce begins to thicken, about 20 minutes.\n2. Place the coconut oil in a large sauté pan over medium heat. Swirl the pan to coat. Add the onion and cook, stirring frequently, until onion is translucent, about 5 minutes. Make a well in the center of the pan and add the cumin. Cook, stirring constantly until the cumin is fragrant, about 30 seconds. Stir cumin into the onions. Add the ground beef and salt. Cook, breaking up the beef with the back of a wooden spoon until beef is no longer pink.\n3. Preheat oven to 400ºF and adjust the rack to the middle position. Pour half the sauce in the bottom of an 11 x 7-inch baking dish and spread it out evenly. Place a crepe on the counter and top with 1/4 cup of the beef filling. Carefully roll the crepe around the beef and place it in the baking dish. Repeat with the remaining beef and crepes. Pour the remaining sauce on top of the enchiladas and sprinkle with the cheese. Bake for 25 minutes, or until golden brown and bubbly on top. Cool for 10 minutes. Serve.\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target "smartCard-inline")'),
	(666, '65ecf156ac509dcad1fe0753', '2024-03-09 17:35:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 4-lb whole chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil, melted\n- dash of salt\n- dash black pepper\n- 1/2 cup chicken broth\n\nInstructions\n\n1. Rinse the chicken and pat it dry. Place in baking pan. Drizzle with oil. Sprinkle on salt and pepper.\n2. Add the stock.\n3. Turn oven to 275 degrees and roast the chicken, covered, for about 3 hours.\n4. Increase to 375 degrees roasting for 30-45 minutes/\n5. Remove from the over allowing to rest 5-10 minutes before carving and serving.'),
	(667, '65ee0b619b77b54774c54f49', '2025-04-30 19:10:48', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 8 ounces baby spinach leaves (fresh or frozen)\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- Black pepper to taste\n- 1 package of mushrooms, sliced (optional)\n- 1/4 cup chopped walnuts, toasted (optional) [toast on a pan over medium heat for 4-5 minutes until golden brown]\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. Heat oil over medium heat in a large pot. Remove the seeds from the squash, scoop the flesh out and place in the pot. Add spinach leaves, cream and goat cheese. Toss well until goat cheese has melted and the mixture is hot.\n3. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with walnuts, if using.'),
	(668, '66b7c63aef984308441f4e1c', '2025-04-28 17:29:26', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 cans of salmon makes 14 patties\n- 3 eggs\n- about 2.5 cups of almond flour\n- Coconut oil for pan\n\nDirections\n\n1. Add salmon and eggs to a bowl and mix.\n2. Make 14 patties at 70 grams each\n3. Something here with the flour\n4. ‌\n5. Stove at 4.5'),
	(669, '67f6e86693b75b1c157d8e81', '2025-05-27 17:22:58', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel or 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 20–25 min. Add more liquid if needed. Serve as-is or over rice. Top with cheddar if desired.'),
	(670, '65ee10511a7846ac72bd44c3', '2024-03-10 15:10:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 spaghetti squash\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 6-8oz turkey bacon, sliced or chopped\n- 1 cup onion, diced\n- 1/2 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- Shredded cheddar cheese\n- Optional garnishes: shredded lettuce, tomato, nutritional yeast, black olives\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees. Slice squash lengthwise. Remove the seeds and guts and lay cut side down in a dish with water to cover sides up 1 inch. Roast for 43 minutes if put in right when preheat starts not after; until the squash is tender and pulls away intro strands easily.\n2. While the squash cooks, heat a large skillet on medium high.\n3. Cut 6-8 oz of sliced bacon in to cubes. Dice the onions. Mix together dry spices in a small dish.\n4. Melt the coconut oil in the preheated skillet. Add the bacon. Cook for 3-5 minutes.\n5. Add onions and saute with the bacon for 2-3 minutes or until the onions have softened slightly.\n6. Noe the ground beef gets added to the bacon and onion. Mix it well, sprinkle in the spices. Cook until ground beef is done.\n7. Harvest the squash and combine it with the meats. Stir all together.\n8. Top with cheese. Bake for 15 minutes and 375 degrees.\n9. Remove from oven and top with any optional ingredients.'),
	(671, '65ee228db885a5033c35e542', '2024-03-10 17:02:20', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 3/4 cup onion, diced\n- 1-2 marina sauce jars\n- coconut oil\n- 1 medium spaghetti squash\n- 2 medium zucchini\n- 8 oz grated cheddar cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon nutmeg\n- salt and pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees to cook squash for 43 minutes putting it in at start of preheat. To prep squash, cut lengthwise and remove string and seeds. Place face down in baking dish with water 1-inch up to the sides.\n2. Brown the ground beef and onions.\n3. Slice zucchini lengthwise into 1/8 inch slices.\n4. Once the spaghetti squash is cooked, shred the inside of the squash with a fork into a strainer. Gently press down on the squash to drain out some of the liquid.\n5. Mix the spaghetti squash with 2/3 of the grated cheese, nutmeg, salt and pepper. Set aside.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, build your lasagne. Zucchini slices on the bottom, spread half of the spaghetti squash mixture, spread half the meat mixture, finish with half of the tomato sauce. Repeat. Finish by adding the remaining zucchini slices (if you have any). Add the remaining cheese.\n7. Bake for 25-30 minutes.'),
	(672, '65ee2de69fd5eb92ee41ba40', '2024-03-10 17:15:42', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 28 oz jar spaghetti sauce\n- 3 medium zucchini or 1 eggplant, sliced 1/8 inch thick\n- sea salt\n- Cashew Ricotta Cheese (see that recipe card)\n- 16 oz shredded mozzarella cheese\n- 1/4 cup PR cheese\n- 1 large egg\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a medium skillet, brown meat. Drain. Add the marina sauce to the meat. Simmer on low while prepping the next steps.\n2. Slice the zucchini or eggplant into slices. Lightly salt the slices and set aside for 10 minutes. Salting it helps to take out the moisture. After 10 minutes, blot excess moisture with a paper towel.\n3. On a skillet, grill zucchini on each side until cooked, about 1-2 minutes per side. Place on a paper towel to soak any additional moisture.\n4. Preheat oven to 350 degrees.\n5. In medium bowl, mix the cashew ricotta, pr cheese and egg. Stir well.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, spread some sauce on the bottom. Layer the zucchini. Then ricotta mixture. Top with mozzarella. Repeat the process until all ingredients are used up. Top with sauce and mozzarella.\n7. Cover with foil and bake for 30 minutes.'),
	(673, '65ee2b079d6349ae5cd0a4ae', '2024-03-10 17:41:45', 'Note: For the veggies-can look for a frozen veggie blend to make this easier.\n\nIngredients (these ingredients are all doubled as this freezes well)\n\n- 8 tablespoon butter\n- 4 leeks, roughly chopped\n- 4 carrots, roughly chopped\n- 2 celery stalk, roughly chopped\n- 5 russet potatoes, diced\n- 6 zucchini, cut into 1 inch pieces\n- 8-10 cups chicken stock\n- 2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in the jumbo pot. Add leeks, carrots, celery. Low-medium heat, cover, cook for 20 minutes.\n2. Add potatoes and stock and thyme. Bring to a boil. Simmer for 10 minutes.\n3. Add zucchini. Simmer 15 more minutes. Until zucchini and potatoes are fork tender.\n4. Add salt and pepper.\n5. Using a hand immersion blender, puree the soup. Be careful not to fill the pot too high or this will be very messy.\n6. Season to taste with salt and pepper.'),
	(674, '65ee33402e06e43ef6df6ab4', '2024-03-10 17:40:35', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon butter\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoon dried italian seasoning\n- 6 cups chicken stock\n- 1 pound chicken thighs\n- 14 ounces diced tomatoes\n- 10 ounces frozen spinach leaves\n- Sea salt\n- PR cheese for sprinkling on top\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in a large pot over medium heat. Add garlic and italian seasoning. Pour in stock. Bring to a boil.\n2. Add chicken cooking for 12-15 minutes, until chicken is cooked through. Using a pair of tongs, remove the chicken placing on a cutting board.\n3. Add tomatoes and spinach to the soup and cook for 5-10 minutes.\n4. Chop chicken into bite-sized pieces. Season with sea salt.\n5. Ladle into bowls and garnish with PR cheese.'),
	(675, '65ee372e7bb627c87df43ca2', '2024-03-10 17:46:25', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 3 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 4 cups white beans\n- 4 cups kidney beans\n- 4 cups pinto beans\n- 4 cups chicken broth\n- cheddar cheese\n- salt and pepper to taste\n- Cayenne pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a large pot, add beans and broth and spices. Boil. Simmer, covered, 10 minutes.\n2. Blend with immersion blender.\n3. Serve with cheese on top.'),
	(676, '66804801d104693530f1c13c', '2024-06-29 12:44:39', 'Don\'t put nuggets in until preheat is done \nPlace parchment paper or equivalent in oven\nPreheat 425\nLay 4-6 nuggets in oven \nSet time for 16 minutes\nFlip nuggets over\nSet timer for another 6-7 minutes (check periodically for preferred brownness)\n\nIf you want veggie, we have mixed veggies, green beans, and broccoli. 1/2 to 1 C covered with water. Bring to boil, reduce heat to light boil for 3-4 minutes (broccoli may need an additional min or two)'),
	(677, '67e09ccb91874e7d03e8bac7', '2025-03-23 18:47:00', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1tsp Black pepper\n- 1/4 cup sunflower seeds, toasted (optional)\n- 1 Cup pasta per serving \n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with sunflower seeds, if using.\n3. Each serving can be done with a cup of penne pasta.'),
	(678, '67f6c4722785635c12d6bfef', '2025-04-09 14:03:49', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp chili powder\n- Salt + pepper to taste\n- Corn or flour tortillas\n  **Optional toppings:** diced tomato, avocado, cheese\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Heat a skillet, toss in black beans + spices, stir until warm and a little thickened.\n2. Warm tortillas.\n3. Spoon beans onto tortillas and pile on your toppings.'),
	(679, '67f6d1a82f24c4e9aa7fd634', '2025-04-09 15:00:02', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained)\n- 1 cup rice (white or brown)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes (with juice)\n- 1 bell pepper, chopped\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp cumin + 1/2 tsp smoked paprika (optional: chili powder, garlic)\n- Salt & pepper\n- Optional toppings: cheese, avocado, green onion, hot sauce\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion + pepper in a bit of oil until soft.\n2. Add spices, stir for a minute.\n3. Add rice, beans, tomatoes, and broth.\n4. Bring to a boil, then reduce to low, cover, and simmer until rice is cooked (about 20 min for white, 35-40 for brown).\n5. Fluff and top as you like!'),
	(680, '67f6d1f2c9c94bac53e7a203', '2025-04-09 15:01:07', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 large sweet potato, cubed\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie broth\n- 1 tsp cumin, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, 1/4 tsp cinnamon (optional but amazing)\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion until soft.\n2. Add sweet potato, beans, tomatoes, broth, and spices.\n3. Simmer until sweet potato is fork-tender (20–25 min).\n4. Taste, season, and top with avocado or a swirl of yogurt.'),
	(681, '67f6d2beff0244014051ceb1', '2025-04-09 15:04:22', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup rice\n- 1 can coconut milk (full-fat or light)\n- 1 cup water or broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp ginger powder\n- Salt to taste\n- Optional: lime, cilantro, chili flakes\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Dump it all in a pot.\n2. Bring to boil, then simmer covered 18–20 min until rice is done.\n3. Stir, taste, and finish with lime juice or chili flakes if you want a little kick.'),
	(682, '67f6d7a90dfe222116694fa7', '2025-04-09 15:25:31', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Weeknight protein bomb\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt, pepper\n- Optional: cooked rice or GF pasta to serve over\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add tomato sauce + black beans, simmer 5–10 min. Serve over rice or pasta. Add cheese if you want.'),
	(683, '67f6d7e733d4ebefa32d1be1', '2025-04-09 15:26:19', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Creamy + slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Optional: chili flakes, chopped spinach\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything 15 minutes. Blend half (optional) for a creamier texture. Garnish with a swirl of coconut milk or cheese.'),
	(684, '67f6d814dd2e1cc72fa318bd', '2025-04-09 15:27:11', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk **or** 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic & onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese for top\n\n**How-to:**\nMix cooked pasta, beans, sauce of choice, and seasonings. Pour into dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(685, '67f6d83b8b90154cd16b9174', '2025-04-09 15:27:46', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Meaty vegan stew\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded with hands or fork)\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 tsp each: garlic powder, onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add tomatoes + black beans. Simmer 20–30 min until thick. Great with rice or GF cornbread.'),
	(686, '67f6d86e51c3735b50f5af4e', '2025-04-09 15:28:38', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cheesy & hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Cooked GF pasta or rice\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Mix with beans, sauce, and pasta or rice. Spread in baking dish, top with cheese, bake 15–20 min.'),
	(687, '67f6d3181ecadb49da60fcbf', '2025-04-09 15:26:27', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained)\n- 3 cloves garlic, minced (or 1 tsp garlic powder)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Olive oil\n- Salt, pepper, pinch of chili flakes\n- Optional: handful of chopped kale or spinach, squeeze of lemon\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté garlic in olive oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, broth, herbs, and seasonings.\n3. Simmer 15–20 minutes until thickened and cozy.\n4. Add greens at the end if using, and finish with lemon juice for brightness.'),
	(688, '67f6d365cbfc9cd17164d86a', '2025-04-09 15:26:25', 'Creamy without cream, and full of flavor.\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb pasta (short shapes like orecchiette, penne, or shells)\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 3 cloves garlic (minced or sliced)\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 tsp rosemary or thyme (dried or fresh)\n- 1/2 cup veggie or chicken broth (or pasta water)\n- Salt, pepper, chili flakes to taste\n- Optional: squeeze of lemon, grated Parmesan, or a handful of spinach\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Cook pasta in salted water until al dente. Save about 1/2 cup pasta water.\n2. While pasta cooks, heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat.\n3. Add garlic and herbs. Sauté until garlic is fragrant.\n4. Add cannellini beans and broth (or pasta water). Simmer 5–7 min until beans start to break down a bit and sauce thickens.\n5. Stir in cooked pasta. Toss to coat and warm through.\n6. Add lemon juice or Parmesan if using, and adjust seasoning.'),
	(689, '67f6d89c820310bb4d5b7dfe', '2025-04-09 15:29:30', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Cozy, Italian-inspired\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cooked chopped spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend one can of beans with broth + coconut milk. Simmer with second can and seasonings for 15–20 minutes. Add greens last if using.'),
	(690, '67f6d8d2bf3d8478b9410442', '2025-04-09 15:30:17', '**Type:** Casserole/Bake\n**Vibe:** Dairy-free Alfredo-ish\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: smoked paprika or Italian herbs\n- Optional: shredded cheddar on top\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans, coconut milk, and seasonings. Mix with pasta, pour into baking dish, top with cheese (if using), bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(691, '67f6d8ed0ba832c5d59c9c5b', '2025-04-28 21:45:22', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-rich and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, stir in beans + sauce, simmer 10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(692, '67f6d9453c6e3f0e54ecc6a9', '2025-04-09 15:32:18', '**Type:** One-pot (or two-pot)\n**Vibe:** Rustic & herby\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 can diced tomatoes\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- White rice (served with or cooked into the beans)\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer beans, tomatoes, seasonings together 15 min. Serve over cooked rice or cook rice directly in with extra liquid.'),
	(693, '67f6d9860b7fd3757b014d4a', '2025-04-09 15:33:21', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild & creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp turmeric\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: serve over rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients together for 15–20 min. Serve over rice or scoop with flatbread if you’ve got it.'),
	(694, '67f6d9aa58884dc595fe1691', '2025-04-27 21:29:03', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty & homey\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1–2 chicken breasts (cooked & chopped or shredded)\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Mashed potatoes (can be made with butter + coconut milk)\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, broth, and seasoning in a casserole dish. Top with mashed potatoes. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(695, '67f6db51765d2af8a6120b7d', '2025-04-09 15:41:00', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Rich, soft, almost risotto-like\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 2 cups broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté seasonings in olive oil, add rice and liquid, bring to boil. Add beans halfway through. Simmer covered 18–20 min. Stir at the end—it’ll get creamy!'),
	(696, '67f6db7c34cc1b5aba24924f', '2025-04-09 15:41:37', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Smooth and simple\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Thyme or rosemary\n- Optional: a handful of spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Blend half or all for a smooth texture.'),
	(697, '67f6db98db7791bf47f312e3', '2025-08-10 17:11:40', '**Type:** One-skillet meal\n**Vibe:** Hearty and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Onion powder, garlic powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n- made four servings \n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Stir in beans and tomato sauce. Simmer for 5–10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(698, '67f6dbb11897fad863756c6b', '2025-04-09 15:42:29', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Mild and creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings. Toss with pasta, put in baking dish, top with cheese. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(699, '67f6dbca7dc8d6736fe0c669', '2025-04-09 15:42:55', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Creamy and lightly spiced\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Cumin, turmeric, chili powder (optional)\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning to taste. Serve hot.'),
	(700, '67f6dbf15835da0a7474d6a8', '2025-04-09 15:43:32', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cozy classic with a twist\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (cubed)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme\n- Optional: GF biscuit topping or mashed potatoes\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, sauce in baking dish. Top with biscuits or mash. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 min.'),
	(701, '67f6dc0b38817fdb9a7f5ccc', '2025-04-13 13:28:47', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty & meaty without meat\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/4 cup water\n- 1 tsp salt\n- 1 tsp Garlic\n- 1 tsp onion powder\n- 1tsp paprika\n- 1 tsp oregano\n- Optional: coconut milk splash at the end\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans & tomatoes, simmer 20–30 min. Great on its own or over pasta or rice.'),
	(702, '67f6e574478306dc9e9ca55c', '2025-04-09 16:24:13', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Optional: peas or frozen mixed veggies\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together 20 minutes until creamy. Add frozen veggies near the end. Serve hot over rice.'),
	(703, '67f6e5a37594122dcbc2377e', '2025-04-09 16:25:42', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-packed, saucy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n- Optional: frozen corn or peas\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with seasonings, stir in chickpeas, Ro-Tel, and veggies. Simmer for 10 minutes.'),
	(704, '67f6e6027c1618ec53193a84', '2025-04-09 16:27:00', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Creamy & veggie-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli + carrots (from a veggie mix)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano or thyme\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20–25 minutes. Adjust thickness with more broth or milk. Serve with a spoon and a blanket.'),
	(705, '67f6e6456e211ca1e4aa1d01', '2025-04-09 16:27:53', '**Type:** Creamy pasta\n**Vibe:** White sauce–style, dairy-free\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend chickpeas, coconut milk, and seasonings. Heat in a saucepan, stir in pasta. Top with cheese if desired. Creamy, cozy, and satisfying'),
	(706, '67f6e6733fb047dae933107e', '2025-04-09 16:28:40', '**Type:** Chili-style\n**Vibe:** Simple and spicy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn or mixed veg\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: top with cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20 minutes. Add cheese at the end if using. Serve in a bowl or over rice.'),
	(707, '67f6e6b89008710652e5ceae', '2025-04-09 16:29:49', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty, like a gratin\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 2 cups cooked diced potatoes\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Top with cheese (if using) and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes.'),
	(708, '67f6e6e42de01a2f2a95d602', '2025-04-09 16:30:25', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Warm, earthy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth with seasonings. Add chickpeas and veggies halfway through. Stir occasionally. Done in ~20 min.'),
	(709, '67f6e742e6f1c9d1c849f7d0', '2025-04-09 16:31:57', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Silky, earthy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Blend part of the beans for a creamy texture or leave chunky. Top with cheddar if you like.'),
	(710, '67f6e7823bceb1b3d8bcc968', '2025-04-09 16:33:03', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty and slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with seasonings. Add beans, tomato sauce, and veggies. Simmer until heated through. Serve solo or over rice.'),
	(711, '67f6e7a7c0bdb6909c3d367d', '2025-04-09 16:33:38', '**Type:** Pasta\n**Vibe:** Mild, creamy, and dreamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Optional: grated cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings until smooth. Heat gently, toss with pasta, and top with cheese if using.'),
	(712, '67f6e7c1f4b788ab03a88cf1', '2025-04-09 16:34:04', '**Type:** Oven-bake\n**Vibe:** Roasty and nourishing\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1.5 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 1/4 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary, salt\n- Optional: cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Bake at 375°F for 25–30 minutes until golden. Top with cheese if desired.'),
	(713, '67f6e7dc4583dbdd2be5be67', '2025-04-09 16:34:32', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild curry, plant-powered\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth or Ro-Tel\n- Cumin, garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans, liquid, and simmer 20 min. Serve with rice or as a stew.'),
	(714, '67f6e803175f15f0baeac4bf', '2025-04-09 16:35:02', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Rustic, creamy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- 1/4–1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheese for topping\n\n**How-to:**\nMix everything, transfer to a baking dish, top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes.'),
	(715, '67f6e81c3a17c51bd6839c7f', '2025-04-09 16:35:28', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen peas or green beans\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning and serve with a spoon and a smile.'),
	(716, '67f6e8831688ad96ae92de1b', '2025-06-02 17:33:29', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory & protein-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 3/4 teaspoon Garlic powder\n- 3/4 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/2 teaspoon tumeric\n- 1/4 teaspoon salt\n- Optional: frozen peas or carrots\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add beans and coconut milk, simmer 15–20 minutes. Serve over rice.'),
	(717, '67f6e8a24e9fd13663bf250d', '2025-04-09 16:37:46', '**Type:** Brothy soup\n**Vibe:** Lighter but filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2–1 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 20 minutes. Optional: blend a portion for a thicker texture.'),
	(718, '67f6e8c26dddd811aa4785a0', '2025-04-09 16:38:19', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy & cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nStir all ingredients together in a baking dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(719, '67f6fe57c9b34bebc5416b69', '2025-04-09 18:10:44', '**Type:** Stir-fry\n**Vibe:** Quick and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded jackfruit with spices, add beans and Ro-Tel. Stir-fry until warmed through. Serve over rice'),
	(720, '67f6fade968000a006f6d470', '2025-04-09 17:55:38', '**Type:** One-pot rice dish\n**Vibe:** Quick & flavorful\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen corn or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nCook everything together in a pot. Simmer 15–20 minutes until rice is done and beans are tender.'),
	(721, '67f6fb0e0c712bac84d6e895', '2025-04-09 17:56:26', '**Type:** One-skillet creamy meal\n**Vibe:** Unexpectedly delicious\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme or curry powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté broccoli briefly, then add kidney beans and coconut milk with seasonings. Simmer until everything is tender and creamy.'),
	(722, '67f6fb2d2e2d1f757637bfa8', '2025-04-09 17:56:57', '**Type:** Skillet hash\n**Vibe:** Sweet, savory, and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1–2 cups cubed sweet potatoes (frozen or pre-cooked)\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n- Optional: ground chicken or beef\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté sweet potatoes until browned and soft. Add beans (and meat, if using), season, and cook until warmed through.'),
	(723, '67f6fb610f93ed8503be7f75', '2025-04-09 17:57:50', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Rich, cozy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 lb ground beef (or ground chicken)\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground meat, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes, adding veggies if you like.'),
	(724, '67f6fc015ab7e5dd2c1d4a16', '2025-04-09 18:00:41', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Spicy and robust\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine everything in a pot and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a side of rice or top with cheese.'),
	(725, '67f6fc2720d00eb77da6f821', '2025-04-09 18:01:07', '**Type:** One-pot chili\n**Vibe:** Hearty, plant-based\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with seasonings, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 30 minutes. Serve with rice or cornbread if desired.'),
	(726, '67f6fc43a4ddded4136e8275', '2025-04-09 18:05:30', '**Type:** One-pan rice dish\n**Vibe:** Flavor-packed, filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth, then add beans and veggies halfway through. Simmer until rice is cooked and beans are tender.'),
	(727, '67f6fd48e0026eacba4fd400', '2025-04-09 18:05:55', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Hearty and cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and tomato sauce in a baking dish. Top with cheese and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(728, '67f6fd69a70a93ba954db476', '2025-04-09 18:06:30', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory and satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, then add beans and coconut milk. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(729, '67f6fd876ff8e5425018be54', '2025-04-09 18:06:58', '**Type:** One-pan curry\n**Vibe:** Creamy and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Ground chicken\n- Garlic/onion powder, curry powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground chicken with spices, then add beans and liquids. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve with rice.'),
	(730, '67f6fda74d30ab49c784ad5b', '2025-05-07 17:27:58', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Bold and hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 teaspoon Chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes. Serve over corn mash (aka polenta), or top with cheese if desired.'),
	(731, '67f6fded3a189d2d126507a9', '2025-04-09 18:08:43', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Simple, savory, and smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 chicken breasts, cooked and shredded\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded chicken with seasonings, then add beans and Ro-Tel. Simmer with coconut milk for 15 minutes until everything is warm and combined.'),
	(732, '67f6fe0eeb47261f077fc5bc', '2025-04-09 18:09:15', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Hearty and veggie-packed\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine all ingredients and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a slice of gluten-free bread or over rice if desired.'),
	(733, '67f6fe2faf8069db3ed70ff9', '2025-04-09 18:09:47', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy, cheesy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and Ro-Tel in a baking dish. Top with cheese if desired. Bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(734, '67f6fe8de3ffa0131aebcc34', '2025-04-09 18:11:28', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Simple and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nMix rice, beans, Ro-Tel, and coconut milk. Pour into a baking dish and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until rice is cooked and bubbly.'),
	(735, '67f6feb7dc439bf5eff6cd44', '2025-04-09 18:12:06', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Smoky and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, smoked paprika, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup broth\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground beef with spices, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 20–25 minutes until everything is cooked through.'),
	(736, '68005051861ebf2dfc1c351e', '2025-04-16 19:51:52', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp coconut oil\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel (or canned tomatoes + green chiles)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt to taste\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- Optional: frozen corn or mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Heat oil in skillet, add seasonings and Ro-Tel, cook 2–3 min.\n2. Add beans and frozen veggies (if using), cook until heated.\n3. Stir in cooked rice and simmer 5–10 minutes.'),
	(737, '680050b91ed28e261cc3dbb2', '2025-04-16 19:52:59', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 chicken breast (cubed)\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp paprika\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1–1.5 cups water or broth\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown chicken in oil. Add seasonings.\n2. Stir in tomatoes, beans, water/broth, and veggies.\n3. Simmer covered for 15–20 min.'),
	(738, '680050f9448a7574075a59ea', '2025-04-16 19:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit, drained & shredded\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/4 tsp oregano\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook jackfruit in a pan to brown slightly.\n2. Add seasonings, Ro-Tel, and pinto beans.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min, mash slightly if desired.'),
	(739, '6800511b1f2c891143a064db', '2025-04-16 19:54:00', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 2 cups water or broth\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté seasonings in oil for 1 min.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, veggies, and broth.\n3. Simmer 20–30 minutes until veggies are tender.'),
	(740, '68005183a8bc2730a5655f53', '2025-04-16 19:55:53', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp oregano\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: nutritional yeast or mild cheddar (if tolerated)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Blend or mash beans for smoother texture (optional).\n2. Heat oil and seasonings, then add beans and tomato sauce.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min. Serve over gluten-free pasta.'),
	(741, '680051a5d487414bc769ea25', '2025-04-16 19:56:21', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 tsp curry powder\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1 cup frozen veggies\n- 1 cup cooked rice or serve over it\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook spices in oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, and veggies. Simmer 10–15 min.\n3. Serve over rice or stir in to make a one-pot dish.'),
	(742, '6824bb4a783db57b9ed8e3ca', '2025-05-14 10:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 jar marinara sauce\n- Canned green beans or sweet peas\n- Italian seasoning\n- garlic powder\n- onion powder\n- salt\n- pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook the ground chicken in a pot until browned.\n2. Add marinara sauce and a bit of water to loosen.\n3. Stir in drained beans (all 3 types) and canned green beans or peas.\n4. Season well with Italian herbs and simmer until flavors blend.\n5. Serve hot either as a stew or scoop into warmed almond flour tortillas for wraps.\n6. Divide into three meals.'),
	(743, '6824babde9b3732c346f3c9d', '2025-05-14 10:53:17', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Tortillas chips\n- Chili Powder\n- Cumin\n- Garlic Powder\n- Onion Powder\n- Paprika\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown the ground beef in a skillet, drain excess fat.\n2. Add frozen mixed vegetables and cook until softened.\n3. Stir in drained black beans and season with chili powder, cumin, etc.\n4. Add a little tomato sauce or water to bind the mix.\n5. Layer over tortilla chips or crush chips on top for a crunchy topping.\n6. Portion out into three meals. Optionally serve with salsa or cheese (if available).\n   '),
	(744, '680051ccffdc026a527075ab', '2025-04-16 19:56:58', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can kidney beans (optional combo)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook all ingredients in a pot over medium heat.\n2. Simmer uncovered for 20–30 min to thicken.\n3. Serve as-is or over rice'),
	(745, '6824bbd5acc27f4664c20175', '2025-05-14 10:52:57', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef (or skip for a vegetarian version)\n- 1 can chickpeas or kidney beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Almond flour tortillas\n- Paprika\n- Cumin\n- Garlic powder\n- Salt\n- black pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté the ground beef (if using) until browned.\n2. Drain excess fat.\n3. Add frozen mixed vegetables and sauté until tender.\n4. Stir in drained beans (chickpeas or kidney beans).\n5. Season well with spices using paprika, cumin, garlic powder, and pepper.\n6. Cook until everything is heated through and slightly crispy.\n7. Spoon into almond flour tortillas and wrap. Serve warm or grilled slightly for a toasted wrap.'),
	(746, '65e35de41116a7a22e54b319', '2025-05-14 10:01:12', '**Ingredients for 3 medium crusts:**\n\n3 cups almond flour\n\n1 1/2 cups arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons baking powder\n\n2 1/4 teaspoons salt\n\n2 1/4 teaspoon oregano\n\n3/8 teaspoon black pepper\n\n4 eggs\n\n3/4 cups milk\n\n**Directions:**\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 425 degrees.\n2. Line a round pizza pan or cookie sheet with parchment paper. (I have 4 pizza pans so I can bake all three at once)\n3. Combine the dry ingredients in a large bowl. Whisk to blend together.\n4. Add eggs and milk to the dry ingredients. Mix well. The batter will be runny—not like typical pizza dough.\n5. Use a spatula to spread the batter evenly onto the pan in a circle shape.\n6. Bake the crust in the preheated oven for 8-12 minutes.\n7. Remove crust from oven and top with sauce and desired toppings. Or freeze the crust for later. Once cooled, place parchment paper between the crusts and they will store perfectly in a ziplock gallon freezer bag until ready to use. I also make sure the size of my circle stays within the range of a gallon bag for this reason.\n8. Bake for another 10-15 minutes with toppings.\n\n‌\n\n**Other Option: Ingredients for 1 large crust:**\n\n2 cups almond flour\n\n1 cup arrowroot powder or tapioca flour\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. baking powder\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon. salt\n\n1 1/2 teaspoon oregano\n\n1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n\n3 eggs\n\n1/2 cup milk\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/](https://unrefinedkitchen.com/2012/04/14/pizza-crust-primalpaleo/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(747, '67f6ffd1505afa379eb5538b', '2025-05-24 10:20:12', '1. 1/2 cup dried beans = one can. Dry beans usually triple in size.\n2. Get the amount you want to make into a drain. Pick out any small stones or debris which are often mixed in with dried beans, so sift through the beans before you cook them. Discard this debris along with any shriveled or discolored beans. Rinse the beans.\n3. To soak the beans, place the dried beans in a large bowl and add water to cover them by 2 to 3 inches. Discard any beans that float.\n4. Boil them for 2-3 minutes. Then, add half a teaspoon of baking soda per one cup of dried beans. leave the beans to soak, covered, for at least 8 hours, or overnight. \n\n(This is by far the easiest method and the one the USDA stands behind. Simply place dried beans in a container, cover them with water and let them soak. They’ll need to soak eight to 12 hours, but the key to eliminating the gas is draining and rinsing every three hours. Yup, you read that right. Drain, rinse and start soaking again every three hours. Discarding the water frequently gets rid of the excess sugar starch—and that’s what you’re really aiming for here, so don’t skip this step!) \n\nIn the morning, drain and rinse the soaked beans until the water is clear.\n5. Transfer the soaked beans to a large pot and cover them with 2 inches of water. Bring the water to a gentle boil, reduce the heat, and simmer for 30 minutes, discarding any foam that rises to the surface.\n6. When the beans have simmered for 30 minutes, season them with salt. Continue cooking until the beans are tender, adding more water if they begin to look dry. The cooking time could be anywhere from 30 minutes to 2 hours more, depending on the size and freshness of your beans. I recommend checking them every 30 minutes.\n7. When the beans are tender, remove them from the heat. Store the beans in an airtight container in the fridge for up to 5 days, or freeze them for several months!'),
	(748, '65e39452587a1979909f4a74', '2025-04-27 21:29:12', '**Serving: 24** **meatballs**\n\n### Ingredients\n\n- 2 pound ground beef\n- 2 large egg\n- 1 onion, minced or onion powder\n- 2 tablespoons tomato paste (can omit)\n- 4 tablespoons dijon mustard\n- 2 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 teaspoon celtic sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon baking soda\n\n### Instructions\n\n- In a large bowl, combine ground beef, egg, and onion\n- Mix in tomato paste, mustard, coconut flour, salt, pepper, and baking soda\n- Use a ¼ cup scoop to form meatballs (about 57 grams each)\n- Place meatballs on a parchment paper lined baking sheet\n- Bake at 350°F for 20-25 minutes, or until instant read thermometer reads 175°F\n- Serve with marinara sauce over spaghetti squash noodles or zucchini noodles\n\nSource: [https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/](https://elanaspantry.com/meatballs/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(749, '65ea48c89c856f6ad662250b', '2025-04-27 21:24:32', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 1 to 1.5 cups kidney beans, cooked or canned\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoons cumin powder\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- Corn chips to serve this all on top of\n- Optional toppings: tomatoes, cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder \n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add spices.\n3. Add kidney beans.\n4. Serve meat and bean mixter over corn chips. Top with desired toppings.'),
	(750, '67f6fee30743c2ee3db00058', '2025-04-15 08:47:58', '- **Chili powder**: 1–2 tsp (depending on how spicy you like it)\n- **Cumin**: 1 tsp\n- **Garlic powder**: 1/2–1 tsp\n- **Onion powder**: 1/2–1 tsp\n- **Smoked paprika**: 1 tsp\n- **Italian seasoning**: 1–2 tsp (usually a blend of herbs like basil, oregano, thyme)\n- **Oregano**: 1 tsp (if using on its own)\n- **Curry powder**: 1–2 tsp (can vary based on the blend\'s strength)\n- **Thyme or rosemary**: 1 tsp\n- **Salt**: Start with 1/4–1/2 tsp and adjust to taste\n- **Pepper**: Freshly cracked, 1/4–1/2 tsp, or to taste\n\nFor **one-pot meals** like stews or chili, you can usually start with these base amounts and adjust based on your personal preferences. It\'s also easy to add a little more towards the end of cooking if you feel the flavors need a boost.\n\nA good tip is to **taste** as you go, especially when working with strong spices like chili powder or cumin, and make adjustments until it feels just right.'),
	(751, '67f2cfc24e06ecf0c14db8d8', '2025-04-13 07:03:32', '1 tbsp chili powder \n1 tsp ground cumin\n1 tsp paprika \n1 tsp garlic powder \n1 tsp onion powder \n1/2 teaspoon oregano \n1/2 teaspoon salt \n1/2 teaspoon black pepper \n\nUse this combination per pound of ground meat. Add 1 tablespoon of water to the meat and spices. Drain the meat before adding the seasoning and water\n\n\n\n\n'),
	(752, '674d02a9d61c5c455626f834', '2024-12-01 18:44:50', 'This recipe can also be used if you just want the cheese sauce\n\n1 cup of pasta \n1 tbsp of butter \n1/4 teaspoon of salt \nShredded cheddar cheese based on desired consistency \nAbout an eighth of a cup of water\n'),
	(753, '65e397521ddf77bca5c237fb', '2024-11-04 18:40:08', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder OR 1/2 tspn Chipotle seasoning (reduce to half tablespoon)\n- 1 pound ground beef or **1 can of jackfruit**\n- 28 ounces diced tomatoes (or 1 jar diced and 1 jar crushed)\n- 2 boxes of kidney beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper (reduce to 3/4 teaspoon)\n- Toppings: avocado, sour cream, grated cheddar cheese\n- Optional: Mix in 1-2 Seasoned Rice packets from Costco\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 15-20 minutes.\n5. Adjust seasoning with salt and pepper as needed.'),
	(754, '65ea455e167fdc301de1f32d', '2024-07-04 13:01:06', '### INGREDIENTS\n\n- 1/2 cup mayonnaise\n- 1/3 cup full-fat canned coconut milk (shake or stir well before using)\n- ½ teaspoon dried dill\n- ½ teaspoon garlic powder\n- ½ teaspoon onion powder\n- ¼ teaspoon sea salt\n- ¼ teaspoon ground black pepper\n\n### INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. In a small bowl, combine all ingredients and mix until smooth and creamy.\n2. Chill for at least 30 minutes before serving.\n3. Store in a covered container or mason jar in the refrigerator for up to 1 week.\n\nSource: [https://therealfooddietitians.com/paleo-ranch-dressing-dip/print/9741/](https://therealfooddietitians.com/paleo-ranch-dressing-dip/print/9741/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(755, '65e3921854d40cc63485e80f', '2024-03-02 14:58:51', '### Ingredients\n\n- 3 tbsp butter\n- 3 tbsp navy bean flour or almond flour\n- 2 cups chicken broth (or filtered water)\n- sea salt (to taste)\n- black pepper (to taste)\n\n### Instructions\n\n- Melt butter over low/medium heat and add flour. Stir until the roux becomes just a little golden brown.\n- Add broth/water and simmer until it is almost as thick as you like it. The gravy will continue to thicken as it cools, so remove from heat and add salt and pepper to taste.\n- If you need to thicken it, mix arrowroot and COLD water first. Then add that to the hot gravy.\n\n### Notes\n\n\\*Navy beans ground into a fine flour using a coffee grinder. To make them more digestible I soak huge batches and then dehydrate before grinding.\n\n\\*For pot roast gravy, add the juice from the crockpot as the liquid.\n\nSource: [https://mommypotamus.com/grain-free-homestyle-gravy-thick-creamy/](https://mommypotamus.com/grain-free-homestyle-gravy-thick-creamy/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(756, '65e3a05c8c1b5970dcacc97d', '2024-03-11 17:58:55', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder\n- 3/8 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1 can of diced tomatoes\n- 2 boxes of pinto beans, drained and rinsed\n- 2 teaspoons sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon ground pepper\n- Corn tortillas (16 qty)\n\nDirections\n\n1. Brown the beef.\n2. Add onion powder, garlic powder, chili powder.\n3. Add tomatoes, beans, salt and pepper.\n4. Bring to a boil and then simmer for 10 minutes.\n5. Fill tortillas, rolled up and into rectangular dish.\n6. Top with cheese.\n7. Bake at 350 degrees for 20 minutes.'),
	(757, '65e3965c9ad871d336849512', '2024-03-21 16:55:51', '### Ingredients\n\n- 2 lbs butternut squash, peeled and cut into 1” chunks\n- 2 Tbsp [coconut oil](https://www.thepaleomom.com/wiki/coconut-oil/ "‌")\n- ¼ cup [chicken broth](https://www.thepaleomom.com/2012/03/recipe-chicken-bone-broth-revisited.html "‌")\n- ¼ cup [maple syrup](https://www.thepaleomom.com/wiki/maple-syrup/ "‌")\n- [salt](https://www.thepaleomom.com/wiki/himalayan-pink-salt/ "‌"), to taste\n\n### Instructions\n\n1. Heat coconut oil in a large pot over medium-high heat. Once hot, add broth and maple syrup. Add butternut squash and stir to coat.\n2. Cover and reduce heat to low and simmer for 16-20 minutes, until squash is soft and starting to absorb the liquid. Salt to taste.\n\nSource: [https://www.thepaleomom.com/recipe-maple-braised-butternut-squash/](https://www.thepaleomom.com/recipe-maple-braised-butternut-squash/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(758, '65e3a1e92948d057fe6ebd6d', '2025-04-27 21:21:14', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef, cooked and drained\n- 1 1/2 cups thinly slice potatoes, cooked and drained\n- 1 can coconut milk (entire can)\n- 1 cup milk (replace with water if we don’t have milk)\n- If needed, 1/2 cup water\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2-4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon sugar\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- If needed for thickening, 1 tablespoon tapioca. Mixed with a small amount of cold water before adding.\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook beef separately.\n2. Cook potatoes separately.\n3. To the cooked beef, add the milk and water and all the seasonings.\n4. If needed, add the tapioca thickener at this stage.\n5. Add the cooked sliced potatoes.'),
	(759, '65e3c056c8a56a5b0e0d01c6', '2024-03-02 18:23:04', '### Ingredients\n\n- 1 can pinto beans, drained and rinsed\n- 1/4  can tomato paste\n- 1/4 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1/16 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/4 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1/4 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 1/4 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/2 teaspoons salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon packed brown sugar or Sucanat\n- 1/8 teaspoon black pepper\n- Cayenne pepper, optional, for heat, to taste\n\n### Directions\n\n- Combine all the ingredients into a pot.\n- Heat on the stove top.\n- Season with salt and pepper, as needed, to taste.'),
	(760, '65e3a89d761eefa02d605b06', '2025-05-10 18:41:34', 'Ingredients\n\n- Cubed chicken, cooked separately\n- Pasta, cooked separately\n- Broccoli florets, cooked separately\n- Cream sauce, cooked separately\n  - 1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n  - 1 teaspoon salt\n  - 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n  - 1/2 teaspoon sugar\n  - 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n  - 1 can of coconut milk-ONLY the thick part, drain the water\n  - 3-4 teaspoons of tapioca powder added to a very little splash of milk or cold water\n\nDirections\n\n1. Cook the chicken, pasta and broccoli all separately.\n2. Mix the cream sauce ingredients together and bring to a slow boil.\n3. Combine all the ingredients together.'),
	(761, '65e3c8e7ac71d8524a75f183', '2024-03-16 17:33:31', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 cups water\n- 2 cups milk (or use water if no milk)\n- 2 tablespoons butter\n- 1/2 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 1/2 cups sharp cheddar cheese, grated\n- 1/2 cup Pecorino cheese, grated\n\nDirections\n\n1. Slowly bring water, milk, butter and salt to a boil\n2. Adjust heat to keep a slow, steady boil, stirring occasionally. Cook pasta one minute longer than indicated with cooking time.\n3. Turn off heat and stir in cheese.'),
	(762, '65e3abc0f8cd991e2ff05bff', '2024-05-03 19:05:41', 'Ingredients:\n\n2 pounds ground beef\n4 teaspoons paprika\n3 teaspoons black pepper\n2 1/2 teaspoons salt\n2 2/3 teaspoon Maple Sugar or Sucanat Sugar\n1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n1/2 teaspoon cayenne pepper\n\nOptional: Lettuce, mayo, cheese, rotel\n\nDirections:\n\n1. Mix all spices together.\n2. Mix spices by hand tenderly into the meat so it doesn’t get too tough.\n3. Form 12 patties, flat like tortillas but also loosely packed so doesn’t dry out. (about 80 grams per patty)\n4. Preheat the pan on mid heat. Browning both sides of the patties but not cooking all the way through. Those become leftovers to freeze and cooked thoroughly as reheated for future meals.\n5. Thoroughly cook the remaining two patties for dinner that night.\n6. Make your burger with whatever toppings you prefer.'),
	(763, '65ea4a816a895d4683c924a6', '2024-03-09 15:35:00', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 2 tablespoons tapioca flour\n- 1 tablespoon onion powder or 1 onion diced\n- 1 1/2 pounds green beans, ends trimmed and cut into 1-in pieces\n- 1 cup milk\n- 1 cup stock\n- 1 1/2 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt the coconut oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Once melted, add the tapioca flour and stir until slightly thickened. About 1 minute.\n2. Reduce heat to medium. Add onion and green beans to the pan. Stir until lightly coated.\n3. Pour in stock and coconut milk, while stirring vigorously. It will thicken quickly.\n4. Cook until green beans turn bright green, about 10 minutes.\n5. Pour into a 9x9 inch pan baking for 35-40 minutes.'),
	(764, '65e3af887349307288afe8a6', '2025-04-27 21:20:59', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 6 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 3/4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1/2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 1 pound ground beef or turkey or jackfruit\n\n\nMashed potato ingredients:\n- 3 pounds potatoes, rinsed and cubed\n- 4 tablespoons butter\n- 1 cup milk\n- 1 1/2 cup grated Pecorino Romano cheese\n- 3/4 tablespoon sea salt\n- ground back pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat.\n2. Stir in the salt, pepper and thyme.\n3. Add the veggies and heat until cooked properly.\n4. In another pot, brown the ground meat.\n5. In a third pot, make the mashed potatoes. Add in the butter, milk cheese and salt and pepper after drained and mashed.\n6. Layer all the ingredients into a large dish. Veggies and meat stirred together. Mashed potatoes layered on top.'),
	(765, '65ecd626107d8ab01905f969', '2024-03-09 15:38:59', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound carrots peeled and trimmed\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil, melted\n- 2 tabelspoons honey\n- salt and pepper to taste\n\nInstructions\n\n1. preheat the over to 400 degrees. Line a sheet pan with parchment paper.\n2. Place carrots in a single layer on the pan.\n3. in a small bowl, mix together the oil, honey, salt and pepper. Pour the honey mixture over the carrots and toss to coat.\n4. Place in the oven and bake for 25-35 minutes, until the carrots are tender and browned. Roasting time may very depending on the size of the carrots.'),
	(766, '67fc058a3968a44cf95a9b8c', '2025-04-27 21:21:31', 'Makes 6 burritos. Can prep insides ahead of time.\n\n- 2 sweet potatoes, peeled and cubed small (about 3-4 cups)\n- 1 red pepper, diced small\n- Coconut oil\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon chili powder\n- ½ teaspoon salt\n- ¼ teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 (15-ounce) can black beans, rinsed and drained\n- 1 cup shredded cheddar cheese\n- 12 tortillas as will likely need to double them up\n\nInstructions\n\n- Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. In a large bowl, toss together the sweet potatoes and red pepper with the oil, cumin, onion powder, chili powder, salt and pepper. Dump the coated veggies onto a large rimmed baking sheet and roast for 18-20 minutes, tossing halfway through. The vegetables should be tender but not mushy at the end of cooking time.\n- Let the vegetable mixture cool. Scrape the mixture into a large bowl and toss with the black beans. Taste the mixture and add additional salt and pepper to taste, if needed. Refrigerate the mixture until ready to assemble the burritos or use immediately.\n- Place 4 tortillas on a microwave-safe plate and cover with a damp paper towel. Microwave for 15-20 seconds until the tortillas are pliable. (Warm up 1/2 cupish of the mixture if premade) Place 1/4 cup or so of the mixture in the center of the tortilla and top with a sprinkle with shredded cheese. Fold in the sides of the tortilla and roll up. Place seam-side down on a baking sheet. Repeat with the remaining tortillas until you have all the burritos you need .\n- Bake in a 375 degree F oven for about 10-15 minutes, until heated through and the top of the tortilla is golden brown. Adjust the baking time as needed depending on if the filling has been refrigerated or not. For a softer tortilla, wrap each burrito in tin foil and heat through. Serve immediately.'),
	(767, '65ece1f0e75f531c7b4dd485', '2024-03-09 16:26:58', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoons paprika\n- 2 teaspoons oregano\n- 1 1/4 teaspoons cumin\n- 1 1/4 teaspoons garlic powder\n- 1 1/4 teaspoons cayenne pepper\n- 3/4 teaspoon onion powder'),
	(768, '65ece37b52d21abd85f26e02', '2025-05-14 09:36:39', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 2 pound cubbed beef\n- 1/4 cup coconut flour\n- 2 teaspoon paprika\n- 4 teaspoon salt\n- 1 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 1 teaspoon oregano\n- 1 teaspoon basil\n- 1 teaspoon rosemary\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/4 teaspoon crushed red pepper\n- 1 head cauliflower, chopped\n- 4 large carrots, peeled and chopped\n- 2 bell peppers, chopped\n- 1 onion, chopped\n- 3 stalks of celery, chopped\n- 2 potatoes, chopped\n- 4 cups stock, chicken or beef\n- 1 jar whole tomatoes\n- 1 tablespoon arrowroot powder for thickening, if needed\n\nDirections\n\n1. Heat oil in large pot over medium high heat.\n2. Combine coconut flour and spices in a large ziploc bag. And meat to the bag and shake until nicely coated.\n3. Add the seasoned meat to the skillet and brown for 3 minutes. Meat will continue to cook in sauce so browning meat is all you need to do.\n4. Add all vegetables and stir to combine.\n5. Cover and let veggies cook for a few minutes.\n6. Add stock and tomatoes. Stir and bring to a low boil.\n7. Lower heat and let simmer for 10-20. minutes.\n8. Add arrowroot powder to a small amount of cold water. Stir and then add to the stew, stirring to help thicken.'),
	(769, '65ece24b7e25ac00221ac8af', '2024-03-09 16:31:56', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 cups white rice\n- 4 cups chicken stock or water\n- 7-8oz tomato paste\n- 1 cup chopped onion\n- 1/2 cup chopped bell pepper\n- 4 cloves diced garlic\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oi\n- 1 teaspoon salt\n\nInstructions\n\n1. In a medium pot, heat oil and sautee onions, bell pepper and garlic until slightly softened.\n2. Add stock/water and tomato paste. Bring to a boil.\n3. Stir in salt and rice. Reduce heat and cook until tender, about 20 minutes.\n4. When rice is ready, taste and add salt if desired.'),
	(770, '65ece67dcbf220432b12ece8', '2024-03-09 17:02:16', 'Ingredients\n\n- 3 tablespoons butter\n- 1 large onion, chopped\n- 1 large red bell pepper, chopped\n- 2 medium poblano peppers, seeded and chopped\n- 1 jalapeno pepper, seeded and chopped\n- 2 cloves garlic, chopped\n- 1 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 tablespoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 tablespoon coconut flour\n- 1 3/4 cups chicken stock\n- 1 1/2 cups crushed tomatoes\n- 4 ounces diced green chilies\n- 1 1/2 cup sour cream\n- 5 cups cooked, shredded chicken (substitute is jack fruit and white beans)\n- 4 cups cheddar cheese, grated\n- 16 corn tortillas\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees. Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the onion and all peppers. Cook for about 8-10 minutes, until softened. Sitr in the garlic, chili powder, cumin, salt and cook for 1 minute.\n2. Sprinkle the coconut flour over the vegetable mixture and cook for 1 minute while stirring continuously. Stir in the stock and bring to a simmer for 4 minutes. Remove from the heat and stir in the tomatoes, chilies and sour cream.\n3. Place the chicken in a large bowl. Pour the vegetable mixture over the top and stir until combined.\n4. Place 8 tortillas on the bottom of a 13x9 dish. Top with half of the chicken mixture and then half of the cheese. Repeat with the remaining ingredients. Bake for 45-50 minutes until cheese is bubbly and the edges of the casserole are just turning golden brown.\n\n‌\n\nSource: Deliciouslyorganic.net'),
	(771, '65eceaabc5244b97f6f0e1b3', '2024-03-09 17:08:46', 'Ingredients\n\n- 4 cups chopped onion\n- 6 cups dry pinto beans, rinsed and soaked overnight\n- 2 large jalapeno, seed and chopped. Keep some seeds for spice.\n- 7 cloves of chopped garlic\n- 5 teaspoons salt\n- 2 teaspoons black pepper\n- 4 pinches of cumin\n- 8 cups water\n\nDirections\n\n1. To soak beans-rinse and drain. Soak in crock pot on high 30-60 minutes. Turn off pot. Soak 7-24 hours. Drain. Rinse. Then follow below.\n2. Combine all ingredients in the slow cooker.\n3. Cook on high for 8 hours.\n4. Drain excess liquid. Retain it though to add to beans later for desired consistency.\n5. Mash beans with potato masher. Add liquid back as needed.\n6. Freeze portions for later.\n\nSource: 100 Real Days Food'),
	(772, '65ecec7b734766a86f3ebd36', '2024-03-09 17:19:13', 'For the sauce:\n\n- 3 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 1/2 teaspoons coconut flour\n- 2 tablespoon chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon dried oregano\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 cups chicken stock\n- 12 ounces tomato paste\n- 1 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n\n#### For the Filling:\n\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- 1 large yellow onion, chopped\n- 1 teaspoon ground cumin\n- 2 pounds ground beef\n- 1/2 teaspoon Celtic sea salt\n- 1 can of Pinto beans\n\n#### For the Wraps:\n\n- 1 recipe savory crepes, page 277 of [The Grain-Free Family Table ](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/the-grain-free-family-table/ "‌")or Siete grain-free tortillas (or corn tortillas)\n- 8 ounces raw cheddar, shredded\n\n### INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Place the coconut oil and coconut flour in a medium sauce pan over medium heat. Whisk constantly and cook until the coconut flour just turns golden brown, about 2 minutes. Add the chili powder, oregano and cumin and cook, stirring frequently until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Whisk in chicken stock, tomato paste and sea salt. Bring to a simmer over medium-low heat and cook until sauce begins to thicken, about 20 minutes.\n2. Place the coconut oil in a large sauté pan over medium heat. Swirl the pan to coat. Add the onion and cook, stirring frequently, until onion is translucent, about 5 minutes. Make a well in the center of the pan and add the cumin. Cook, stirring constantly until the cumin is fragrant, about 30 seconds. Stir cumin into the onions. Add the ground beef and salt. Cook, breaking up the beef with the back of a wooden spoon until beef is no longer pink.\n3. Preheat oven to 400ºF and adjust the rack to the middle position. Pour half the sauce in the bottom of an 11 x 7-inch baking dish and spread it out evenly. Place a crepe on the counter and top with 1/4 cup of the beef filling. Carefully roll the crepe around the beef and place it in the baking dish. Repeat with the remaining beef and crepes. Pour the remaining sauce on top of the enchiladas and sprinkle with the cheese. Bake for 25 minutes, or until golden brown and bubbly on top. Cool for 10 minutes. Serve.\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target](https://deliciouslyorganic.net/beef-enchiladas-grain-free-paleo/#tasty-recipes-143604-jump-target "smartCard-inline")'),
	(773, '65ecee7c5c43ffab28481c30', '2024-03-09 17:23:44', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1-2 green plantains (per person)\n- coconut oil\n- salt to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Peel the plantains. Slice them in half diagonally cutting them into shape of french fries. Thickness is up to you.\n2. Pour oil in the pan. You want enough to cover the plantains halfway up their sides.\n3. Fry until crispy over medium heat until crispy on the outside and cooked through on the inside.\n4. Strain on paper towel, salt and serve.'),
	(774, '65ecf156ac509dcad1fe0753', '2024-03-09 17:35:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 4-lb whole chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil, melted\n- dash of salt\n- dash black pepper\n- 1/2 cup chicken broth\n\nInstructions\n\n1. Rinse the chicken and pat it dry. Place in baking pan. Drizzle with oil. Sprinkle on salt and pepper.\n2. Add the stock.\n3. Turn oven to 275 degrees and roast the chicken, covered, for about 3 hours.\n4. Increase to 375 degrees roasting for 30-45 minutes/\n5. Remove from the over allowing to rest 5-10 minutes before carving and serving.'),
	(775, '65ecf2a1551551c1fc10207f', '2024-03-09 17:39:36', 'Ingredients\n\n- 4 russet potatoes, cut in half lengthwise, halves cut into fourths to make 32 wedges\n- 1/4 cup melted coconut oil\n- sea salt\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 425 degrees. Toss the potatoes with the oil in a large bowl and season generously with salt.\n2. Dump the potatoes out onto a baking sheet, spreading in a single layer.\n3. Roast for 30-35 minutes, shaking the pan every now and then, until the potatoes are cooked through and golden brown.'),
	(776, '65ee0b619b77b54774c54f49', '2025-04-30 19:10:48', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 2 tablespoons coconut oil\n- 8 ounces baby spinach leaves (fresh or frozen)\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- Black pepper to taste\n- 1 package of mushrooms, sliced (optional)\n- 1/4 cup chopped walnuts, toasted (optional) [toast on a pan over medium heat for 4-5 minutes until golden brown]\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. Heat oil over medium heat in a large pot. Remove the seeds from the squash, scoop the flesh out and place in the pot. Add spinach leaves, cream and goat cheese. Toss well until goat cheese has melted and the mixture is hot.\n3. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with walnuts, if using.'),
	(777, '65ee08ea1a7846ac72b3c9a0', '2024-03-10 14:27:42', 'Ingredients\n\n- 3 tablespoons evoo\n- 2 cloves garlic\n- 1 tablespoon italian seasoning blend\n- 1 24-ounce jar of whole or crushed tomatoes\n- 1 teaspoon salt\n\nInstructions\n\n1. Place olive oil, garlic and seasoning blend in a cold sauce pan. Turn the heat to medium and heat until garlic starts to sizzle; about 1 minute.\n2. Pour in tomatoes and sea salt. Bring to a low simmer.\n3. Season with additional salt to taste.\n4. Stores in fridge for 5 days or double the recipe and freeze it.'),
	(778, '66b7c63aef984308441f4e1c', '2025-04-28 17:29:26', 'Ingredients\n\n- 2 cans of salmon makes 14 patties\n- 3 eggs\n- about 2.5 cups of almond flour\n- Coconut oil for pan\n\nDirections\n\n1. Add salmon and eggs to a bowl and mix.\n2. Make 14 patties at 70 grams each\n3. Something here with the flour\n4. ‌\n5. Stove at 4.5'),
	(779, '65ee09c712c116e9f56214da', '2024-03-10 14:34:03', 'Ingredients:\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 5 tablespoons butter\n- 1 cup the cream only of coconut milk (can from fridge)\n- 2 teaspoon salt\n- 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n- 2 cups grated cheddar cheese\n- 1/2 cup grated pecorino romano cheese\n\nInstructions:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 400 degrees.\n2. Cut spaghettis squash in half and place cut side down in baking dish. Pour water into the dish so that in comes up about 1 inch on the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n3. Scoop out seeds and remove flesh.\n4. Preheat over to 350 degrees. Warm butter, coconut milk cream, salt and pepper in a small sauce pan over medium heat. As soon as it begins to lightly simmer, whisk in cheddar cheese until melted. Remove from heat.\n5. Place the squash in a large bowl and pour cheese sauce over top. Toss until combined.\n6. Pour the mixture into a 11x7 dish, spreading evenly with a spatula. Sprinkle on the PR cheese. Bake for 45 minutes until bubbly and golden brown.'),
	(780, '67f6e86693b75b1c157d8e81', '2025-05-27 17:22:58', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel or 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 20–25 min. Add more liquid if needed. Serve as-is or over rice. Top with cheddar if desired.'),
	(781, '65ecf24d870dd2e15f0c3ca5', '2024-03-10 16:48:02', '### Ingredients\n\n- 1 quart Chicken Stock\n- 2 medium onions, coarsely chopped\n- 2 cloves garlic\n- pan drippings from roasted chicken or roasted turkey\n- ½ teaspoon celtic sea salt\n- 1 tablespoon thyme\n\n### Instructions\n\n- In a medium saucepan, heat chicken stock, onions and garlic to a boil\n- Reduce heat and simmer until onions and garlic are soft, about 30 minutes\n- Pour pan drippings into saucepan\n- Blend stock-onion-drippings mixture in a vitamix until smooth\n- Place mixture back in saucepan and reheat, then season with salt and thyme\n- Serve over turkey, Mashed Cauliflower, or anything else\n\n‌\n\nSource: [https://elanaspantry.com/herb-gravy/](https://elanaspantry.com/herb-gravy/ "smartCard-inline")'),
	(782, '65ee10511a7846ac72bd44c3', '2024-03-10 15:10:28', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 spaghetti squash\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 6-8oz turkey bacon, sliced or chopped\n- 1 cup onion, diced\n- 1/2 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 tablespoon coconut oil\n- Shredded cheddar cheese\n- Optional garnishes: shredded lettuce, tomato, nutritional yeast, black olives\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees. Slice squash lengthwise. Remove the seeds and guts and lay cut side down in a dish with water to cover sides up 1 inch. Roast for 43 minutes if put in right when preheat starts not after; until the squash is tender and pulls away intro strands easily.\n2. While the squash cooks, heat a large skillet on medium high.\n3. Cut 6-8 oz of sliced bacon in to cubes. Dice the onions. Mix together dry spices in a small dish.\n4. Melt the coconut oil in the preheated skillet. Add the bacon. Cook for 3-5 minutes.\n5. Add onions and saute with the bacon for 2-3 minutes or until the onions have softened slightly.\n6. Noe the ground beef gets added to the bacon and onion. Mix it well, sprinkle in the spices. Cook until ground beef is done.\n7. Harvest the squash and combine it with the meats. Stir all together.\n8. Top with cheese. Bake for 15 minutes and 375 degrees.\n9. Remove from oven and top with any optional ingredients.'),
	(783, '65ee311a8a1d2726097b8c02', '2024-03-10 17:21:16', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 1/2 cups raw cashews, soaked\n- 1/2 cup water\n- 1 tablespoon nutritional yeast\n- 1 tablespoon of ACV\n- 1/4 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1/8 teaspoon onion powder\n- sea salt and black pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. **Soak the cashews for at least two hours in a bowl of water**, covering the cashews in about an inch of water as they will puff up a bit. Drain cashews and place all remaining ingredients into a food processor. Blend until creamy scrapping the sides as needed.\n2. Taste for flavors adding any additional ingredients.\n3. Makes approx 2 cups. Can store in the fridge up to a week.'),
	(784, '65ee228db885a5033c35e542', '2024-03-10 17:02:20', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 3/4 cup onion, diced\n- 1-2 marina sauce jars\n- coconut oil\n- 1 medium spaghetti squash\n- 2 medium zucchini\n- 8 oz grated cheddar cheese\n- 1/2 teaspoon nutmeg\n- salt and pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 375 degrees to cook squash for 43 minutes putting it in at start of preheat. To prep squash, cut lengthwise and remove string and seeds. Place face down in baking dish with water 1-inch up to the sides.\n2. Brown the ground beef and onions.\n3. Slice zucchini lengthwise into 1/8 inch slices.\n4. Once the spaghetti squash is cooked, shred the inside of the squash with a fork into a strainer. Gently press down on the squash to drain out some of the liquid.\n5. Mix the spaghetti squash with 2/3 of the grated cheese, nutmeg, salt and pepper. Set aside.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, build your lasagne. Zucchini slices on the bottom, spread half of the spaghetti squash mixture, spread half the meat mixture, finish with half of the tomato sauce. Repeat. Finish by adding the remaining zucchini slices (if you have any). Add the remaining cheese.\n7. Bake for 25-30 minutes.'),
	(785, '65ee3264a37bb8e6adef6ead', '2024-03-10 17:22:05', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 1/2 cups raw cashews, soaked\n- 1/2 cup water\n- 1 tablespoon nutritional yeast\n- 1 tablespoon of ACV\n\nDirections\n\n1. **Soak the cashews for at least two hours in a bowl of water**, covering the cashews in about an inch of water as they will puff up a bit. Drain cashews and place all remaining ingredients into a food processor. Blend until creamy scrapping the sides as needed.\n2. Makes approx 2 cups. Can store in the fridge up to a week.'),
	(786, '65ee2de69fd5eb92ee41ba40', '2024-03-10 17:15:42', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 28 oz jar spaghetti sauce\n- 3 medium zucchini or 1 eggplant, sliced 1/8 inch thick\n- sea salt\n- Cashew Ricotta Cheese (see that recipe card)\n- 16 oz shredded mozzarella cheese\n- 1/4 cup PR cheese\n- 1 large egg\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a medium skillet, brown meat. Drain. Add the marina sauce to the meat. Simmer on low while prepping the next steps.\n2. Slice the zucchini or eggplant into slices. Lightly salt the slices and set aside for 10 minutes. Salting it helps to take out the moisture. After 10 minutes, blot excess moisture with a paper towel.\n3. On a skillet, grill zucchini on each side until cooked, about 1-2 minutes per side. Place on a paper towel to soak any additional moisture.\n4. Preheat oven to 350 degrees.\n5. In medium bowl, mix the cashew ricotta, pr cheese and egg. Stir well.\n6. In a 13x9 dish, spread some sauce on the bottom. Layer the zucchini. Then ricotta mixture. Top with mozzarella. Repeat the process until all ingredients are used up. Top with sauce and mozzarella.\n7. Cover with foil and bake for 30 minutes.'),
	(787, '660094acc92698bb05e09a01', '2024-03-24 16:07:53', ''),
	(788, '65ee2b079d6349ae5cd0a4ae', '2024-03-10 17:41:45', 'Note: For the veggies-can look for a frozen veggie blend to make this easier.\n\nIngredients (these ingredients are all doubled as this freezes well)\n\n- 8 tablespoon butter\n- 4 leeks, roughly chopped\n- 4 carrots, roughly chopped\n- 2 celery stalk, roughly chopped\n- 5 russet potatoes, diced\n- 6 zucchini, cut into 1 inch pieces\n- 8-10 cups chicken stock\n- 2 teaspoon dried thyme\n- 4 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1/2 teaspoon black pepper\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in the jumbo pot. Add leeks, carrots, celery. Low-medium heat, cover, cook for 20 minutes.\n2. Add potatoes and stock and thyme. Bring to a boil. Simmer for 10 minutes.\n3. Add zucchini. Simmer 15 more minutes. Until zucchini and potatoes are fork tender.\n4. Add salt and pepper.\n5. Using a hand immersion blender, puree the soup. Be careful not to fill the pot too high or this will be very messy.\n6. Season to taste with salt and pepper.'),
	(789, '66b7c3184068f33b52b99099', '2024-08-10 14:56:31', 'Directions\n\n1. Slice squash length wise and remove seeds.\n2. Add each half flat side down in baking dish.\n3. Add water to dish to cover a inch at least of the squash.\n4. Bake 375 degrees for 43 minutes.\n5. After baked, use a fork to scrap it all into a dish. Add salt. Large squash needs 2.5 teaspoon salt.\n6. Can also use this as a dish with chicken, spinach and goat cheese.'),
	(790, '65ee33402e06e43ef6df6ab4', '2024-03-10 17:40:35', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 tablespoon butter\n- 2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 2 teaspoon dried italian seasoning\n- 6 cups chicken stock\n- 1 pound chicken thighs\n- 14 ounces diced tomatoes\n- 10 ounces frozen spinach leaves\n- Sea salt\n- PR cheese for sprinkling on top\n\nDirections\n\n1. Melt butter in a large pot over medium heat. Add garlic and italian seasoning. Pour in stock. Bring to a boil.\n2. Add chicken cooking for 12-15 minutes, until chicken is cooked through. Using a pair of tongs, remove the chicken placing on a cutting board.\n3. Add tomatoes and spinach to the soup and cook for 5-10 minutes.\n4. Chop chicken into bite-sized pieces. Season with sea salt.\n5. Ladle into bowls and garnish with PR cheese.'),
	(791, '65ee372e7bb627c87df43ca2', '2024-03-10 17:46:25', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 3 tablespoon onion powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon chili powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon thyme\n- 4 cups white beans\n- 4 cups kidney beans\n- 4 cups pinto beans\n- 4 cups chicken broth\n- cheddar cheese\n- salt and pepper to taste\n- Cayenne pepper to taste\n\nDirections\n\n1. In a large pot, add beans and broth and spices. Boil. Simmer, covered, 10 minutes.\n2. Blend with immersion blender.\n3. Serve with cheese on top.'),
	(792, '66804801d104693530f1c13c', '2024-06-29 12:44:39', 'Don\'t put nuggets in until preheat is done \nPlace parchment paper or equivalent in oven\nPreheat 425\nLay 4-6 nuggets in oven \nSet time for 16 minutes\nFlip nuggets over\nSet timer for another 6-7 minutes (check periodically for preferred brownness)\n\nIf you want veggie, we have mixed veggies, green beans, and broccoli. 1/2 to 1 C covered with water. Bring to boil, reduce heat to light boil for 3-4 minutes (broccoli may need an additional min or two)'),
	(793, '67e09ccb91874e7d03e8bac7', '2025-03-23 18:47:00', 'Ingredients\n\n- 1 large spaghetti squash\n- 3 cups of shredded/cubbed cooked chicken\n- 1 can of coconut milk, cream only\n- 1 1/2 cup crumbled goat cheese\n- 3 teaspoon sea salt\n- 1tsp Black pepper\n- 1/4 cup sunflower seeds, toasted (optional)\n- 1 Cup pasta per serving \n\nDirections\n\n1. Preheat oven to 400 degrees. Cut squash in half and place cut side down in a large baking dish. Pour water into the dish so it reaches about 1 inch up the sides of the squash. Bake for 1 hour.\n2. stir in the chicken and sea salt and mushrooms if using. Season to taste with black pepper. Top with sunflower seeds, if using.\n3. Each serving can be done with a cup of penne pasta.'),
	(794, '67f6c4722785635c12d6bfef', '2025-04-09 14:03:49', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp chili powder\n- Salt + pepper to taste\n- Corn or flour tortillas\n  **Optional toppings:** diced tomato, avocado, cheese\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Heat a skillet, toss in black beans + spices, stir until warm and a little thickened.\n2. Warm tortillas.\n3. Spoon beans onto tortillas and pile on your toppings.'),
	(795, '67f6d1a82f24c4e9aa7fd634', '2025-04-09 15:00:02', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans (drained)\n- 1 cup rice (white or brown)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes (with juice)\n- 1 bell pepper, chopped\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp cumin + 1/2 tsp smoked paprika (optional: chili powder, garlic)\n- Salt & pepper\n- Optional toppings: cheese, avocado, green onion, hot sauce\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion + pepper in a bit of oil until soft.\n2. Add spices, stir for a minute.\n3. Add rice, beans, tomatoes, and broth.\n4. Bring to a boil, then reduce to low, cover, and simmer until rice is cooked (about 20 min for white, 35-40 for brown).\n5. Fluff and top as you like!'),
	(796, '67f6d1f2c9c94bac53e7a203', '2025-04-09 15:01:07', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 large sweet potato, cubed\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 onion, chopped\n- 2 cups veggie broth\n- 1 tsp cumin, 1/2 tsp smoked paprika, 1/4 tsp cinnamon (optional but amazing)\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté onion until soft.\n2. Add sweet potato, beans, tomatoes, broth, and spices.\n3. Simmer until sweet potato is fork-tender (20–25 min).\n4. Taste, season, and top with avocado or a swirl of yogurt.'),
	(797, '67f6d2beff0244014051ceb1', '2025-04-09 15:04:22', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup rice\n- 1 can coconut milk (full-fat or light)\n- 1 cup water or broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp ginger powder\n- Salt to taste\n- Optional: lime, cilantro, chili flakes\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Dump it all in a pot.\n2. Bring to boil, then simmer covered 18–20 min until rice is done.\n3. Stir, taste, and finish with lime juice or chili flakes if you want a little kick.'),
	(798, '67f6d7a90dfe222116694fa7', '2025-04-09 15:25:31', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Weeknight protein bomb\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt, pepper\n- Optional: cooked rice or GF pasta to serve over\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add tomato sauce + black beans, simmer 5–10 min. Serve over rice or pasta. Add cheese if you want.'),
	(799, '67f6d7e733d4ebefa32d1be1', '2025-04-09 15:26:19', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Creamy + slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Optional: chili flakes, chopped spinach\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything 15 minutes. Blend half (optional) for a creamier texture. Garnish with a swirl of coconut milk or cheese.'),
	(800, '67f6d814dd2e1cc72fa318bd', '2025-04-09 15:27:11', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk **or** 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic & onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese for top\n\n**How-to:**\nMix cooked pasta, beans, sauce of choice, and seasonings. Pour into dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(801, '67f6d83b8b90154cd16b9174', '2025-04-09 15:27:46', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Meaty vegan stew\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded with hands or fork)\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/2 tsp each: garlic powder, onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add tomatoes + black beans. Simmer 20–30 min until thick. Great with rice or GF cornbread.'),
	(802, '67f6d86e51c3735b50f5af4e', '2025-04-09 15:28:38', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cheesy & hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Spices: garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- Cooked GF pasta or rice\n- Optional: shredded cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Mix with beans, sauce, and pasta or rice. Spread in baking dish, top with cheese, bake 15–20 min.'),
	(803, '67f6d3181ecadb49da60fcbf', '2025-04-09 15:26:27', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained)\n- 3 cloves garlic, minced (or 1 tsp garlic powder)\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 2 cups veggie or chicken broth\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Olive oil\n- Salt, pepper, pinch of chili flakes\n- Optional: handful of chopped kale or spinach, squeeze of lemon\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Sauté garlic in olive oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, broth, herbs, and seasonings.\n3. Simmer 15–20 minutes until thickened and cozy.\n4. Add greens at the end if using, and finish with lemon juice for brightness.'),
	(804, '67f6d365cbfc9cd17164d86a', '2025-04-09 15:26:25', 'Creamy without cream, and full of flavor.\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb pasta (short shapes like orecchiette, penne, or shells)\n- 2 cans cannellini beans (drained + rinsed)\n- 3 cloves garlic (minced or sliced)\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 tsp rosemary or thyme (dried or fresh)\n- 1/2 cup veggie or chicken broth (or pasta water)\n- Salt, pepper, chili flakes to taste\n- Optional: squeeze of lemon, grated Parmesan, or a handful of spinach\n\n**How-to:**\n\n1. Cook pasta in salted water until al dente. Save about 1/2 cup pasta water.\n2. While pasta cooks, heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat.\n3. Add garlic and herbs. Sauté until garlic is fragrant.\n4. Add cannellini beans and broth (or pasta water). Simmer 5–7 min until beans start to break down a bit and sauce thickens.\n5. Stir in cooked pasta. Toss to coat and warm through.\n6. Add lemon juice or Parmesan if using, and adjust seasoning.'),
	(805, '67f6d89c820310bb4d5b7dfe', '2025-04-09 15:29:30', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Cozy, Italian-inspired\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 cans cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp dried rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cooked chopped spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend one can of beans with broth + coconut milk. Simmer with second can and seasonings for 15–20 minutes. Add greens last if using.'),
	(806, '67f6d8d2bf3d8478b9410442', '2025-04-09 15:30:17', '**Type:** Casserole/Bake\n**Vibe:** Dairy-free Alfredo-ish\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: smoked paprika or Italian herbs\n- Optional: shredded cheddar on top\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans, coconut milk, and seasonings. Mix with pasta, pour into baking dish, top with cheese (if using), bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(807, '67f6d8ed0ba832c5d59c9c5b', '2025-04-28 21:45:22', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-rich and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, salt, pepper\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, stir in beans + sauce, simmer 10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(808, '67f6d9453c6e3f0e54ecc6a9', '2025-04-09 15:32:18', '**Type:** One-pot (or two-pot)\n**Vibe:** Rustic & herby\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 can diced tomatoes\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- White rice (served with or cooked into the beans)\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer beans, tomatoes, seasonings together 15 min. Serve over cooked rice or cook rice directly in with extra liquid.'),
	(809, '67f6d9860b7fd3757b014d4a', '2025-04-09 15:33:21', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild & creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp turmeric\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: serve over rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients together for 15–20 min. Serve over rice or scoop with flatbread if you’ve got it.'),
	(810, '67f6d9aa58884dc595fe1691', '2025-04-27 21:29:03', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty & homey\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1–2 chicken breasts (cooked & chopped or shredded)\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Mashed potatoes (can be made with butter + coconut milk)\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, broth, and seasoning in a casserole dish. Top with mashed potatoes. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(811, '67f6db51765d2af8a6120b7d', '2025-04-09 15:41:00', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Rich, soft, almost risotto-like\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 2 cups broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté seasonings in olive oil, add rice and liquid, bring to boil. Add beans halfway through. Simmer covered 18–20 min. Stir at the end—it’ll get creamy!'),
	(812, '67f6db7c34cc1b5aba24924f', '2025-04-09 15:41:37', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Smooth and simple\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 can coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Thyme or rosemary\n- Optional: a handful of spinach or kale\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Blend half or all for a smooth texture.'),
	(813, '67f6db98db7791bf47f312e3', '2025-08-10 17:11:40', '**Type:** One-skillet meal\n**Vibe:** Hearty and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Onion powder, garlic powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n- made four servings \n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with spices. Stir in beans and tomato sauce. Simmer for 5–10 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(814, '67f6dbb11897fad863756c6b', '2025-04-09 15:42:29', '**Type:** Bake\n**Vibe:** Mild and creamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked GF pasta\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian herbs\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings. Toss with pasta, put in baking dish, top with cheese. Bake at 375°F for 20 min.'),
	(815, '67f6dbca7dc8d6736fe0c669', '2025-04-09 15:42:55', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Creamy and lightly spiced\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Cumin, turmeric, chili powder (optional)\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning to taste. Serve hot.'),
	(816, '67f6dbf15835da0a7474d6a8', '2025-04-09 15:43:32', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Cozy classic with a twist\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (cubed)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme\n- Optional: GF biscuit topping or mashed potatoes\n\n**How-to:**\nMix beans, chicken, sauce in baking dish. Top with biscuits or mash. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 min.'),
	(817, '67f6dc0b38817fdb9a7f5ccc', '2025-04-13 13:28:47', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty & meaty without meat\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can diced tomatoes\n- 1/4 cup water\n- 1 tsp salt\n- 1 tsp Garlic\n- 1 tsp onion powder\n- 1tsp paprika\n- 1 tsp oregano\n- Optional: coconut milk splash at the end\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans & tomatoes, simmer 20–30 min. Great on its own or over pasta or rice.'),
	(818, '67f6e574478306dc9e9ca55c', '2025-04-09 16:24:13', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Cozy comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Optional: peas or frozen mixed veggies\n- Serve with rice\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together 20 minutes until creamy. Add frozen veggies near the end. Serve hot over rice.'),
	(819, '67f6e5a37594122dcbc2377e', '2025-04-09 16:25:42', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Protein-packed, saucy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n- Optional: frozen corn or peas\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with seasonings, stir in chickpeas, Ro-Tel, and veggies. Simmer for 10 minutes.'),
	(820, '67f6e6027c1618ec53193a84', '2025-04-09 16:27:00', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Creamy & veggie-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli + carrots (from a veggie mix)\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano or thyme\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20–25 minutes. Adjust thickness with more broth or milk. Serve with a spoon and a blanket.'),
	(821, '67f6e6456e211ca1e4aa1d01', '2025-04-09 16:27:53', '**Type:** Creamy pasta\n**Vibe:** White sauce–style, dairy-free\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend chickpeas, coconut milk, and seasonings. Heat in a saucepan, stir in pasta. Top with cheese if desired. Creamy, cozy, and satisfying'),
	(822, '67f6e6733fb047dae933107e', '2025-04-09 16:28:40', '**Type:** Chili-style\n**Vibe:** Simple and spicy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup frozen corn or mixed veg\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- Garlic/onion powder\n- Optional: top with cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything together for 20 minutes. Add cheese at the end if using. Serve in a bowl or over rice.'),
	(823, '67f6e6b89008710652e5ceae', '2025-04-09 16:29:49', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Hearty, like a gratin\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 2 cups cooked diced potatoes\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary or thyme\n- Optional: cheddar cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Top with cheese (if using) and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes.'),
	(824, '67f6e6e42de01a2f2a95d602', '2025-04-09 16:30:25', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Warm, earthy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth with seasonings. Add chickpeas and veggies halfway through. Stir occasionally. Done in ~20 min.'),
	(825, '67f6e742e6f1c9d1c849f7d0', '2025-04-09 16:31:57', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Silky, earthy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, salt\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 15–20 minutes. Blend part of the beans for a creamy texture or leave chunky. Top with cheddar if you like.'),
	(826, '67f6e7823bceb1b3d8bcc968', '2025-04-09 16:33:03', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Hearty and slightly smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown beef with seasonings. Add beans, tomato sauce, and veggies. Simmer until heated through. Serve solo or over rice.'),
	(827, '67f6e7a7c0bdb6909c3d367d', '2025-04-09 16:33:38', '**Type:** Pasta\n**Vibe:** Mild, creamy, and dreamy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp Italian seasoning\n- Optional: grated cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nBlend beans with coconut milk and seasonings until smooth. Heat gently, toss with pasta, and top with cheese if using.'),
	(828, '67f6e7c1f4b788ab03a88cf1', '2025-04-09 16:34:04', '**Type:** Oven-bake\n**Vibe:** Roasty and nourishing\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1.5 cups frozen mixed veggies\n- 1/4 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, rosemary, salt\n- Optional: cheese topping\n\n**How-to:**\nToss everything in a baking dish. Bake at 375°F for 25–30 minutes until golden. Top with cheese if desired.'),
	(829, '67f6e7dc4583dbdd2be5be67', '2025-04-09 16:34:32', '**Type:** One-pot\n**Vibe:** Mild curry, plant-powered\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth or Ro-Tel\n- Cumin, garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, add beans, liquid, and simmer 20 min. Serve with rice or as a stew.'),
	(830, '67f6e803175f15f0baeac4bf', '2025-04-09 16:35:02', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Rustic, creamy, satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- 1/4–1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheese for topping\n\n**How-to:**\nMix everything, transfer to a baking dish, top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes.'),
	(831, '67f6e81c3a17c51bd6839c7f', '2025-04-09 16:35:28', '**Type:** Soup\n**Vibe:** Classic comfort\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1–2 cooked chicken breasts (shredded)\n- 1 can Great Northern beans\n- 1 cup frozen peas or green beans\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer all ingredients for 15–20 minutes. Adjust seasoning and serve with a spoon and a smile.'),
	(832, '67f6e8831688ad96ae92de1b', '2025-06-02 17:33:29', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory & protein-rich\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2–1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 3/4 teaspoon Garlic powder\n- 3/4 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon paprika\n- 1/2 teaspoon tumeric\n- 1/4 teaspoon salt\n- Optional: frozen peas or carrots\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown chicken with spices, add beans and coconut milk, simmer 15–20 minutes. Serve over rice.'),
	(833, '67f6e8a24e9fd13663bf250d', '2025-04-09 16:37:46', '**Type:** Brothy soup\n**Vibe:** Lighter but filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2–1 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nSimmer everything for 20 minutes. Optional: blend a portion for a thicker texture.'),
	(834, '67f6e8c26dddd811aa4785a0', '2025-04-09 16:38:19', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy & cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- Cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nStir all ingredients together in a baking dish. Top with cheese if using. Bake at 375°F for 20–25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(835, '67f6fe57c9b34bebc5416b69', '2025-04-09 18:10:44', '**Type:** Stir-fry\n**Vibe:** Quick and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded jackfruit with spices, add beans and Ro-Tel. Stir-fry until warmed through. Serve over rice'),
	(836, '67f6fade968000a006f6d470', '2025-04-09 17:55:38', '**Type:** One-pot rice dish\n**Vibe:** Quick & flavorful\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen corn or green beans\n\n**How-to:**\nCook everything together in a pot. Simmer 15–20 minutes until rice is done and beans are tender.'),
	(837, '67f6fb0e0c712bac84d6e895', '2025-04-09 17:56:26', '**Type:** One-skillet creamy meal\n**Vibe:** Unexpectedly delicious\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 cup frozen broccoli\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme or curry powder\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté broccoli briefly, then add kidney beans and coconut milk with seasonings. Simmer until everything is tender and creamy.'),
	(838, '67f6fb2d2e2d1f757637bfa8', '2025-04-09 17:56:57', '**Type:** Skillet hash\n**Vibe:** Sweet, savory, and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1–2 cups cubed sweet potatoes (frozen or pre-cooked)\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder\n- Optional: ground chicken or beef\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté sweet potatoes until browned and soft. Add beans (and meat, if using), season, and cook until warmed through.'),
	(839, '67f6fb610f93ed8503be7f75', '2025-04-09 17:57:50', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Rich, cozy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 lb ground beef (or ground chicken)\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, smoked paprika\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground meat, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes, adding veggies if you like.'),
	(840, '67f6fc015ab7e5dd2c1d4a16', '2025-04-09 18:00:41', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Spicy and robust\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth or water\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine everything in a pot and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a side of rice or top with cheese.'),
	(841, '67f6fc2720d00eb77da6f821', '2025-04-09 18:01:07', '**Type:** One-pot chili\n**Vibe:** Hearty, plant-based\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, chili powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with seasonings, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 30 minutes. Serve with rice or cornbread if desired.'),
	(842, '67f6fc43a4ddded4136e8275', '2025-04-09 18:05:30', '**Type:** One-pan rice dish\n**Vibe:** Flavor-packed, filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 2 cups broth\n- 1 cup frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nCook rice in broth, then add beans and veggies halfway through. Simmer until rice is cooked and beans are tender.'),
	(843, '67f6fd48e0026eacba4fd400', '2025-04-09 18:05:55', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Hearty and cheesy\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup cooked gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup tomato sauce or Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and tomato sauce in a baking dish. Top with cheese and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(844, '67f6fd69a70a93ba954db476', '2025-04-09 18:06:30', '**Type:** One-pan\n**Vibe:** Savory and satisfying\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté jackfruit with spices, then add beans and coconut milk. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve as-is or over rice.'),
	(845, '67f6fd876ff8e5425018be54', '2025-04-09 18:06:58', '**Type:** One-pan curry\n**Vibe:** Creamy and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- 1/2 cup broth\n- Ground chicken\n- Garlic/onion powder, curry powder, cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground chicken with spices, then add beans and liquids. Simmer for 20 minutes. Serve with rice.'),
	(846, '67f6fda74d30ab49c784ad5b', '2025-05-07 17:27:58', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Bold and hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 teaspoon Chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes. Serve over corn mash (aka polenta), or top with cheese if desired.'),
	(847, '67f6fded3a189d2d126507a9', '2025-04-09 18:08:43', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Simple, savory, and smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 chicken breasts, cooked and shredded\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded chicken with seasonings, then add beans and Ro-Tel. Simmer with coconut milk for 15 minutes until everything is warm and combined.'),
	(848, '67f6fe0eeb47261f077fc5bc', '2025-04-09 18:09:15', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Hearty and veggie-packed\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine all ingredients and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a slice of gluten-free bread or over rice if desired.'),
	(849, '67f6fe2faf8069db3ed70ff9', '2025-04-09 18:09:47', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy, cheesy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and Ro-Tel in a baking dish. Top with cheese if desired. Bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.'),
	(850, '67f6fe8de3ffa0131aebcc34', '2025-04-09 18:11:28', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Simple and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nMix rice, beans, Ro-Tel, and coconut milk. Pour into a baking dish and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until rice is cooked and bubbly.'),
	(851, '67f6feb7dc439bf5eff6cd44', '2025-04-09 18:12:06', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Smoky and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, smoked paprika, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup broth\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground beef with spices, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 20–25 minutes until everything is cooked through.'),
	(852, '68005051861ebf2dfc1c351e', '2025-04-16 19:51:52', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp coconut oil\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel (or canned tomatoes + green chiles)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt to taste\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- Optional: frozen corn or mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Heat oil in skillet, add seasonings and Ro-Tel, cook 2–3 min.\n2. Add beans and frozen veggies (if using), cook until heated.\n3. Stir in cooked rice and simmer 5–10 minutes.'),
	(853, '680050b91ed28e261cc3dbb2', '2025-04-16 19:52:59', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 chicken breast (cubed)\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp paprika\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1–1.5 cups water or broth\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown chicken in oil. Add seasonings.\n2. Stir in tomatoes, beans, water/broth, and veggies.\n3. Simmer covered for 15–20 min.'),
	(854, '680050f9448a7574075a59ea', '2025-04-16 19:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit, drained & shredded\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/4 tsp oregano\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook jackfruit in a pan to brown slightly.\n2. Add seasonings, Ro-Tel, and pinto beans.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min, mash slightly if desired.'),
	(855, '6800511b1f2c891143a064db', '2025-04-16 19:54:00', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 2 cups water or broth\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté seasonings in oil for 1 min.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, veggies, and broth.\n3. Simmer 20–30 minutes until veggies are tender.'),
	(856, '68005183a8bc2730a5655f53', '2025-04-16 19:55:53', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp oregano\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: nutritional yeast or mild cheddar (if tolerated)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Blend or mash beans for smoother texture (optional).\n2. Heat oil and seasonings, then add beans and tomato sauce.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min. Serve over gluten-free pasta.'),
	(857, '680051a5d487414bc769ea25', '2025-04-16 19:56:21', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 tsp curry powder\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1 cup frozen veggies\n- 1 cup cooked rice or serve over it\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook spices in oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, and veggies. Simmer 10–15 min.\n3. Serve over rice or stir in to make a one-pot dish.'),
	(858, '6824bb4a783db57b9ed8e3ca', '2025-05-14 10:53:32', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 jar marinara sauce\n- Canned green beans or sweet peas\n- Italian seasoning\n- garlic powder\n- onion powder\n- salt\n- pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook the ground chicken in a pot until browned.\n2. Add marinara sauce and a bit of water to loosen.\n3. Stir in drained beans (all 3 types) and canned green beans or peas.\n4. Season well with Italian herbs and simmer until flavors blend.\n5. Serve hot either as a stew or scoop into warmed almond flour tortillas for wraps.\n6. Divide into three meals.'),
	(859, '6824babde9b3732c346f3c9d', '2025-05-14 10:53:17', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Tortillas chips\n- Chili Powder\n- Cumin\n- Garlic Powder\n- Onion Powder\n- Paprika\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown the ground beef in a skillet, drain excess fat.\n2. Add frozen mixed vegetables and cook until softened.\n3. Stir in drained black beans and season with chili powder, cumin, etc.\n4. Add a little tomato sauce or water to bind the mix.\n5. Layer over tortilla chips or crush chips on top for a crunchy topping.\n6. Portion out into three meals. Optionally serve with salsa or cheese (if available).\n   '),
	(860, '680051ccffdc026a527075ab', '2025-04-16 19:56:58', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can kidney beans (optional combo)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook all ingredients in a pot over medium heat.\n2. Simmer uncovered for 20–30 min to thicken.\n3. Serve as-is or over rice'),
	(861, '6824bbd5acc27f4664c20175', '2025-05-14 10:52:57', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef (or skip for a vegetarian version)\n- 1 can chickpeas or kidney beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Almond flour tortillas\n- Paprika\n- Cumin\n- Garlic powder\n- Salt\n- black pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté the ground beef (if using) until browned.\n2. Drain excess fat.\n3. Add frozen mixed vegetables and sauté until tender.\n4. Stir in drained beans (chickpeas or kidney beans).\n5. Season well with spices using paprika, cumin, garlic powder, and pepper.\n6. Cook until everything is heated through and slightly crispy.\n7. Spoon into almond flour tortillas and wrap. Serve warm or grilled slightly for a toasted wrap.');
