	('67f6fda74d30ab49c784ad5b', 'Spicy Mixed Bean & Ro-Tel Chili', '**Type:** Chili\n**Vibe:** Bold and hearty\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can navy beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup broth\n- 1 teaspoon Chili powder\n- 1 teaspoon garlic powder\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine beans, Ro-Tel, and seasonings. Simmer for 20–30 minutes. Serve over corn mash (aka polenta), or top with cheese if desired.', '2025-05-07 17:27:58', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('67f6fded3a189d2d126507a9', 'Mixed Bean and Ro-Tel & Chicken Bean Skillet', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Simple, savory, and smoky\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 chicken breasts, cooked and shredded\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded chicken with seasonings, then add beans and Ro-Tel. Simmer with coconut milk for 15 minutes until everything is warm and combined.', '2025-04-09 18:08:43', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('67f6fe0eeb47261f077fc5bc', 'Mixed Bean and Ro-Tel Veggie & Bean Stew', '**Type:** Stew\n**Vibe:** Hearty and veggie-packed\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1.5 cups broth\n- Frozen mixed veggies\n- Garlic/onion powder, thyme, oregano\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine all ingredients and simmer for 25–30 minutes. Serve with a slice of gluten-free bread or over rice if desired.', '2025-04-09 18:09:15', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('67f6fe2faf8069db3ed70ff9', 'Ro-Tel & Mixed Bean Pasta Bake', '**Type:** Oven-baked pasta\n**Vibe:** Cozy, cheesy, and comforting\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1 cup gluten-free pasta\n- 1/2 cup Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, oregano, Italian seasoning\n- Optional: cheddar cheese\n\n**How-to:**\nCombine pasta, beans, and Ro-Tel in a baking dish. Top with cheese if desired. Bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until bubbly.', '2025-04-09 18:09:47', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('67f6fe57c9b34bebc5416b69', 'Ro-Tel Bean & Jackfruit Stir-fry', '**Type:** Stir-fry\n**Vibe:** Quick and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can red kidney beans\n- 1 can jackfruit, shredded\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, cumin, smoked paprika\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n\n**How-to:**\nSauté shredded jackfruit with spices, add beans and Ro-Tel. Stir-fry until warmed through. Serve over rice', '2025-04-09 18:10:44', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('67f6fe8de3ffa0131aebcc34', 'Ro-Tel Mixed Bean & Rice Casserole', '**Type:** Casserole\n**Vibe:** Simple and filling\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can northern beans\n- 1 cup white rice\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- 1/2 cup coconut milk\n- Garlic/onion powder, Italian seasoning\n\n**How-to:**\nMix rice, beans, Ro-Tel, and coconut milk. Pour into a baking dish and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes until rice is cooked and bubbly.', '2025-04-09 18:11:28', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('67f6feb7dc439bf5eff6cd44', 'Ro-Tel & Ground Beef Mixed Bean Skillet', '**Type:** Skillet\n**Vibe:** Smoky and savory\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground beef\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 can black beans\n- 1/2 can Ro-Tel\n- Garlic/onion powder, smoked paprika, chili powder\n- 1/2 cup broth\n\n**How-to:**\nBrown ground beef with spices, then add beans, Ro-Tel, and broth. Simmer for 20–25 minutes until everything is cooked through.', '2025-04-09 18:12:06', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('67f6fee30743c2ee3db00058', 'General Spice Quantities (for most recipes)', '- **Chili powder**: 1–2 tsp (depending on how spicy you like it)\n- **Cumin**: 1 tsp\n- **Garlic powder**: 1/2–1 tsp\n- **Onion powder**: 1/2–1 tsp\n- **Smoked paprika**: 1 tsp\n- **Italian seasoning**: 1–2 tsp (usually a blend of herbs like basil, oregano, thyme)\n- **Oregano**: 1 tsp (if using on its own)\n- **Curry powder**: 1–2 tsp (can vary based on the blend\'s strength)\n- **Thyme or rosemary**: 1 tsp\n- **Salt**: Start with 1/4–1/2 tsp and adjust to taste\n- **Pepper**: Freshly cracked, 1/4–1/2 tsp, or to taste\n\nFor **one-pot meals** like stews or chili, you can usually start with these base amounts and adjust based on your personal preferences. It\'s also easy to add a little more towards the end of cooking if you feel the flavors need a boost.\n\nA good tip is to **taste** as you go, especially when working with strong spices like chili powder or cumin, and make adjustments until it feels just right.', '2025-04-15 08:47:58', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('67f6ffd1505afa379eb5538b', 'Prepping Dried Beans', '1. 1/2 cup dried beans = one can. Dry beans usually triple in size.\n2. Get the amount you want to make into a drain. Pick out any small stones or debris which are often mixed in with dried beans, so sift through the beans before you cook them. Discard this debris along with any shriveled or discolored beans. Rinse the beans.\n3. To soak the beans, place the dried beans in a large bowl and add water to cover them by 2 to 3 inches. Discard any beans that float.\n4. Boil them for 2-3 minutes. Then, add half a teaspoon of baking soda per one cup of dried beans. leave the beans to soak, covered, for at least 8 hours, or overnight. \n\n(This is by far the easiest method and the one the USDA stands behind. Simply place dried beans in a container, cover them with water and let them soak. They’ll need to soak eight to 12 hours, but the key to eliminating the gas is draining and rinsing every three hours. Yup, you read that right. Drain, rinse and start soaking again every three hours. Discarding the water frequently gets rid of the excess sugar starch—and that’s what you’re really aiming for here, so don’t skip this step!) \n\nIn the morning, drain and rinse the soaked beans until the water is clear.\n5. Transfer the soaked beans to a large pot and cover them with 2 inches of water. Bring the water to a gentle boil, reduce the heat, and simmer for 30 minutes, discarding any foam that rises to the surface.\n6. When the beans have simmered for 30 minutes, season them with salt. Continue cooking until the beans are tender, adding more water if they begin to look dry. The cooking time could be anywhere from 30 minutes to 2 hours more, depending on the size and freshness of your beans. I recommend checking them every 30 minutes.\n7. When the beans are tender, remove them from the heat. Store the beans in an airtight container in the fridge for up to 5 days, or freeze them for several months!', '2025-05-24 10:20:12', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('67fc058a3968a44cf95a9b8c', 'Black Bean and Sweet Potato Burrito', 'Makes 6 burritos. Can prep insides ahead of time.\n\n- 2 sweet potatoes, peeled and cubed small (about 3-4 cups)\n- 1 red pepper, diced small\n- Coconut oil\n- 1 teaspoon cumin\n- 1 teaspoon onion powder\n- 1 teaspoon chili powder\n- ½ teaspoon salt\n- ¼ teaspoon black pepper\n- 1 (15-ounce) can black beans, rinsed and drained\n- 1 cup shredded cheddar cheese\n- 12 tortillas as will likely need to double them up\n\nInstructions\n\n- Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F. In a large bowl, toss together the sweet potatoes and red pepper with the oil, cumin, onion powder, chili powder, salt and pepper. Dump the coated veggies onto a large rimmed baking sheet and roast for 18-20 minutes, tossing halfway through. The vegetables should be tender but not mushy at the end of cooking time.\n- Let the vegetable mixture cool. Scrape the mixture into a large bowl and toss with the black beans. Taste the mixture and add additional salt and pepper to taste, if needed. Refrigerate the mixture until ready to assemble the burritos or use immediately.\n- Place 4 tortillas on a microwave-safe plate and cover with a damp paper towel. Microwave for 15-20 seconds until the tortillas are pliable. (Warm up 1/2 cupish of the mixture if premade) Place 1/4 cup or so of the mixture in the center of the tortilla and top with a sprinkle with shredded cheese. Fold in the sides of the tortilla and roll up. Place seam-side down on a baking sheet. Repeat with the remaining tortillas until you have all the burritos you need .\n- Bake in a 375 degree F oven for about 10-15 minutes, until heated through and the top of the tortilla is golden brown. Adjust the baking time as needed depending on if the filling has been refrigerated or not. For a softer tortilla, wrap each burrito in tin foil and heat through. Serve immediately.', '2025-04-27 21:21:31', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('68005051861ebf2dfc1c351e', 'Smoky Pinto Bean & Rice Skillet', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp coconut oil\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel (or canned tomatoes + green chiles)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt to taste\n- 1 cup cooked white rice\n- Optional: frozen corn or mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Heat oil in skillet, add seasonings and Ro-Tel, cook 2–3 min.\n2. Add beans and frozen veggies (if using), cook until heated.\n3. Stir in cooked rice and simmer 5–10 minutes.', '2025-04-16 19:51:52', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('680050b91ed28e261cc3dbb2', 'Pinto Bean & Chicken Stew', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 chicken breast (cubed)\n- 1 can pinto beans (drained)\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp paprika\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1–1.5 cups water or broth\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: frozen peas or green beans\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown chicken in oil. Add seasonings.\n2. Stir in tomatoes, beans, water/broth, and veggies.\n3. Simmer covered for 15–20 min.', '2025-04-16 19:52:59', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('680050f9448a7574075a59ea', 'Taco-Inspired Pinto Bean & Jackfruit Hash', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 can jackfruit, drained & shredded\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/4 tsp oregano\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook jackfruit in a pan to brown slightly.\n2. Add seasonings, Ro-Tel, and pinto beans.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min, mash slightly if desired.', '2025-04-16 19:53:32', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('6800511b1f2c891143a064db', 'Pinto Bean & Veggie Soup', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 2 cups water or broth\n- 1 tsp Italian seasoning\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- Optional: frozen mixed veggies\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté seasonings in oil for 1 min.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, veggies, and broth.\n3. Simmer 20–30 minutes until veggies are tender.', '2025-04-16 19:54:00', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('68005183a8bc2730a5655f53', 'Pinto Bean Pasta Sauce (over GF Pasta)', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1/2 tsp oregano\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- Salt and pepper\n- Optional: nutritional yeast or mild cheddar (if tolerated)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Blend or mash beans for smoother texture (optional).\n2. Heat oil and seasonings, then add beans and tomato sauce.\n3. Simmer 10–15 min. Serve over gluten-free pasta.', '2025-04-16 19:55:53', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('680051a5d487414bc769ea25', 'Curry-Spiced Pinto Bean & Veggie Bowl', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 tsp curry powder\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- 1/2 tsp onion powder\n- 1 cup canned tomatoes\n- 1 cup frozen veggies\n- 1 cup cooked rice or serve over it\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook spices in oil until fragrant.\n2. Add tomatoes, beans, and veggies. Simmer 10–15 min.\n3. Serve over rice or stir in to make a one-pot dish.', '2025-04-16 19:56:21', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('680051ccffdc026a527075ab', 'Pinto Bean Chili (No Tomato Paste Needed)', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 tbsp oil\n- 1 can pinto beans\n- 1 can kidney beans (optional combo)\n- 1 can Ro-Tel\n- 1 cup tomato sauce\n- 1 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp cumin\n- 1/2 tsp smoked paprika\n- 1/2 tsp garlic powder\n- Salt to taste\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook all ingredients in a pot over medium heat.\n2. Simmer uncovered for 20–30 min to thicken.\n3. Serve as-is or over rice', '2025-04-16 19:56:58', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('6824babde9b3732c346f3c9d', 'Tex-Mex Skillet Casserole', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef\n- 1 can black beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Tortillas chips\n- Chili Powder\n- Cumin\n- Garlic Powder\n- Onion Powder\n- Paprika\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Brown the ground beef in a skillet, drain excess fat.\n2. Add frozen mixed vegetables and cook until softened.\n3. Stir in drained black beans and season with chili powder, cumin, etc.\n4. Add a little tomato sauce or water to bind the mix.\n5. Layer over tortilla chips or crush chips on top for a crunchy topping.\n6. Portion out into three meals. Optionally serve with salsa or cheese (if available).\n   ', '2025-05-14 10:53:17', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('6824bb4a783db57b9ed8e3ca', 'Italian-Inspired Bean & Chicken Stew', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1 lb ground chicken\n- 1 can cannellini beans\n- 1 can chickpeas\n- 1 can kidney beans\n- 1 jar marinara sauce\n- Canned green beans or sweet peas\n- Italian seasoning\n- garlic powder\n- onion powder\n- salt\n- pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Cook the ground chicken in a pot until browned.\n2. Add marinara sauce and a bit of water to loosen.\n3. Stir in drained beans (all 3 types) and canned green beans or peas.\n4. Season well with Italian herbs and simmer until flavors blend.\n5. Serve hot either as a stew or scoop into warmed almond flour tortillas for wraps.\n6. Divide into three meals.', '2025-05-14 10:53:32', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16'),
	('6824bbd5acc27f4664c20175', 'Savory Bean & Veggie Hash Wraps', '**Ingredients:**\n\n- 1/2 lb ground beef (or skip for a vegetarian version)\n- 1 can chickpeas or kidney beans\n- Frozen mixed vegetables\n- Almond flour tortillas\n- Paprika\n- Cumin\n- Garlic powder\n- Salt\n- black pepper\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. Sauté the ground beef (if using) until browned.\n2. Drain excess fat.\n3. Add frozen mixed vegetables and sauté until tender.\n4. Stir in drained beans (chickpeas or kidney beans).\n5. Season well with spices using paprika, cumin, garlic powder, and pepper.\n6. Cook until everything is heated through and slightly crispy.\n7. Spoon into almond flour tortillas and wrap. Serve warm or grilled slightly for a toasted wrap.', '2025-05-14 10:52:57', '2025-08-11 15:30:16', '2025-08-11 10:30:16');
